{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:31:47.285Z","ordinal":313255,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d0dee8b0-874f-434e-94b7-d5b6a81d08e4","process_id":"42535","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes per OS user with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 16, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Node 22 validation is delegated to the required PR CI matrix.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes for one OS user on one Linux host. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base release/v1.3.1 --head codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued --title \"feat(cli): bound concurrent client processes\" --body-file \"$body_file\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes per OS user with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 16, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Node 22 validation is delegated to the required PR CI matrix.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes for one OS user on one Linux host. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base release/v1.3.1 --head codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued --title \"feat(cli): bound concurrent client processes\" --body-file \"$body_file\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":839249597}},"started_at_ms":1795843904445,"completed_at_ms":1795843907285}}
