{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:42:37.638Z","ordinal":313529,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a69cbdbc887d29c1cdae3f10f56b1","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The failures are all caused by the new default of 16 being reached while the existing CLI test suite launches many independent processes in parallel. They are not failures in the tested policy or audit behavior; each affected command was stopped at admission before reaching its assertion. I’m raising the default to the already-enforced hard maximum of 64, keeping operator overrides and the bounded cross-process mechanism, then I’ll rerun the affected verification."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":87,"started_at_ms":1795844555882,"completed_at_ms":1795844557638}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:42:37.642Z","ordinal":313530,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a69cbdbc887d29c1cdae3f10f56b1","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The failures are all caused by the new default of 16 being reached while the existing CLI test suite launches many independent processes in parallel. They are not failures in the tested policy or audit behavior; each affected command was stopped at admission before reaching its assertion. I’m raising the default to the already-enforced hard maximum of 64, keeping operator overrides and the bounded cross-process mechanism, then I’ll rerun the affected verification.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","create_time":1795844555.8615375,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":137996,"sampled_through_sequence":137994,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a69cbdbc887d29c1cdae3f10f56b1","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a220ad-4b4a-7fe2-b5ee-a7414ecf3ca3","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":10888}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:42:52.829Z","ordinal":313531,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a69cd9f8487d2a4db1d2a2300afcb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_14885376add5418e99e6fed31a3d471b","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/cli/src/core/client_lease.ts\\n@@\\n-export const DEFAULT_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS = 16;\\n+export const DEFAULT_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS = MAX_SHARED_RESOURCE_CAPACITY;\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md\\n@@\\n-On Linux, Nexus admits up to 16 concurrent CLI client processes for the same OS user, across its home directories. To set a different limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\\n+On Linux, Nexus admits up to 64 concurrent CLI client processes for the same OS user, across its home directories. To set a different limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-**Progress (2026-11-28, active client admission):** The normal CLI and sidecar client lifecycle now reserves one named slot through the existing `SharedResourceAdmission` before using state. The limit is 16 concurrent client processes per OS user on one host by default; the parent process may set `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64. Since admission happens before project `.env` loading, this setting must be exported by the launching environment. The kernel releases the slot on process exit; an unref'd descriptor heartbeat keeps a live slot from aging out of `/tmp`. Exclusive state restore uses the existing exclusive client lease and does not consume an active-client slot. Five focused cross-process lease tests passed, including aggregate counting across separate homes, and a sidecar integration test verified that a second client exits before announcing a session at a limit of one. `npm run build` and `git diff --check` pass. This limits cooperating Nexus client processes on one Linux host, not ACP sessions within one process or unrelated programs. It does not enforce CPU/memory quotas. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for aggregate CPU/memory, in-process session counts, other disk state, cross-process provider accounting, and cleanup/recovery outside established lease boundaries.\\n+**Progress (2026-11-28, active client admission):** The normal CLI and sidecar client lifecycle now reserves one named slot through the existing `SharedResourceAdmission` before using state. The limit is 64 concurrent client processes per OS user on one host by default; the parent process may set `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64. Since admission happens before project `.env` loading, this setting must be exported by the launching environment. The kernel releases the slot on process exit; an unref'd descriptor heartbeat keeps a live slot from aging out of `/tmp`. Exclusive state restore uses the existing exclusive client lease and does not consume an active-client slot. Five focused cross-process lease tests and a sidecar integration regression passed with explicit limits. Initial exact-head CI revealed that the previous default of 16 blocked existing CLI test subprocesses that run concurrently, so the default now uses the existing shared-resource hard maximum of 64; the affected full-suite CI matrix must be rerun. `npm run build` and `git diff --check` pass before this adjustment. This limits cooperating Nexus client processes on one Linux host, not ACP sessions within one process or unrelated programs. It does not enforce CPU/memory quotas. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for aggregate CPU/memory, in-process session counts, other disk state, cross-process provider accounting, and cleanup/recovery outside established lease boundaries.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","create_time":1795844557.6249838}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":137997,"sampled_through_sequence":137994,"client_authored":false}}
