client processes per OS user on one host by default; the parent process may set `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64. Since admission happens before project `.env` loading, this setting must be exported by the launching environment. The kernel releases the slot on process exit; an unref'd descriptor heartbeat keeps a live slot from aging out of `/tmp`. Exclusive state restore uses the existing exclusive client lease and does not consume an active-client slot. Five focused cross-process lease tests and a sidecar integration regression passed with explicit limits. Initial exact-head CI revealed that the previous default of 16 blocked existing CLI test subprocesses that run concurrently, so the default now uses the existing shared-resource hard maximum of 64; the affected full-suite CI matrix must be rerun. `npm run build` and `git diff --check` pass before this adjustment. This limits cooperating Nexus client processes on one Linux host, not ACP sessions within one process or unrelated programs. It does not enforce CPU/memory quotas. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for aggregate CPU/memory, in-process session counts, other disk state, cross-process provider accounting, and cleanup/recovery outside established lease boundaries.\n \n","move_path":null},"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/cli/src/core/client_lease.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -10,3 +10,3 @@\n const activeClientHeartbeatTimers = new WeakMap<FileGuard, ReturnType<typeof setInterval>>();\n-export const DEFAULT_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS = 16;\n+export const DEFAULT_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS = MAX_SHARED_RESOURCE_CAPACITY;\n \n","move_path":null},"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -33,3 +33,3 @@\n \n-On Linux, Nexus admits up to 16 concurrent CLI client processes for the same OS user, across its home directories. To set a different limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\n+On Linux, Nexus admits up to 64 concurrent CLI client processes for the same OS user, across its home directories. To set a different limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/cli/src/core/client_lease.ts\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795844572910,"completed_at_ms":1795844572915}}
