{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:43:38.930Z","ordinal":313569,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a6a00f5b087d2ab3eb27d0e94f065","status":"completed","call_id":"call_95136c04dc914aaf9c7c4710057df9ad","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \\\"$body_file\\\" <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes per OS user with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 64, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\\\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\\\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1 before the default adjustment; it explicitly sets the limit to 1.\\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\n- First hosted run at `c5afe272b44a5eabb062c4c0fb6a81934db14497` exposed existing test subprocesses being denied at the initial default of 16. The default was adjusted to the existing hard maximum of 64 in `e0384ea9f`; hosted CI for this latest exact head is pending.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes.\\n\\n## Limits\\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes for one OS user on one Linux host. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\\nEOF\\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file \\\"$body_file\\\" && gh pr view 934 --json headRefOid,state,mergeStateStatus,url\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":2500}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","create_time":1795844608.9624531}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138014,"sampled_through_sequence":138012,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:43:38.991Z","ordinal":313570,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0a69ff1d1c87d28db749267ab67b7b","usage":{"input_tokens":135367,"cached_input_tokens":134912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":631,"reasoning_output_tokens":67,"total_tokens":135998},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":22773562,"cached_input_tokens":22474624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":68355,"reasoning_output_tokens":39517,"total_tokens":22841917},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6520536570,"cached_input_tokens":6447364736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15083206,"reasoning_output_tokens":8896953,"total_tokens":6535619776}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:43:41.757Z","ordinal":313571,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1826700b-c1b7-42b1-aee8-3060062aceea","process_id":"29919","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes per OS user with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 64, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1 before the default adjustment; it explicitly sets the limit to 1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- First hosted run at `c5afe272b44a5eabb062c4c0fb6a81934db14497` exposed existing test subprocesses being denied at the initial default of 16. The default was adjusted to the existing hard maximum of 64 in `e0384ea9f`; hosted CI for this latest exact head is pending.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes for one OS user on one Linux host. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file \"$body_file\" && gh pr view 934 --json headRefOid,state,mergeStateStatus,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes per OS user with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 64, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1 before the default adjustment; it explicitly sets the limit to 1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1 after the default adjustment.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- First hosted run at `c5afe272b44a5eabb062c4c0fb6a81934db14497` exposed existing test subprocesses being denied at the initial default of 16. The default was adjusted to the existing hard maximum of 64 in `e0384ea9f`; hosted CI for this latest exact head is pending.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes for one OS user on one Linux host. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file \"$body_file\" && gh pr view 934 --json headRefOid,state,mergeStateStatus,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\n{\"headRefOid\":\"e0384ea9f2c46728e99e1be0c5cb8aa6b63bf096\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNSTABLE\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":567158941}},"started_at_ms":1795844619189,"completed_at_ms":1795844621756}}
