cesses for the same OS user, across its home directories. To set a different limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\\n+On Linux, Nexus admits up to 16 concurrent CLI client processes using the same canonical Nexus home. To set a different per-home limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\\n@@\\n-The setting is read before project `.env` files load, so it must be present in the parent environment. This limit counts cooperating Nexus client processes on one Linux host; it does not count sessions hosted inside a process or limit CPU and memory use.\\n+The setting is read before project `.env` files load, so it must be present in the parent environment. This limit applies independently to each Nexus home on one Linux host; it does not count sessions hosted inside a process or limit aggregate CPU and memory use across homes.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","create_time":1795845161.6240273}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138091,"sampled_through_sequence":138089,"client_authored":false}}
