{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T05:53:55.619Z","ordinal":313779,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7b5950e9-be5f-470c-a424-6b83703c8b60","process_id":"56399","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes using the same canonical home with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 16 per home, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Earlier exact-head CI runs exposed that a per-OS-user global cap incorrectly denied unrelated tests running in separate temporary homes. Admission is now scoped to the canonical home; the current exact-head CI matrix is pending.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes using one home.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes using one canonical home on one Linux host. Separate homes have separate limits. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file \"$body_file\" && gh pr view 934 --json headRefOid,state,mergeStateStatus,url && gh run list --branch codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued --limit 3 --json databaseId,status,conclusion,createdAt,headSha,workflowName"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \"$body_file\" <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes using the same canonical home with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 16 per home, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Earlier exact-head CI runs exposed that a per-OS-user global cap incorrectly denied unrelated tests running in separate temporary homes. Admission is now scoped to the canonical home; the current exact-head CI matrix is pending.\n\n## Reference coding\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes using one home.\n\n## Limits\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes using one canonical home on one Linux host. Separate homes have separate limits. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file \"$body_file\" && gh pr view 934 --json headRefOid,state,mergeStateStatus,url && gh run list --branch codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued --limit 3 --json databaseId,status,conclusion,createdAt,headSha,workflowName"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\n{\"headRefOid\":\"6d7631910ef9771dafbcd4610170b25ffee7e2d8\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNSTABLE\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\"}\n[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-28T05:53:41Z\",\"databaseId\":46114133845,\"headSha\":\"6d7631910ef9771dafbcd4610170b25ffee7e2d8\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-28T05:53:41Z\",\"databaseId\":46114133839,\"headSha\":\"6d7631910ef9771dafbcd4610170b25ffee7e2d8\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-28T05:43:30Z\",\"databaseId\":46113389210,\"headSha\":\"e0384ea9f2c46728e99e1be0c5cb8aa6b63bf096\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":453002806}},"started_at_ms":1795845232165,"completed_at_ms":1795845235618}}
