ate, cross-process provider accounting, and cleanup/recovery outside established lease boundaries.\n \n","move_path":null},"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -33,3 +33,3 @@\n \n-On Linux, Nexus admits up to 16 concurrent CLI client processes using the same canonical Nexus home. To set a different per-home limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\n+On Linux, Nexus admits up to 64 concurrent CLI client processes using the same canonical Nexus home. To set a different per-home limit, export `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` in the launching shell or service environment before starting Nexus; accepted values are 1 through 64. For example:\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/cli/src/core/client_lease.ts\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/CLIENT_GUIDE.md\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795845651571,"completed_at_ms":1795845651575}}
