urity-v131\",\"since\":\"2026-11-26T12:36:31Z\",\"pid\":2586499,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v131\",\"scope\":\"Port and qualify context maturity slice on current release.\"}\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_persistence_protection.test.ts.released-20261126T134840Z-pr871-merged/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"GPT-6 Codex\",\"branch\":\"codex/context-maturity-v131\",\"since\":\"2026-11-26T12:36:31Z\",\"pid\":2586499,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v131\",\"scope\":\"Port and qualify context maturity slice on current release.\"}\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_core_objective.ts/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"Codex\",\"branch\":\"codex/context-maturity-v130\",\"since\":\"2026-11-25T06:35:11Z\",\"pid\":11247,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130\",\"scope\":\"Preserve prior objective classification change while rebasing context maturity\"}\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_slash_router.test.ts.released-20261126T134840Z-pr871-merged/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"GPT-6 Codex\",\"branch\":\"codex/context-maturity-v131\",\"since\":\"2026-11-26T12:36:31Z\",\"pid\":2586499,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v131\",\"scope\":\"Port and qualify context maturity slice on current release.\"}\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:66:The original rules are C-oriented. Their safety intent transfers; literal restrictions such as banning all heap allocation or pointer indirection do not transfer to TypeScript/Rust without losing their rationale. The measurable adaptations and individual evidence are in [`POWER_OF_TEN_CONTROL_MATRIX.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_CONTROL_MATRIX.md).\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:93:Tests executed or inspected are itemized with dispositions and commands in [`POWER_OF_TEN_ADVERSARIAL_TESTS.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_ADVERSARIAL_TESTS.md). Executed successfully: the Rust suite (393 tests passed), npm dependency install (27 packages, audit reported zero vulnerabilities), TypeScript build, and Rust Clippy with warnings denied. The full CLI suite ran for over 45 minutes, showed multiple failures and environment-dependent skips, and was interrupted before an aggregate summary (exit 130); it is inconclusive, not green. No live gateway inference, host restart, real power-loss, or multi-process shared-workspace destructive trial was run.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:99:Risk details for every finding are machine-readable in `POWER_OF_TEN_FINDINGS.json`.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:132:Execute remediation in dependency order from [`POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md): first protect the acceptance authority, then add budgets that survive nested delegation and resume, next bind durable evidence to candidate/policy identity, then close aggregate resource/cancellation gaps, and finally wire static analysis and targeted complexity diagnostics into CI. Keep the full CLI regression and hosted required checks separate from external model qualification. Do not claim external or installed acceptance based on source tests alone.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:622:| `/context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]` | Report separate evidence-based levels for navigability, retrieval speed, freshness, and compounding value |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:91:**Async TypeScript plugin deadline gap (release head `a1f07419ba63402eb5f01dfe85783ae282aa9817`):** `PluginManager.executeCustomTool` directly returns the plugin handler promise (`cli/src/plugins.ts:440-446`); `executeToolPipeline` directly awaits pre- and post-middleware (`cli/src/plugins.ts:470-510`); and the turn/tool observer hooks are awaited in sequence (`cli/src/plugins.ts:549-585`). `executeToolCall` awaits `notifyToolCall` before journaling or entering the execution spine, then dispatches custom tools and middleware through these methods (`cli/src/core/tool_pipeline.ts:881-904`). These paths do not receive or enforce the Rust RPC deadline. The adversarial probes in `POWER_OF_TEN_PLUGIN_EXECUTION_CONTAINMENT.md` show a pending handler still performing an effect later, and middleware calling `next()` after the caller's external 10 ms observation deadline. A `Promise.race` wrapper or cooperative `AbortSignal` alone is not a sufficient fix: it cannot stop an in-process callback, and a late middleware `next()` could dispatch a tool after Nexus reports timeout.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:66:The original rules are C-oriented. Their safety intent transfers; literal restrictions such as banning all heap allocation or pointer indirection do not transfer to TypeScript/Rust without losing their rationale. The measurable adaptations and individual evidence are in [`POWER_OF_TEN_CONTROL_MATRIX.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_CONTROL_MATRIX.md).\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:93:Tests executed or inspected are itemized with dispositions and commands in [`POWER_OF_TEN_ADVERSARIAL_TESTS.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_ADVERSARIAL_TESTS.md). Executed successfully: the Rust suite (393 tests passed), npm dependency install (27 packages, audit reported zero vulnerabilities), TypeScript build, and Rust Clippy with warnings denied. The full CLI suite ran for over 45 minutes, showed multiple failures and environment-dependent skips, and was interrupted before an aggregate summary (exit 130); it is inconclusive, not green. No live gateway inference, host restart, real power-loss, or multi-process shared-workspace destructive trial was run.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:99:Risk details for every finding are machine-readable in `POWER_OF_TEN_FINDINGS.json`.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:132:Execute remediation in dependency order from [`POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`](POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md): first protect the acceptance authority, then add budgets that survive nested delegation and resume, next bind durable evidence to candidate/policy identity, then close aggregate resource/cancellation gaps, and finally wire static analysis and targeted complexity diagnostics into CI. Keep the full CLI regression and hosted required checks separate from external model qualification. Do not claim external or installed acceptance based on source tests alone.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:42:The current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:65:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.1.md:74:| Operation active-time budget | #823; `cli/test/p10_operation_active_budget.test.ts`; `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md:24:| WP-P10-02 remainder (side/delegated inference accounting, per-tool deadlines, general unknown-outcome reconciliation, whole-operation token accounting) | Open; Codex-owned | #823 body (\"Scope and limits\"), `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:637:| `/context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]` | Report separate evidence-based levels for navigability, retrieval speed, freshness, and compounding value |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:5:PR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:46:The current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:69:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/releases/v1.3.0-rc.1.md:74:| Operation active-time budget | #823; `cli/test/p10_operation_active_budget.test.ts`; `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/docs/releases/v1.3.0-READINESS.md:24:| WP-P10-02 remainder (side/delegated inference accounting, per-tool deadlines, general unknown-outcome reconciliation, whole-operation token accounting) | Open; Codex-owned | #823 body (\"Scope and limits\"), `docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:309:  const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":4,"nanos":832804546}},"started_at_ms":1795846272862,"completed_at_ms":1795846277696}}
