c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n\nPR #913's documentation correction merged as `6c03d3fb9a270a031029ce83defc19e71efcd777`. Its exact PR head `db541febf0b2649afecd293ea45e427773528d86` passed the required Node 22, Node 24, Linux, and test-shard checks. Post-merge CI (`46044645724`) passed on `6c03d3f`. CodeQL on that merge commit was cancelled when a higher-priority run for its descendant release head was queued; CodeQL passed on descendant `0bd437819cdbb048f0e3c5f7e52da37721d685cd` (run `46045000745`). That release head's hosted CI (`46045000832`) and CodeQL both passed. These post-merge results were checked on 2026-11-27. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; no local `make test` result is recorded for `0bd4378`, so this report distinguishes hosted check success from that separately named command. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n\n## Current v1.3.1 integration verification\n\nThe following focused checks were run on the integrated implementation with isolated temporary `HOME` and XDG configuration. No live or paid inference service was used. PR #871's first hosted CI run on `851eec0b9efcd8e356c0cf056d46917acbaaa7b4` exposed two stale expectations for operator-only knowledge promotion and two fingerprint tests affected by inherited system Git configuration. Those regressions were corrected before merge. The final PR head and its merge commit then passed the exact-head and post-merge checks listed above.\n\n## release/v1.3.1\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","create_time":1795846307.1391947}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138295,"sampled_through_sequence":138291,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
