{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:16:49.019Z","ordinal":314359,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-499372b2-67b9-4b51-bdf0-26f4b090f8cc","process_id":"81187","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short; sed -n '1,30p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md; git show 48d044902:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -12; git show origin/release/v1.3.1:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -12"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-postmerge-closure","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; sed -n '1,30p' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md; git show 48d044902:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -12; git show origin/release/v1.3.1:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -12"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"UU docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n\nStatus: implementation complete and merged to `release/v1.3.1` in PR #871. The feature provides local, content-free context inventory, provenance, and request-observability; it does not prove provider-side prompt receipt or establish task-quality improvement.\n\n<<<<<<< HEAD\nPR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n||||||| parent of 48d044902 (docs(context): record PR 930 post-merge checks)\nPR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, `6f95e7f`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, `46029833997`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that head.\n=======\nPR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The follow-up wording correction in PR #930 (head `9785b8efd3ccfad77c4e077ac14f4a7964b33e1a`) merged as `007c9fc892568e9a1375662caee0db13a800b102`; its exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI (`46102061647`) and CodeQL (`46102061586`) passed on the merge commit. The advisory Entire check was neutral and was not a required gate. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n>>>>>>> 48d044902 (docs(context): record PR 930 post-merge checks)\n\nPR #913's documentation correction merged as `6c03d3fb9a270a031029ce83defc19e71efcd777`. Its exact PR head `db541febf0b2649afecd293ea45e427773528d86` passed the required Node 22, Node 24, Linux, and test-shard checks. Post-merge CI (`46044645724`) passed on `6c03d3f`. CodeQL on that merge commit was cancelled when a higher-priority run for its descendant release head was queued; CodeQL passed on descendant `0bd437819cdbb048f0e3c5f7e52da37721d685cd` (run `46045000745`). That release head's hosted CI (`46045000832`) and CodeQL both passed. These post-merge results were checked on 2026-11-27. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; no local `make test` result is recorded for `0bd4378`, so this report distinguishes hosted check success from that separately named command. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n\n## Current v1.3.1 integration verification\n\nThe following focused checks were run on the integrated implementation with isolated temporary `HOME` and XDG configuration. No live or paid inference service was used. PR #871's first hosted CI run on `851eec0b9efcd8e356c0cf056d46917acbaaa7b4` exposed two stale expectations for operator-only knowledge promotion and two fingerprint tests affected by inherited system Git configuration. Those regressions were corrected before merge. The final PR head and its merge commit then passed the exact-head and post-merge checks listed above.\n\n| Check | Result | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| `npm run build` (from `cli/`) | Passed | TypeScript build/type check on the integrated source. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` | 20 passed, 0 failed | Inventory, request manifests, freshness invalidation, maturity evidence thresholds and ordering. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` | 3 passed, 0 failed | Operator-only promotion and legacy memory controls. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/session_durable_fields.test.ts` | 4 passed, 0 failed | Durable session integration. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/session_export_escaping.test.ts` | 5 passed, 0 failed | Session export escaping. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/persistence_protection.test.ts` | 27 passed, 0 failed | Session, workspace, checkpoint, export and persistence protections. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` | 90 passed, 0 failed | Local provider-wire fixtures only. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/slash_router.test.ts` | 39 passed, 0 failed after rebuilding the Rust core | The first run failed because the isolated worktree lacked a built core; the rerun passed after a worktree-local build. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` | 1 passed, 0 failed | Receipt persistence failure cannot authorize verified acceptance. Local fixture only; no live inference. |\n| `node --import tsx --test test/audit_export.test.ts` | 22 passed, 0 failed | Audit bundle export preserves deterministic context provenance timestamps and marks reconstructed timing as unmeasured. |\n# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n\nStatus: implementation complete and merged to `release/v1.3.1` in PR #871. The feature provides local, content-free context inventory, provenance, and request-observability; it does not prove provider-side prompt receipt or establish task-quality improvement.\n\nPR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commi