{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:44:07.559Z","ordinal":314940,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a2208e-347b-7f62-bb1f-c24475a2832b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ad1bb81c-2859-46f9-af9e-d4b5289a7beb","process_id":"85821","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git fetch origin b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 && git show --stat --oneline b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 && git ls-tree -r --name-only b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 | rg 'CONTEXT-MATURITY|context-engineering' | head -20 && git show b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -7 && git status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-postmerge-closure","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git fetch origin b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 && git show --stat --oneline b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 && git ls-tree -r --name-only b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 | rg 'CONTEXT-MATURITY|context-engineering' | head -20 && git show b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95:docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | head -7 && git status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"From https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n * branch                b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95 -> FETCH_HEAD\nb3f37c552 Merge pull request #935 from mikeholownych/codex/context-maturity-postmerge-closure\n\n docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DECISION-MEMO.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/README.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/TURN-SPECIFIC-CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-HYPOTHESIS.md\ndocs/research/context-engineering/tools/context_forensics.py\ndocs/research/context-engineering/tools/evidence_reuse_census.py\ndocs/research/context-engineering/tools/measure_compaction.ts\ndocs/research/context-engineering/tools/simulate_policies.py\n# Nexus context maturity and inventory\n\nStatus: implementation complete and merged to `release/v1.3.1` in PR #871. The feature provides local, content-free context inventory, provenance, and request-observability; it does not prove provider-side prompt receipt or establish task-quality improvement.\n\nPR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The follow-up wording correction in PR #930 (head `9785b8efd3ccfad77c4e077ac14f4a7964b33e1a`) merged as `007c9fc892568e9a1375662caee0db13a800b102`; its exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI (`46102061647`) and CodeQL (`46102061586`) passed on the merge commit. The advisory Entire check was neutral and was not a required gate. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n\nPR #913's documentation correction merged as `6c03d3fb9a270a031029ce83defc19e71efcd777`. Its exact PR head `db541febf0b2649afecd293ea45e427773528d86` passed the required Node 22, Node 24, Linux, and test-shard checks. Post-merge CI (`46044645724`) passed on `6c03d3f`. CodeQL on that merge commit was cancelled when a higher-priority run for its descendant release head was queued; CodeQL passed on descendant `0bd437819cdbb048f0e3c5f7e52da37721d685cd` (run `46045000745`). That release head's hosted CI (`46045000832`) and CodeQL both passed. These post-merge results were checked on 2026-11-27. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; no local `make test` result is recorded for `0bd4378`, so this report distinguishes hosted check success from that separately named command. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\n## codex/context-maturity-postmerge-closure...origin/codex/context-maturity-postmerge-closure\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":983562054}},"started_at_ms":1795848245575,"completed_at_ms":1795848247559}}
