{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:47:10.447Z","ordinal":315092,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0a78eaa56487d28560eefacd545ced","usage":{"input_tokens":187937,"cached_input_tokens":185856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":127,"reasoning_output_tokens":10,"total_tokens":188064},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2827589,"cached_input_tokens":2781184,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6953,"reasoning_output_tokens":4357,"total_tokens":2834542},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6550719805,"cached_input_tokens":6477160064,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15145222,"reasoning_output_tokens":8926867,"total_tokens":6565865027}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:47:11.317Z","ordinal":315093,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-371a30cc-1a56-4fb5-adaf-871dda3965e1","process_id":"19232","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba cli/src/core/file_guard.ts | sed -n '54,130p'; nl -ba cli/src/index.ts | sed -n '88,140p'; sed -n '1,140p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba cli/src/core/file_guard.ts","name":"file_guard.ts","path":"cli/src/core/file_guard.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba cli/src/index.ts","name":"index.ts","path":"cli/src/index.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,140p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md","name":"XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md","path":"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    54\t/**\n    55\t * Returns null on contention; every unsuccessful path closes its descriptor.\n    56\t * The utility exits immediately after acquiring a lock on the shared open file\n    57\t * description. The caller retains that descriptor through its critical section.\n    58\t * Never unlink or replace a guard: SIGKILL releases ownership in the kernel.\n    59\t */\n    60\texport function acquireFileGuard(guardPath: string, options: FileGuardOptions = {}): FileGuard | null {\n    61\t  const label = options.label ?? \"File guard\";\n    62\t  const utility = options.utility ?? \"/usr/bin/flock\";\n    63\t  const waitMs = options.waitMs ?? 0;\n    64\t  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(waitMs) || waitMs < 0) throw new Error(\"Invalid file-guard wait bound\");\n    65\t  const fd = openGuardFile(guardPath, label);\n    66\t  try {\n    67\t    const args = [...(options.mode === \"shared\" ? [\"--shared\"] : []), ...(waitMs ? [\"-w\", String(waitMs / 1000)] : [\"-n\"]), \"-E\", \"75\", \"3\"];\n    68\t    const probe = spawnSync(utility, args, { stdio: [\"ignore\", \"ignore\", \"ignore\", fd], timeout: Math.max(2000, waitMs + 1000) });\n    69\t    if (probe.error) throw new Error(`${label} utility ${utility} is unavailable: ${probe.error.message}`);\n    70\t    if (probe.status === 0) { validateGuardIdentity(guardPath, fd, label); return { path: guardPath, fd }; }\n    71\t    if (probe.status === 75) { fs.closeSync(fd); return null; }\n    72\t    throw new Error(`${label} acquisition failed (exit ${probe.status})`);\n    73\t  } catch (error) {\n    74\t    try { fs.closeSync(fd); } catch {}\n    75\t    throw error;\n    76\t  }\n    77\t}\n    78\t\n    79\texport function releaseFileGuard(guard: FileGuard | null): void {\n    80\t  if (!guard || released.has(guard)) return;\n    81\t  released.add(guard);\n    82\t  try { fs.closeSync(guard.fd); } catch {}\n    83\t}\n    88\t} catch (error) {\n    89\t  console.error(`nexus: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n    90\t  process.exit(2);\n    91\t}\n    92\tconst { acquireClientLease, releaseClientLease, clientInvocationKind } = await import(\"./core/client_lease.js\");\n    93\tconst invocationKind = clientInvocationKind(startupArgs);\n    94\tconst startupReadOnly = invocationKind === \"metadata\" || (startupArgs[0] === \"upgrade\" && startupArgs.includes(\"--check\"));\n    95\tlet operatorConfigStartupError: Error | undefined;\n    96\t// `upgrade --check` is read-only, so it must not replay a transaction. It also\n    97\t// must not load configuration while a restore journal says that config may be\n    98\t// only partially applied. Refuse before loadEnvironment() and let a normal\n    99\t// managed launch perform recovery.\n   100\tif (startupArgs[0] === \"upgrade\" && startupArgs.includes(\"--check\")) {\n   101\t  try {\n   102\t    const { hasPendingStateRestore } = await import(\"./core/state_restore.js\");\n   103\t    if (hasPendingStateRestore(process.env.HOME || os.homedir())) {\n   104\t      throw new Error(\"Pending state restore must be recovered before running upgrade --check\");\n   105\t    }\n   106\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   107\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error?.message ?? \"Nexus restore state could not be verified\")}`);\n   108\t    process.exit(2);\n   109\t  }\n   110\t}\n   111\t// A durable state-restore intent must be replayed before environment/config\n   112\t// loading or any normal client is admitted. The recovery command takes the\n   113\t// exclusive lifetime lease; ordinary clients take their shared lease below.\n   114\tif (invocationKind === \"restore\" || (invocationKind === \"client\" && !startupReadOnly)) {\n   115\t  try {\n   116\t    const { hasPendingStateRestore, recoverPendingStateRestore } = await import(\"./core/state_restore.js\");\n   117\t    const home = process.env.HOME || os.homedir();\n   118\t    if (hasPendingStateRestore(home) && !recoverPendingStateRestore(home)) {\n   119\t      throw new Error(\"Pending state restore could not be recovered; no state was admitted\");\n   120\t    }\n   121\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   122\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error?.message ?? \"Nexus restore recovery failed closed\")}`);\n   123\t    process.exit(2);\n   124\t  }\n   125\t}\n   126\tif (invocationKind === \"client\") {\n   127\t  try {\n   128\t    const lease = acquireClientLease(process.env.HOME || os.homedir());\n   129\t    process.once(\"exit\", () => releaseClientLease(lease));\n   130\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   131\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error)}`);\n   132\t    process.exit(2);\n   133\t  }\n   134\t  try {\n   135\t    loadEnvironment();\n   136\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   137\t    console.error(`[config] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error)}`);\n   138\t    process.exit(2);\n   139\t  }\n   140\t  operatorConfigStartupError = operatorConfigLoadError();\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":684959917}},"started_at_ms":1795848430631,"completed_at_ms":1795848431316}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:47:11.358Z","ordinal":315094,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a220e8-66fe-7193-b3e7-14838fd6f25e","call_id":"call_6b3ad9217c294f698d714d9bd2da313d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"    54\t/**\n    55\t * Returns null on contention; every unsuccessful path closes its descriptor.\n    56\t * The utility exits immediately after acquiring a lock on the shared open file\n    57\t * description. The caller retains that descriptor through its critical section.\n    58\t * Never unlink or replace a guard: SIGKILL releases ownership in the kernel.\n    59\t */\n    60\texport function acquireFileGuard(guardPath: string, options: FileGuardOptions = {}): FileGuard | null {\n    61\t  const label = options.label ?? \"File guard\";\n    62\t  const utility = options.utility ?? \"/usr/bin/flock\";\n    63\t  const waitMs = options.waitMs ?? 0;\n    64\t  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(waitMs) || waitMs < 0) throw new Error(\"Invalid file-guard wait bound\");\n    65\t  const fd = openGuardFile(guardPath, label);\n    66\t  try {\n    67\t    const args = [...(options.mode === \"shared\" ? [\"--shared\"] : []), ...(waitMs ? [\"-w\", String(waitMs / 1000)] : [\"-n\"]), \"-E\", \"75\", \"3\"];\n    68\t    const probe = spawnSync(utility, args, { stdio: [\"ignore\", \"ignore\", \"ignore\", fd], timeout: Math.max(2000, waitMs + 1000) });\n    69\t    if (probe.error) throw new Error(`${label} utility ${utility} is unavailable: ${probe.error.message}`);\n    70\t    if (probe.status === 0) { validateGuardIdentity(guardPath, fd, label); return { path: guardPath, fd }; }\n    71\t    if (probe.status === 75) { fs.closeSync(fd); return null; }\n    72\t    throw new Error(`${label} acquisition failed (exit ${probe.status})`);\n    73\t  } catch (error) {\n    74\t    try { fs.closeSync(fd); } catch {}\n    75\t    throw error;\n    76\t  }\n    77\t}\n    78\t\n    79\texport function releaseFileGuard(guard: FileGuard | null): void {\n    80\t  if (!guard || released.has(guard)) return;\n    81\t  released.add(guard);\n    82\t  try { fs.closeSync(guard.fd); } catch {}\n    83\t}\n    88\t} catch (error) {\n    89\t  console.error(`nexus: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n    90\t  process.exit(2);\n    91\t}\n    92\tconst { acquireClientLease, releaseClientLease, clientInvocationKind } = await import(\"./core/client_lease.js\");\n    93\tconst invocationKind = clientInvocationKind(startupArgs);\n    94\tconst startupReadOnly = invocationKind === \"metadata\" || (startupArgs[0] === \"upgrade\" && startupArgs.includes(\"--check\"));\n    95\tlet operatorConfigStartupError: Error | undefined;\n    96\t// `upgrade --check` is read-only, so it must not replay a transaction. It also\n    97\t// must not load configuration while a restore journal says that config may be\n    98\t// only partially applied. Refuse before loadEnvironment() and let a normal\n    99\t// managed launch perform recovery.\n   100\tif (startupArgs[0] === \"upgrade\" && startupArgs.includes(\"--check\")) {\n   101\t  try {\n   102\t    const { hasPendingStateRestore } = await import(\"./core/state_restore.js\");\n   103\t    if (hasPendingStateRestore(process.env.HOME || os.homedir())) {\n   104\t      throw new Error(\"Pending state restore must be recovered before running upgrade --check\");\n   105\t    }\n   106\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   107\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error?.message ?? \"Nexus restore state could not be verified\")}`);\n   108\t    process.exit(2);\n   109\t  }\n   110\t}\n   111\t// A durable state-restore intent must be replayed before environment/config\n   112\t// loading or any normal client is admitted. The recovery command takes the\n   113\t// exclusive lifetime lease; ordinary clients take their shared lease below.\n   114\tif (invocationKind === \"restore\" || (invocationKind === \"client\" && !startupReadOnly)) {\n   115\t  try {\n   116\t    const { hasPendingStateRestore, recoverPendingStateRestore } = await import(\"./core/state_restore.js\");\n   117\t    const home = process.env.HOME || os.homedir();\n   118\t    if (hasPendingStateRestore(home) && !recoverPendingStateRestore(home)) {\n   119\t      throw new Error(\"Pending state restore could not be recovered; no state was admitted\");\n   120\t    }\n   121\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   122\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error?.message ?? \"Nexus restore recovery failed closed\")}`);\n   123\t    process.exit(2);\n   124\t  }\n   125\t}\n   126\tif (invocationKind === \"client\") {\n   127\t  try {\n   128\t    const lease = acquireClientLease(process.env.HOME || os.homedir());\n   129\t    process.once(\"exit\", () => releaseClientLease(lease));\n   130\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   131\t    console.error(`[maintenance] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error)}`);\n   132\t    process.exit(2);\n   133\t  }\n   134\t  try {\n   135\t    loadEnvironment();\n   136\t  } catch (error: any) {\n   137\t    console.error(`[config] ${formatDiagnosticForOutput(error)}`);\n   138\t    process.exit(2);\n   139\t  }\n   140\t  operatorConfigStartupError = operatorConfigLoadError();\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795848431.3585393}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138707,"sampled_through_sequence":138704,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
