{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:54:25.815Z","ordinal":315249,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a7aa07b5087d296a2d82701319034","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The isolated unattended-gate test reproduces the 64-client refusal by itself, so it isn’t simply leftover activity from the rest of CI. I’m tracing temporary lease opens and closes in that test to see whether it creates more client processes than its nine explicit commands or fails to release their slots."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":61,"started_at_ms":1795848864527,"completed_at_ms":1795848865814}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:54:25.819Z","ordinal":315250,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a7aa07b5087d296a2d82701319034","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The isolated unattended-gate test reproduces the 64-client refusal by itself, so it isn’t simply leftover activity from the rest of CI. I’m tracing temporary lease opens and closes in that test to see whether it creates more client processes than its nine explicit commands or fails to release their slots.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795848864.4854958,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138779,"sampled_through_sequence":138772,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a7aa07b5087d296a2d82701319034","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a220ef-081a-7040-b752-99fd79a47a59","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":10914}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T06:54:35.604Z","ordinal":315251,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a7aa1cb8887d2a463fd1d292b0c01","status":"completed","call_id":"call_5b67012314a944ddabd22f125bedf9b1","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/p10-client-lease-trace.mjs <<'EOF'\\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\\nconst open = fs.openSync.bind(fs);\\nconst close = fs.closeSync.bind(fs);\\nconst tracePath = process.env.CLIENT_LEASE_TRACE;\\nlet logFd;\\ntry { if (tracePath) logFd = open(tracePath, fs.constants.O_APPEND | fs.constants.O_CREAT | fs.constants.O_WRONLY, 0o600); } catch {}\\nconst opened = new Map();\\nfunction emit(event, details = {}) {\\n  if (logFd === undefined) return;\\n  try { fs.writeSync(logFd, `${JSON.stringify({ event, pid: process.pid, home: process.env.HOME, ...details })}\\\\n`); } catch {}\\n}\\nfs.openSync = function(path, ...args) {\\n  const fd = open(path, ...args);\\n  if (typeof path === 'string' && path.includes('/nexus-client-leases-')) {\\n    opened.set(fd, path);\\n    emit('open', { fd, path });\\n  }\\n  return fd;\\n};\\nfs.closeSync = function(fd) {\\n  const path = opened.get(fd);\\n  if (path) { opened.delete(fd); emit('close', { fd, path }); }\\n  return close(fd);\\n};\\nprocess.once('exit', () => emit('exit', { unclosed: [...opened.entries()].map(([fd, path]) => ({ fd, path })) }));\\nEOF\\ntrace_file=/tmp/p10-client-lease-trace.jsonl; : > \\\"$trace_file\\\"; test_home=$(mktemp -d); env HOME=\\\"$test_home\\\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\\\"$test_home/.config\\\" XDG_DATA_HOME=\\\"$test_home/.local/share\\\" XDG_STATE_HOME=\\\"$test_home/.local/state\\\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\\\"$test_home/.cache\\\" CLIENT_LEASE_TRACE=\\\"$trace_file\\\" NODE_OPTIONS='--import=/tmp/p10-client-lease-trace.mjs' node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern='job start has no way' test/unattended_gate.test.ts; printf '\\\\nTRACE\\\\n'; rg '\\\"event\\\":\\\"open\\\"|\\\"event\\\":\\