{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:02:22.549Z","ordinal":315531,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-553b86fe-df7d-4ba9-b401-2470f5fd1eee","process_id":"91653","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff --check && git status --short && git log -5 --oneline && gh pr view 934 --json title,body,headRefOid,baseRefName,url"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued/cli","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff --check && git status --short && git log -5 --oneline && gh pr view 934 --json title,body,headRefOid,baseRefName,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" M src/core/client_lease.ts\n M test/client_lease.test.ts\n7c644811a fix(cli): set client cap to supported ceiling\n6d7631910 fix(cli): scope admission to client home\ne0384ea9f fix(cli): allow test subprocess concurrency\nc5afe272b feat(cli): bound concurrent client processes\n0eb2d032a Merge pull request #933 from mikeholownych/codex/p10-02-postmerge-doc-evidence\n{\"baseRefName\":\"release/v1.3.1\",\"body\":\"## Summary\\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes using the same canonical home with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 64 per home, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — 5/5 passed on Node 24.11.1.\\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern=\\\"rejects an extra same-home sidecar\\\" test/sidecar.test.ts` — 1/1 passed on Node 24.11.1.\\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\n- Earlier exact-head CI showed that a per-OS-user global cap mixed unrelated homes, and a per-home default of 16 constrained existing same-home integration tests. Admission is per canonical home and now defaults to the existing hard maximum of 64; hosted CI for this latest exact head is pending.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes using one home.\\n\\n## Limits\\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes using one canonical home on one Linux host. Separate homes have separate limits. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\\n\",\"headRefOid\":\"7c644811a4acb62d71090d330bbbb32ee7957a0d\",\"title\":\"feat(cli): bound concurrent client processes\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":97908734}},"started_at_ms":1795849340450,"completed_at_ms":1795849342549}}
