{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:03:33.832Z","ordinal":315598,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a7cbb65f487d294d494f2fb9be89a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_88c651a82e854ffbbb8844d19964227e","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git push origin HEAD && python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nbody = '''## Summary\\n- Bound ordinary Linux Nexus CLI client processes using the same canonical home with the existing cross-process shared-slot admission mechanism; default 64 per home, configurable from 1 to 64 in the parent environment.\\n- Reuse the existing lifetime client lease and kernel-owned slots; exclusive state restore continues using its existing path.\\n- Wait up to 10 seconds for the shared admission guard so simultaneous client starts are not mistaken for capacity exhaustion; true capacity exhaustion still fails closed.\\n- Add cross-process and sidecar regressions, operator guidance, and current assurance-plan progress.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/client_lease.test.ts` — passed 3 consecutive runs on Node 24.11.1, including a 16-process same-home contention regression. The regression failed before the fix with false `ClientActiveLimitError` results.\\n- `npm run build` — passed on Node 24.11.1.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\n- Earlier exact-head CI showed that a per-OS-user global cap mixed unrelated homes, and a per-home default of 16 constrained existing same-home integration tests. Admission is per canonical home and defaults to the existing hard maximum of 64. The latest exact-head hosted CI is pending.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\nXERJ search of the local OpenCode corpus found process-local keyed mutex and child-process lease examples, but no directly applicable cross-process aggregate client admission design. This change reuses Nexus's existing `SharedResourceAdmission` and kernel-backed `FileGuard` slot mechanism. The unrelated process-local patterns were not used because they cannot coordinate independent CLI processes using one home.\\n\\n## Limits\\nThis caps cooperating Nexus client processes using one canonical home on one Linux host. Separate homes have separate limits. It does not cap sessions inside one process, CPU or memory, or non-Nexus processes. `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` must be set by the launching environment because admission runs before project `.env` loading. WP-P10-04 remains partially open for the other documented aggregate resource and recovery gaps.\\n'''\\nPath('/tmp/nexus-pr-934-body.md').write_text(body)\\nPY\\ngh pr edit 934 --body-file /tmp/nexus-pr-934-body.md && gh pr checks 934\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:2500});text(JSON.stringify(r))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795849403.4001644}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":138938,"sampled_through_sequence":138935,"client_authored":false}}
