/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35:- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37:- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51:| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n60:| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n61:| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n62:| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n63:| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n64:| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n65:| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n66:| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n67:| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n71:| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n72:| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n76:| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n86:3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97:| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n102:The following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n110:| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n2026-11-28T03:10:00Z ARCHIVE CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.taken-over-20261123T101212Z owner-approved reconciliation; preserve worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130 and local files; context maturity report records PR #911 merged as 2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7.\n2026-11-28T03:15:00Z CLAIM REDACTED.md codex/context-maturity-paperwork-20261127 - record verified PR #911 merge head 2c300c9 and post-merge checks.\n2026-11-28T03:18:00Z RELEASE REDACTED.md PR #930 merged as 007c9fc892568e9a1375662caee0db13a800b102; required exact-head checks passed (test-matrix 22/24, linux-x86_64, JS/TS); Entire advisory failed; post-merge CI and CodeQL still running; preserve worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-paperwork.\n2026-11-28T04:54:32Z RELEASE FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md PR #933 merged as 0eb2d032aaef1a96ab91b49f1bb1f00c36bb17fb; exact-head required checks passed; post-merge CI/CodeQL pending.\n2026-11-28T05:07:09Z POSTMERGE PR #933 merge 0eb2d032aaef1a96ab91b49f1bb1f00c36bb17fb; CI run 46109683174 and CodeQL run 46109683087 passed on exact merge commit; Entire advisory failed and is not a required merge check.\n2026-11-28T05:20:00Z RELEASE WP_P10_02_PLUGIN_PROCESS_BOUNDARY PR #932 merged as d0276535118aa197fc56371ab697220e20d5fd43; exact-head required checks passed; post-merge CI 46107372969 and CodeQL 46107372886 passed; preserved worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-plugin-process-boundary.\n2026-11-28T05:16:35Z CLAIM WP_P10_04_ACTIVE_CLIENT_ADMISSION codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=914858 bounded concurrent client admission\n2026-11-28T05:16:35Z CLAIM FILE_cli_src_core_client_lease.ts codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=914858 bounded concurrent client admission\n2026-11-28T05:16:35Z CLAIM FILE_cli_test_client_lease.test.ts codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=914858 bounded concurrent client admission\n2026-11-28T05:16:35Z CLAIM FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=914858 bounded concurrent client admission\n2026-11-28T05:22:36Z CLAIM FILE_docs_CLIENT_GUIDE.md codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=954566 document active client limit\n2026-11-28T05:23:33Z CLAIM FILE_cli_test_sidecar.test.ts codex/p10-04-active-client-admission-continued pid=956335 sidecar client admission integration test\n2026-11-28T06:31:16Z RELEASE REDACTED.md PR #935 merged as b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95; report records PR #930 merge 007c9fc and successful exact-head/post-merge checks; PR #935 exact-head required checks passed; post-merge CI/CodeQL pending.\n2026-11-28T06:45:00Z POST-MERGE REDACTED.md PR #935 merge b3f37c552aece6f3c810a856028152f68669cf95; CI run 46116988341 passed and CodeQL run 46116988355 passed.\n2026-11-28T06:58:50Z TAKEOVER WP_P10_04_ACTIVE_CLIENT_ADMISSION old_pid=914858 absent; FILE_cli_src_core_client_lease.ts old_pid=914858 absent; FILE_cli_test_client_lease.te