{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:29:11.238Z","ordinal":316213,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a82c592f887d28389ef9a7d459389","status":"completed","call_id":"call_7e4de475a2444eec8cc6f3c66a8f0312","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '137,160p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && git log --oneline -- docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md -6 && git status --short\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2600});text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795850949.577594}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139230,"sampled_through_sequence":139228,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:29:11.283Z","ordinal":316214,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0a82c3939c87d28a94a0ccbb5259ad","usage":{"input_tokens":130509,"cached_input_tokens":129152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":165,"reasoning_output_tokens":65,"total_tokens":130674},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":23617976,"cached_input_tokens":23303936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":52802,"reasoning_output_tokens":30672,"total_tokens":23670778},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6571510192,"cached_input_tokens":6497682816,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15191071,"reasoning_output_tokens":8953182,"total_tokens":6586701263}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:29:11.654Z","ordinal":316215,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-96997cb5-eafe-4fc7-8be8-7b223d386807","process_id":"84090","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '137,160p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && git log --oneline -- docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md -6 && git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '137,160p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && git log --oneline -- docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md -6 && git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02 for shared task budgets; existing operation-local scheduling is already implemented.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** The earlier claim that `Promise.all` makes operation scheduling unbounded was inaccurate. `ConvergenceScheduler.assign` bounds in-flight units by `effectiveConcurrency`, resource slots, and operation-local CPU/memory reservations (`cli/src/core/scheduler.ts:267-307`); parallel execution defaults to one and requires explicit per-unit requests and a per-operation budget (`cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:101-119`). `OperationRunner.executeBatch` uses `Promise.all` only for the already-admitted due set (`cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:276-299`). PR #830 added same-host cross-operation slots for declared inference resources; PR #831 added same-home LSP process slots. Remaining gaps are aggregate CPU/memory consumption, product-wide session/operation count, write-time disk limits, provider request/token/cost totals across separate processes, and cleanup/recovery accounting outside those lease boundaries. Those current gaps are not evidence that per-operation scheduling is unbounded, and no OS-level host CPU/memory ceiling is claimed.\n\n**Follow-up evidence (2026-11-26, current release):** Cross-operation inference-resource slots and same-home LSP slots have since been implemented in `SharedResourceAdmission` (PRs #830 and #831; see `docs/assurance/WP-P10-04_RESOURCE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.md`). A separate process-boundary probe on release commit `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d` confirms that `UsageLedger` provider request/token/cost caps remain process-local: two fresh Node 24.11.1 processes sharing one temporary `HOME` and workspace each admitted under `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS=1`, then wrote two receipts to the shared workspace file. No live inference was run. This is a confirmed gap only if these limits are expected to aggregate across processes; their reset/window semantics are not defined, so do not turn them into persistent global quotas without an explicit accounting epoch. Durable operation inference counters are the existing operation-scoped control and must not be duplicated here.\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `core/resources.ts`, operation scheduler/runner, client leases, tool runner, durable state/compaction and process cleanup.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Preserve the existing operation-local scheduler and `ResourceRegistry`; do not duplicate their admission checks. First inventory actual session, process, storage and provider ownership. Extend an existing shared lifecycle/lease boundary only where it can enforce aggregate limits across operations and sessions; if no such boundary exists, specify the smallest shared admission interface and make its ownership explicit. Reuse Rust process registry, output ring buffer, sandbox pids limit, `client_lease`, per-operation lock and session archival where they already cover the resource. Do not claim provider spend limits without a reliable token/cost source; use bounded request/token accounting when available and describe provider-side uncertainty.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing operation-level tests continue to show that units beyond `maxConcurrentUnits` or explicit CPU/memory budget remain unlaunched. New multi-operation/session tests demonstrate that aggregate configured limits are not exceeded under concurrent admission and that rejected admission has no side effect. Cancellation, process exit, failed persistence, and restart release or reconcile leases without orphan children. Repeated compaction/resume respects a measured active-context bound; retained disk has deterministic quota/retention behavior. Cross-session tests demonstrate no cross-workspace data access. Each claim must identify whether the limit is enforced in-process, across processes, or only per operation.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Start with advisory resource estimates, then enforce with operator-visible defaults; do not kill unrelated sessions. Rollback disables only the new admission layer while retaining process cleanup. Residual risk: OS estimates are approximate; host OOM remains an external failure mode without cgroups/container limits.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #889):** A shared, cross-process active-operation cap now reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version processes using the same admission store. It does not bound aggregate CPU/memory, session count, disk use, provider spend, or processes that do not participate in this lease protocol; older running Nexus versions do not hold the new lease until they exit. Cancellation and crash reconciliation outside the existing lease boundary still need separate evidence.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #919):** Session history archive writes enforce an aggregate cap equal to the existing 2 GiB retained-state ceiling. `SessionManager.assertSessionArchiveCapacity` scans archive files under the existing state-store guard, rejects unreadable/non-regular entries and scans above 100,000 entries, and refuses a write before archive append or fork creation if it would cross the cap. It preserves existing archives and does not add another cleanup or admission framework. The new `session_archive_bounds.test.ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n\n## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n\n**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n\n84d001032 docs(assurance): record plugin containment merge evidence\n3394b3a42 fix(plugins): reject malformed worker continuations\ne3bfcdf2a feat(plugins): contain callbacks in bounded workers\n6ed05cf49 docs(assurance): specify plugin execution containment\n5a868ae35 docs(assurance): record journal gate qualification\n3b0776dcf fix(recovery): checkpoint task before mutation journal\ne54a1f708 fix(recovery): enforce journal gate within complexity limit\naae698505 fix(recovery): block mutations without durable start record\nb77b8abb1 docs(assurance): record per-tool deadline merge evidence\n03e022f8c feat(tools): add bounded per-tool RPC deadlines\n70d19dbfb docs(assurance): reconcile P10-02 merged evidence\n95ac38186 docs(assurance): record P10-04 post-merge evidence\nd17785814 docs(assurance): record P10-04 exact-head CI\ne5d1e966e feat(session): bound aggregate history archives\n53cbe78dc docs(assurance): record P10 crash recovery evidence\nbcd9f2487 test(assurance): cover sibling outcomes after process crash\n5b8f36645 docs(assurance): reconcile P10-03 receipt fix evidence\n8d9419327 docs: record P10-04 aggregate operation cap\nd874160b0 docs(assurance): record crash recovery verification\n3650efe68 test(assurance): verify recovery after process crash\ncd3c8636a fix(operations): enforce admitted output token limits\n8b27b147c fix(acceptance): fail closed on receipt construction failure\n45a348808 docs(protocol): publish operation token stop reason\n495140a85 feat(operations): reserve token estimates before inference\n4bde469dd docs: record cross-process provider limit scope\n448f13fbe fix: gate operation completion on token budget\n2fa5a4f33 feat(operations): report durable token usage\n36e39deb9 docs(assurance): record operation inference budget evidence\n0517197dd docs(assurance): record P10-03 merge verification\n396c4a5e3 Correct acceptance identity verification status\n172941c09 Report legacy acceptance identity in audit exports\n2cd0310ee docs(assurance): reconcile inference budget evidence\n3add5f2f3 fix: bound non-command RPC timeout inputs\ncc0af6c02 fix: bound command RPC timeout configuration\n2d10d3780 feat: bind acceptance receipts to verification identity\n8ea727e87 fix: retire Rust workers after RPC timeouts\n2d9d4b21c docs: record P10-03 receipt failure enforcement\ne05726e4d feat(operation): bound aggregate active execution time\n61a9c6ccd docs(assurance): reconcile elapsed budget evidence\na9e8e2206 docs(protocol): record elapsed time fields in run result schema\n8bd9beb5a feat(assurance): bound cumulative objective execution time\n799cb508f docs(assurance): reconcile remediation plan with merged controls\n9f8f931fc docs(assurance): record candidate-binding verification\n7e58def9d feat(audit): bind exported receipts to the current candidate\n107053ef4 docs(assurance): update P10-03 flight evidence\nb36dac6c5 docs(assurance): record deadline and complexity gate evidence\n23a563ff3 ci: gate critical function complexity against release baseline\n826a2d545 docs(budget): clarify inference ceiling coverage\n748863d20 fix(audit): preserve flight recording gaps\nd24997ea9 fix(audit): expose skipped flight log records\n75a838be1 docs(plan): record inference budget publication\n3bde358c5 feat(budget): bound objective inference submissions\n18a42f6ab docs(assurance): align P10 plan with maintainer constraints\n8fb613a48 docs(budgets): document delegated invocation ceiling\nc690cae7b feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches\n8e28ca6ef docs(assurance): publish Power of Ten gap analysis\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":154508921}},"started_at_ms":1795850951499,"completed_at_ms":1795850951654}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:29:11.697Z","ordinal":316216,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2210e-dc10-71b0-8009-b7495291a5d7","call_id":"call_7e4de475a2444eec8cc6f3c66a8f0312","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2825)\nTotal output lines: 80\n\n## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02 for shared task budgets; existing operation-local scheduling is already implemented.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** The earlier claim that `Promise.all` makes operation scheduling unbounded was inaccurate. `ConvergenceScheduler.assign` bounds in-flight units by `effectiveConcurrency`, resource slots, and operation-local CPU/memory reservations (`cli/src/core/scheduler.ts:267-307`); parallel execution defaults to one and requires explicit per-unit requests and a per-operation budget (`cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:101-119`). `OperationRunner.executeBatch` uses `Promise.all` only for the already-admitted due set (`cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:276-299`). PR #830 added same-host cross-operation slots for declared inference resources; PR #831 added same-home LSP process slots. Remaining gaps are aggregate CPU/memory consumption, product-wide session/operation count, write-time disk limits, provider request/token/cost totals across separate processes, and cleanup/recovery accounting outside those lease boundaries. Those current gaps are not evidence that per-operation scheduling is unbounded, and no OS-level host CPU/memory ceiling is claimed.\n\n**Follow-up evidence (2026-11-26, current release):** Cross-operation inference-resource slots and same-home LSP slots have since been implemented in `SharedResourceAdmission` (PRs #830 and #831; see `docs/assurance/WP-P10-04_RESOURCE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.md`). A separate process-boundary probe on release commit `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d` confirms that `UsageLedger` provider request/token/cost caps remain process-local: two fresh Node 24.11.1 processes sharing one temporary `HOME` and workspace each admitted under `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS=1`, then wrote two receipts to the shared workspace file. No live inference was run. This is a confirmed gap only if these limits are expected to aggregate across processes; their reset/window semantics are not defined, so do not turn them into persistent global quotas without an explicit accounting epoch. Durable operation inference counters are the existing operation-scoped control and must not be duplicated here.\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `core/resources.ts`, operation scheduler/runner, client leases, tool runner, durable state/compaction and process cleanup.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Preserve the existing operation-local scheduler and `ResourceRegistry`; do not duplicate their admission checks. First inventory actual session, process, storage and provider ownership. Extend an existing shared lifecycle/lease boundary only where it can enforce aggregate limits across operations and sessions; if no such boundary exists, specify the smallest shared admission interface and make its ownership explicit. Reuse Rust process registry, output ring buffer, sandbox pids limit, `client_lease`, per-operation lock and session archival where they already cover the resource. Do not claim provider spend limits without a reliable token/cost source; use bounded request/token accounting when available and describe provider-side uncertainty.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing operation-level tests continue to show that units beyond `maxConcurrentUnits` or explicit CPU/memory budget remain unlaunched. New multi-operation/session tests demonstrate that aggregate configured limits are not exceeded under concurrent admission and that rejected admission has no side effect. Cancellation, process exit, failed persistence, and restart release or reconcile leases without orphan children. Repeated compaction/resume respects a measured active-context bound; retained disk has deterministic quota/retention behavior. Cross-session tests demonstrate no cross-workspace data access. Each claim must identify whether the limit is enforced in-process, across processes, or only per operation.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Start with advisory resource estimates, then enforce with operator-visible defaults; do not kill unrelated sessions. Rollback disables only the new admission layer while retaining process cleanup. Residual risk: OS estimates are approximate; host OOM remains an external failure mode without cgroups/container limits.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #889):** A shared, cross-process active-operation cap now reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version …225 tokens truncated…ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n\n## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n\n**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n\n84d001032 docs(assurance): record plugin containment merge evidence\n3394b3a42 fix(plugins): reject malformed worker continuations\ne3bfcdf2a feat(plugins): contain callbacks in bounded workers\n6ed05cf49 docs(assurance): specify plugin execution containment\n5a868ae35 docs(assurance): record journal gate qualification\n3b0776dcf fix(recovery): checkpoint task before mutation journal\ne54a1f708 fix(recovery): enforce journal gate within complexity limit\naae698505 fix(recovery): block mutations without durable start record\nb77b8abb1 docs(assurance): record per-tool deadline merge evidence\n03e022f8c feat(tools): add bounded per-tool RPC deadlines\n70d19dbfb docs(assurance): reconcile P10-02 merged evidence\n95ac38186 docs(assurance): record P10-04 post-merge evidence\nd17785814 docs(assurance): record P10-04 exact-head CI\ne5d1e966e feat(session): bound aggregate history archives\n53cbe78dc docs(assurance): record P10 crash recovery evidence\nbcd9f2487 test(assurance): cover sibling outcomes after process crash\n5b8f36645 docs(assurance): reconcile P10-03 receipt fix evidence\n8d9419327 docs: record P10-04 aggregate operation cap\nd874160b0 docs(assurance): record crash recovery verification\n3650efe68 test(assurance): verify recovery after process crash\ncd3c8636a fix(operations): enforce admitted output token limits\n8b27b147c fix(acceptance): fail closed on receipt construction failure\n45a348808 docs(protocol): publish operation token stop reason\n495140a85 feat(operations): reserve token estimates before inference\n4bde469dd docs: record cross-process provider limit scope\n448f13fbe fix: gate operation completion on token budget\n2fa5a4f33 feat(operations): report durable token usage\n36e39deb9 docs(assurance): record operation inference budget evidence\n0517197dd docs(assurance): record P10-03 merge verification\n396c4a5e3 Correct acceptance identity verification status\n172941c09 Report legacy acceptance identity in audit exports\n2cd0310ee docs(assurance): reconcile inference budget evidence\n3add5f2f3 fix: bound non-command RPC timeout inputs\ncc0af6c02 fix: bound command RPC timeout configuration\n2d10d3780 feat: bind acceptance receipts to verification identity\n8ea727e87 fix: retire Rust workers after RPC timeouts\n2d9d4b21c docs: record P10-03 receipt failure enforcement\ne05726e4d feat(operation): bound aggregate active execution time\n61a9c6ccd docs(assurance): reconcile elapsed budget evidence\na9e8e2206 docs(protocol): record elapsed time fields in run result schema\n8bd9beb5a feat(assurance): bound cumulative objective execution time\n799cb508f docs(assurance): reconcile remediation plan with merged controls\n9f8f931fc docs(assurance): record candidate-binding verification\n7e58def9d feat(audit): bind exported receipts to the current candidate\n107053ef4 docs(assurance): update P10-03 flight evidence\nb36dac6c5 docs(assurance): record deadline and complexity gate evidence\n23a563ff3 ci: gate critical function complexity against release baseline\n826a2d545 docs(budget): clarify inference ceiling coverage\n748863d20 fix(audit): preserve flight recording gaps\nd24997ea9 fix(audit): expose skipped flight log records\n75a838be1 docs(plan): record inference budget publication\n3bde358c5 feat(budget): bound objective inference submissions\n18a42f6ab docs(assurance): align P10 plan with maintainer constraints\n8fb613a48 docs(budgets): document delegated invocation ceiling\nc690cae7b feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches\n8e28ca6ef docs(assurance): publish Power of Ten gap analysis\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795850951.6968403}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139231,"sampled_through_sequence":139228,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
