{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:30:27.675Z","ordinal":316249,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a830a379887d2a39eb91f33fd0053","status":"completed","call_id":"call_1e7ade6b7d424a0dad9a68ab244d5b92","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-client-admission-evidence/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\\n+**Progress (2026-11-28, merged PR #934):** Linux CLI clients sharing one canonical home now use the existing kernel-backed client lease and `SharedResourceAdmission` to enforce a configurable process cap, defaulting to 64. The admission guard waits at most 10 seconds so simultaneous starts do not turn lock contention into a false “client limit reached” result; genuine slot exhaustion still refuses admission. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced the false refusal before the wait-bound fix and passed in three consecutive runs afterward on Node 24.11.1. `npm run build` passed. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices and all eight shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host; it does not bound sessions inside a process, resource consumption, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\\n+\\n+## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\nconst r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --check && git diff -- docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && git status --short\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-client-admission-evidence\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2200});text(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795851018.2400491}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139246,"sampled_through_sequence":139244,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:30:27.754Z","ordinal":316250,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0ed0f250-0e52-44f1-a965-d5450e0dd173","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-client-admission-evidence/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -158,2 +158,4 @@\n \n+**Progress (2026-11-28, merged PR #934):** Linux CLI clients sharing one canonical home now use the existing kernel-backed client lease and `SharedResourceAdmission` to enforce a configurable process cap, defaulting to 64. The admission guard waits at most 10 seconds so simultaneous starts do not turn lock contention into a false “client limit reached” result; genuine slot exhaustion still refuses admission. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced the false refusal before the wait-bound fix and passed in three consecutive runs afterward on Node 24.11.1. `npm run build` passed. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices and all eight shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host; it does not bound sessions inside a process, resource consumption, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n+\n ## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-04-client-admission-evidence/docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795851027751,"completed_at_ms":1795851027754}}
