{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:56:53.031Z","ordinal":316914,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a893ebafc87d2b996c86c255f7bde","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The client-admission work from the interrupted slice is complete and merged:\n\n- [PR #934](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934) fixes false “client limit reached” errors during simultaneous starts. Its regression reproduced the failure before the fix and passed three consecutive times afterward. The TypeScript build, required PR checks, post-merge CI, and CodeQL all passed.\n- [PR #936](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/936) updates the assurance plan with the verified results and remaining limits. Its required checks, post-merge CI, and CodeQL all passed.\n- The Entire checks failed as advisories on both PRs; they were not required merge gates. The worktrees are preserved and clean, and the related claims are archived.\n\n**The broader WP-P10-04 work remains open.** Its documented gaps include aggregate CPU and memory limits, provider-accounting scope, session counts, and cleanup or recovery beyond current lease boundaries. I found no other open P10-related PRs, but these remaining roadmap items are not complete.\n\nThe owner checkout is clean at `688e29a`; its local `release/v1.3.1` branch is eight commits behind `origin/release/v1.3.1` at `9a4ebe08`. I left that checkout untouched.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":43,"lineEnd":47,"note":"rechecked current PR and hosted check state rather than relying on historical status"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"content_token_count":342,"started_at_ms":1795852606757,"completed_at_ms":1795852613031}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:56:53.046Z","ordinal":316915,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a893ebafc87d2b996c86c255f7bde","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The client-admission work from the interrupted slice is complete and merged:\n\n- [PR #934](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/934) fixes false “client limit reached” errors during simultaneous starts. Its regression reproduced the failure before the fix and passed three consecutive times afterward. The TypeScript build, required PR checks, post-merge CI, and CodeQL all passed.\n- [PR #936](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/936) updates the assurance plan with the verified results and remaining limits. Its required checks, post-merge CI, and CodeQL all passed.\n- The Entire checks failed as advisories on both PRs; they were not required merge gates. The worktrees are preserved and clean, and the related claims are archived.\n\n**The broader WP-P10-04 work remains open.** Its documented gaps include aggregate CPU and memory limits, provider-accounting scope, session counts, and cleanup or recovery beyond current lease boundaries. I found no other open P10-related PRs, but these remaining roadmap items are not complete.\n\nThe owner checkout is clean at `688e29a`; its local `release/v1.3.1` branch is eight commits behind `origin/release/v1.3.1` at `9a4ebe08`. I left that checkout untouched.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:43-47|note=[rechecked current PR and hosted check state rather than relying on historical status]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a220e5-c285-7e72-9bb5-c6a32a48db70","create_time":1795852606.733608,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139558,"sampled_through_sequence":1395