{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:57:04.103Z","ordinal":316934,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a1b2e680-b61a-42b3-b583-141633e51da5","process_id":"82997","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short && git rev-parse HEAD && git rev-parse origin/release/v1.3.1 && git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/release/v1.3.1 && gh pr list --state open --limit 100 --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,url && sed -n '120,205p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name 'WP_P10*' -printf '%f\\n' | sort"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short && git rev-parse HEAD && git rev-parse origin/release/v1.3.1 && git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/release/v1.3.1 && gh pr list --state open --limit 100 --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,url && sed -n '120,205p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && find \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name 'WP_P10*' -printf '%f\\n' | sort"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"688e29a402b71dcfe2243fec466afe36fc963b56\n9a4ebe08bebe67b2418b4912f1df09eb818dbe87\n0\t8\n[]\n\n**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, merged as `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required checks passed on PR merge candidate `117ea0a807c0070333d401da5f7994cb694cc705`; post-merge CI passed on `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`.\n\n**Stacked Git-configuration follow-up (PR #772, merged as `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84`):** Audit export lists repository-scoped Git settings that name executable programs or redirect Git behavior and marks receipt binding unavailable when any are present or the listing fails. Its five adversarial configurations are tested with a same-size tracked-file re-hash. The negative control without the preflight executes the planted clean filter and fails the marker assertion. Local verification passed on Node 24: `audit_export` 20/20, `audit_command` 8/8, `audit_bundle` 25/25, `audit_schema` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6, `candidate_git_paths` 36/36, and `tsc --noEmit`. Required PR checks passed on merge candidate `99a742ce529df0b79facb936002993e46e1d16f6`; post-merge CI passed on `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84` (run `45351066175`; CodeQL run `45351065784`). The non-required Entire check failed and did not gate merging under repository guidance.\n\n**Mandatory receipt-persistence failure slice (PR #858, merged as `33565128d7e2be14d7e80a09757144c3da28430a`):** If durable candidate-receipt persistence fails or the durable task state is unavailable, the in-memory receipt is invalidated, verified completion remains false, and the turn returns `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the speculative worktree is retained and cannot auto-merge. Failure injection verifies this path, while the successful receipt-binding regression still verifies normal acceptance and merge. Local focused tests passed (2/2), adjacent audit-export tests passed (21/21), and `npm run build` passed. Required checks passed on the exact PR merge candidate; post-merge CI run `45745010423` and CodeQL run `45745010340` passed on descendant release tip `1a5a05b204bba6cebe4ccbf2aaf94c571d474eae`, which includes the fix.\n\n**Acceptance identity slice (PR #863, merged):** Candidate validation receipts now include the source revision and candidate digest/id, verifier command and result, a digest of the pre-change verifier definition when available, Nexus/Node/OS/architecture identity, and a canonical digest of the effective policy and verifier configuration. Raw verifier contents and effective policy are not copied into the receipt. The receipt explicitly records `independentApproval: \"unavailable_single_maintainer\"`; it does not assert independent review. `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` checks the receipt fields, confirms the verifier source sentinel is absent, and retains the failure-closed persistence assertions. `audit_export.test.ts` checks that the existing state manager and audit bundle preserve the identity. Required PR checks passed on exact head `2d10d3780c0621d3cd5b9aecb811cbe30b4ea074`; post-merge CI run `45773723629` and CodeQL run `45773723883` passed on release commit `a421799bacaeb94d5dc64b5726dce18e6c1dd658`. WP-P10-03 still has same-user evidence mutability and no independent approval.\n\n**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\n\n**Receipt-construction fail-closed slice (PR #884, release; PR #886, main):** The first implementation's outer receipt-construction catch only cleared `verifiedWorktreeCompletion`; if candidate identity construction threw after a passing configured verifier, `task_completed` still returned success and the final turn was `COMPLETED/VERIFIED`. A failure-injection regression reproduced this at release base `abfa58c62c651ed4e113d0d9203667986739289d`. The catch now sets the existing acceptance failure latch, clears the active in-memory receipt, and invalidates any receipt for the candidate worktree. `run_turn.ts` consumes that latch as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; no change to the turn runner was needed. The merged regression asserts non-success, no active receipt, and no auto-merge while retaining the worktree. PR #884 merged as `4987ac573fe8415e3fe561a2adbb82d77014afde` on `release/v1.3.1`; all required exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI run `45911392549` and CodeQL run `45911392550` succeeded on that merge commit. PR #886 forward-ported the fix to `main` at `881798b282a0bc1198628955d5645ae27402b1b6`; all required exact-head checks passed (CI run `45920208046`, CodeQL run `45920208028`). I reran `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` and `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` together on Node 24.11.1 with the worktree-local Rust core built; all 3 tests passed. The earlier local attempts without that core were invalid because the verifier/tool runner never reached receipt creation. No independent approver is available; this local failure-injection test does not add external evidence immutability or independent review.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing tests cover altered, deleted, reordered and truncated events and candidate mutation invalidation. Failure injection confirms an omitted event cannot be followed by an apparently intact chain, sanitizer failure does not preserve that claim, and mandatory receipt-persistence failure prevents verified acceptance. The release/v1.3.1 acceptance-identity slice adds source revision, candidate digest, verifier definition digest, command/result, runtime, and policy identity to durable receipts and verifies bundle retention. Legacy receipt export migration behavior is now tested: older receipts remain readable with their historical status, are not assigned synthesized acceptance identity, and are explicitly identified as missing structured identity. Exact-head CI and post-merge CI/CodeQL are complete for the legacy export follow-up. Same-user bundle mutability and the lack of independent approval remain explicit limitations; local evidence does not provide external immutability or a second-person review.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Legacy logs remain readable but classify `integrity=unverified_legacy`; never silently “upgrade” them to verified. Keep old export path read-only during migration. Residual risk: same-user can delete both evidence and local chain unless an external signed/immutable copy is retained.\n\n## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02 for shared task budgets; existing operation-local scheduling is already implemented.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** The earlier claim that `Promise.all` makes operation scheduling unbounded was inaccurate. `ConvergenceScheduler.assign` bounds in-flight units by `effectiveConcurrency`, resource slots, and operation-local CPU/memory reservations (`cli/src/core/scheduler.ts:267-307`); parallel execution defaults to one and requires explicit per-unit requests and a per-operation budget (`cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:101-119`). `OperationRunner.executeBatch` uses `Promise.all` only for the already-admitted due set (`cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:276-299`). PR #830 added same-host cross-operation slots for declared inference resources; PR #831 added same-home LSP process slots. Remaining gaps are aggregate CPU/memory consumption, product-wide session/operation count, write-time disk limits, provider request/token/cost totals across separate processes, and cleanup/recovery accounting outside those lease boundaries. Those current gaps are not evidence that per-operation scheduling is unbounded, and no OS-level host CPU/memory ceiling is claimed.\n\n**Follow-up evidence (2026-11-26, current release):** Cross-operation inference-resource slots and same-home LSP slots have since been implemented in `SharedResourceAdmission` (PRs #830 and #831; see `docs/assurance/WP-P10-04_RESOURCE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.md`). A separate process-boundary probe on release commit `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d` confirms that `UsageLedger` provider request/token/cost caps remain process-local: two fresh Node 24.11.1 processes sharing one temporary `HOME` and workspace each admitted under `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS=1`, then wrote two receipts to the shared workspace file. No live inference was run. This is a confirmed gap only if these limits are expected to aggregate across processes; their reset/window semantics are not defined, so do not turn them into persistent global quotas without an explicit accounting epoch. Durable operation inference counters are the existing operation-scoped control and must not be duplicated here.\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `core/resources.ts`, operation scheduler/runner, client leases, tool runner, durable state/compaction and process cleanup.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Preserve the existing operation-local scheduler and `ResourceRegistry`; do not duplicate their admission checks. First inventory actual session, process, storage and provider ownership. Extend an existing shared lifecycle/lease boundary only where it can enforce aggregate limits across operations and sessions; if no such boundary exists, specify the smallest shared admission interface and make its ownership explicit. Reuse Rust process registry, output ring buffer, sandbox pids limit, `client_lease`, per-operation lock and session archival where they already cover the resource. Do not claim provider spend limits without a reliable token/cost source; use bounded request/token accounting when available and describe provider-side uncertainty.\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing operation-level tests continue to show that units beyond `maxConcurrentUnits` or explicit CPU/memory budget remain unlaunched. New multi-operation/session tests demonstrate that aggregate configured limits are not exceeded under concurrent admission and that rejected admission has no side effect. Cancellation, process exit, failed persistence, and restart release or reconcile leases without orphan children. Repeated compaction/resume respects a measured active-context bound; retained disk has deterministic quota/retention behavior. Cross-session tests demonstrate no cross-workspace data access. Each claim must identify whether the limit is enforced in-process, across processes, or only per operation.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** Start with advisory resource estimates, then enforce with operator-visible defaults; do not kill unrelated sessions. Rollback disables only the new admission layer while retaining process cleanup. Residual risk: OS estimates are approximate; host OOM remains an external failure mode without cgroups/container limits.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #889):** A shared, cross-process active-operation cap now reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version processes using the same admission store. It does not bound aggregate CPU/memory, session count, disk use, provider spend, or processes that do not participate in this lease protocol; older running Nexus versions do not hold the new lease until they exit. Cancellation and crash reconciliation outside the existing lease boundary still need separate evidence.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #919):** Session history archive writes enforce an aggregate cap equal to the existing 2 GiB retained-state ceiling. `SessionManager.assertSessionArchiveCapacity` scans archive files under the existing state-store guard, rejects unreadable/non-regular entries and scans above 100,000 entries, and refuses a write before archive append or fork creation if it would cross the cap. It preserves existing archives and does not add another cleanup or admission framework. The new `session_archive_bounds.test.ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n\n## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n\n**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n\n**Gap/evidence:** Strict TS build, CodeQL JS/TS, Clippy, and diff-scoped rustfmt are present in CI. No Rust CodeQL or targeted complexity gate was found. `runTurnImpl` remains a critical large function.\n\n**Affected surfaces:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `core/Cargo.toml`, TS configuration and targeted complexity documentation.\n\n**Design / reuse:** Reuse the existing `make lint` gate for typecheck, Clippy, and changed-file rustfmt; do not add a duplicate CI job. Keep Rust warnings scoped and justified rather than inventing a large analyzer bundle. Add complexity reporting or thresholds only for critical high-change functions after measuring the baseline; avoid arbitrary whole-repository size caps.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75,196-197`). Workflow run `45047617708` completed successfully on that exact main SHA, including all three static-gate steps. Do not add a duplicate Clippy job. Remaining work in this package is a narrowly scoped, evidence-based complexity metric and its enforcement policy; the independent protection dependency from WP-P10-01 remains unavailable in this single-user repository.\n\n**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #766):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails if a tracked function disappears or its cyclomatic complexity or control nesting increases, and reports line count without enforcing a global size cap. Extracted helpers require separate assessment. The focused tests passed 3/3; typecheck, Clippy, and fmt passed. PR #766's required Node 22/24, Linux, and test-shard checks passed at exact head `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631`; post-merge CI passed on `061843fc5fca4c874ac298093120b46073e50ab9` (`45319250946`).\n\n**Required tests / acceptance:** The focused tests prove that decision-count and nesting growth are rejected and that the tracked release-baseline functions pass. `make lint` runs in the required Node 22/24 and Linux CI gates. The gate also fails closed if a tracked function or baseline source cannot be resolved. The verification workflow remains changeable by the sole maintainer under the current single-user policy; independent protection is unavailable and must not be implied.\n\n**Migration / rollback:** If historical warnings appear on a new toolchain, baseline them narrowly with tracked expiry/owner; do not suppress globally. The sole maintainer may direct rollback of this specific gate; any rollback must be visible in the PR and must not be described as independently approved. Residual risk: static analysis cannot establish requirements correctness or provider behavior.\n\n## Dependency-aware order\n\n1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\n4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\n\nEach implementable package lands independently with its own negative tests. CI green on a PR is not proof the implementation is correct; hosted checks must be tied to the exact candidate and reported alongside the single-maintainer review limitation.\nWP_P10_02_CRASH_EVIDENCE_DOCS.released-20261127T075558Z-pr899-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_DURABLE_BUDGET.released-20261119-rd7\nWP_P10_02_DURABLE_EFFECT_JOURNAL_FAIL_CLOSED.released-20261128T011343Z-pr924-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_HARD_TOKEN_RESERVATION.released-20261126T231636Z-pr883-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_OBJECTIVE_ELAPSED_BUDGET.released-20261124T1030Z-pr774-merged\nWP_P10_02_OPERATION_INFERENCE_ADMISSION.released-20261126T11-pr869-pr870-postmerge\nWP_P10_02_PLUGIN_EXECUTION_BOUNDARY.released-20261128T024240Z-pr928-docs\nWP_P10_02_POSTMERGE_DOC_EVIDENCE.released-20261128T014209Z-pr926-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_PROGRESS_RECONCILIATION.released-20261125-pr821-merged\nWP_P10_02_PROVIDER_ENFORCED_OUTPUT_CEILING.released-20261127T004111Z-pr885-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_PROVIDER_OUTCOME_FOLLOWUP.released-20261127T1300Z-pr901-merged-ci\nWP_P10_02_RPC_TIMEOUT_WORKER_TERMINATION.released-20261126T060322Z-pr862-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_SHARED_REQUEST_ADMISSION.released-20261126T021315Z-pr857-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_02_TOOL_TIMEOUT_BOUND.released-20261126T0642Z-pr864-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_03_ACCEPTANCE_IDENTITY.released-20261126T055401Z-pr863-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_03_ACCEPTANCE_RECEIPT_CREATION.released-20261126T234314Z-pr884-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_03_AUDIT_PLAN_EVIDENCE.released-20261124T050116Z-pr769-merged\nWP_P10_03_MAIN_FORWARDPORT.released-20261126-pr873-merged\nWP_P10_03_POSTMERGE_EVIDENCE.released-20261126T11-pr869-pr870-postmerge\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_CONSTRUCTION_CURRENT.released-20261127T1346Z-pr904-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_CONSTRUCTION_FOLLOWUP.released-20261127T-release-superseded-pr884\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_FAIL_CLOSED.released-20261126T030311Z-pr858-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_PERSISTENCE.taken-over-20261125T220442Z-owner-approved-p10-03.released-20261126T134840Z-pr858-merged\nWP_P10_04_ACTIVE_CLIENT_ADMISSION.released-20261128T0744Z-pr934-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_04_ACTIVE_OPERATION_ADMISSION.released-20261127T-PROGRESS-PR889\nWP_P10_04_AGGREGATE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.released-20261125T163335Z-pr829-merged\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_OPERATION_ADMISSION.released-20261125T181901Z-pr830-merged\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_OPERATION_ADMISSION_TEST_FIXTURE.released-20261125T181901Z-pr830-merged\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_SESSION_LSP_ADMISSION.released-20261125T191442Z-pr831-merged\nWP_P10_04_PLAN_STATUS.released-20261127T0345Z-pr890-postmerge-ci\nWP_P10_04_SESSION_ARCHIVE_BOUND.released-20261128T011515Z-pr920-postmerge-ci\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":434812143}},"started_at_ms":1795852623668,"completed_at_ms":1795852624103}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:57:04.151Z","ordinal":316935,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a22128-6117-7f90-849e-3e6f5a8be55d","call_id":"call_e1047ff86a6345988a47ef277fd72c91","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f9560a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.434988506,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5720,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5720)\\nTotal output lines: 99\\n\\n688e29a402b71dcfe2243fec466afe36fc963b56\\n9a4ebe08bebe67b2418b4912f1df09eb818dbe87\\n0\\t8\\n[]\\n\\n**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, merged as `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required checks passed on PR merge candidate `117ea0a807c0070333d401da5f7994cb694cc705`; post-merge CI passed on `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`.\\n\\n**Stacked Git-configuration follow-up (PR #772, merged as `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84`):** Audit export lists repository-scoped Git settings that name executable programs or redirect Git behavior and marks receipt binding unavailable when any are present or the listing fails. Its five adversarial configurations are tested with a same-size tracked-file re-hash. The negative control without the preflight executes the planted clean filter and fails the marker assertion. Local verification passed on Node 24: `audit_export` 20/20, `audit_command` 8/8, `audit_bundle` 25/25, `audit_schema` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6, `candidate_git_paths` 36/36, and `tsc --noEmit`. Required PR checks passed on merge candidate `99a742ce529df0b79facb936002993e46e1d16f6`; post-merge CI passed on `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84` (run `45351066175`; CodeQL run `45351065784`). The non-required Entire check failed and did not gate merging under repository guidance.\\n\\n**Mandatory receipt-persistence failure slice (PR #858, merged as `33565128d7e2be14d7e80a09757144c3da28430a`):** If durable candidate-receipt persistence fails or the durable task state is unavailable, the in-memory receipt is invalidated, verified completion remains false, and the turn returns `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the speculative worktree is retained and cannot auto-merge. Failure injection verifies this path, while the successful receipt-binding regression still verifies normal acceptance and merge. Local focused tests passed (2/2), adjacent audit-export tests passed (21/21), and `npm run build` passed. Required checks passed on the exact PR merge candidate; post-merge CI run `45745010423` and CodeQL run `45745010340` passed on descendant release tip `1a5a05b204bba6cebe4ccbf2aaf94c571d474eae`, which includes the fix.\\n\\n**Acceptance identity slice (PR #863, merged):** Candidate validation receipts now include the source revision and candidate digest/id, verifier command and result, a digest of the pre-change verifier definition when available, Nexus/Node/OS/architecture identity, and a canonical digest of the effective policy and verifier configuration. Raw verifier contents and effective policy are not copied into the receipt. The receipt explicitly records `independentApproval: \\\"unavailable_single_maintainer\\\"`; it does not assert independent review. `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` checks the receipt fields, confirms the verifier source sentinel is absent, and retains the failure-closed persistence assertions. `audit_export.test.ts` checks that the existing state manager and audit bundle preserve the identity. Required PR checks passed on exact head `2d10d3780c0621d3cd5b9aecb811cbe30b4ea074`; post-merge CI run `45773723629` and CodeQL run `45773723883` passed on release commit `a421799bacaeb94d5dc64b5726dce18e6c1dd658`. WP-P10-03 still has same-user evidence mutability and no independent approval.\\n\\n**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\\n\\n**Receipt-construction fail-closed slice (PR #884, release; PR #886, main):** The first implementation's outer receipt-construction catch only cleared `verifiedWorktreeCompletion`; if candidate identity construction threw after a passing configured verifier, `task_completed` still returned success and the final turn was `COMPLETED/VERIFIED`. A failure-injection regression reproduced this at release base `abfa58c62c651ed4e113d0d9203667986739289d`. The catch now sets the existing acceptance failure latch, clears the active in-memory receipt, and invalidates any receipt for the candidate worktree. `run_turn.ts` consumes that latch as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; no change to the turn runner was needed. The merged regression asserts non-success, no active receipt, and no auto-merge while retaining the worktree. PR #884 merged as `4987ac573fe8415e3fe561a2adbb82d77014afde` on `release/v1.3.1`; all required exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI run `45911392549` and CodeQL run `45911392550` succeeded on that merge commit. PR #886 forward-ported the fix to `main` at `881798b282a0bc1198628955d5645ae27402b1b6`; all required exact-head checks passed (CI run `45920208046`, CodeQL run `45920208028`). I reran `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` and `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` together on Node 24.11.1 with the worktree-local Rust core built; all 3 tests passed. The earlier local attempts without that core were invalid because the verifier/tool runner never reached receipt creation. No independent approver is available; this local failure-injection test does not add external evidence immutability or independent review.\\n\\n**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing tests cover altered, deleted, reordered and truncated events and candidate mutation invalidation. Failure injection confirms an omitted event cannot be followed by an apparently intact chain, sanitizer failure does not preserve that claim, and mandatory receipt-persistence failure prevents verified acceptance. The release/v1.3.1 acceptance-identity slice adds source revision, candidate digest, verifier definition digest, command/result, runtime, and policy identity to durable receipts and verifies bundle retention. Legacy receipt export migration behavior is now tested: older receipts remain readable with their historical status, are not assigned synthesized acceptance identity, and are explicitly identified as missing structured identity. Exact-head CI and post-merge CI/CodeQL are complete for the legacy export follow-up. Same-user bundle mutability and the lack of independent approval remain explicit limitations; local evidence does not provide external immutability or a second-person review.\\n\\n**Migration / rollback:** Legacy logs remain readable but classify `integrity=unverified_legacy`; never silently “upgrade” them to verified. Keep old export path read-only during migration. Residual risk: same-user can delete both evidence and local chain unless an external signed/immutable copy is retained.\\n\\n## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\\n\\n**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02 for shared task budgets; existing operation-local scheduling is already implemented.\\n\\n**Gap/evidence:** The earlier claim that `Promise.all` makes operation scheduling unbounded was inaccurate. `ConvergenceScheduler.assign` bounds in-flight units by `effectiveConcurrency`, resource slots, and operation-local CPU/memory reservations (`cli/src/core/scheduler.ts:267-307`); parallel execution defaults to one and requires explicit per-unit requests and a per-operation budget (`cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:101-119`). `OperationRunner.executeBatch` uses `Promise.all` only for the already-admitted due set (`cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:276-299`). PR #830 added same-host cross-operation slots for declared inference resources; PR #831 added same-home LSP process slots. Remaining gaps are aggregate CPU/memory consumption, product-wide session/operation count, write-time disk limits, provider request/token/cost totals across separate processes, and cleanup/recovery accounting outside those lease boundaries. Those current gaps are not evidence that per-operation scheduling is unbounded, and no OS-level host CPU/memory ceiling is claimed.\\n\\n**Follow-up evidence (2026-11-26, current release):** Cross-operation inference-resource slots and same-home LSP slots have since been implemented in `SharedResourceAdmission` (PRs #830 and #831; see `docs/assura…720 tokens truncated…reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version processes using the same admission store. It does not bound aggregate CPU/memory, session count, disk use, provider spend, or processes that do not participate in this lease protocol; older running Nexus versions do not hold the new lease until they exit. Cancellation and crash reconciliation outside the existing lease boundary still need separate evidence.\\n\\n**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #919):** Session history archive writes enforce an aggregate cap equal to the existing 2 GiB retained-state ceiling. `SessionManager.assertSessionArchiveCapacity` scans archive files under the existing state-store guard, rejects unreadable/non-regular entries and scans above 100,000 entries, and refuses a write before archive append or fork creation if it would cross the cap. It preserves existing archives and does not add another cleanup or admission framework. The new `session_archive_bounds.test.ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\\n\\n## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\\n\\n**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\\n\\n**Gap/evidence:** Strict TS build, CodeQL JS/TS, Clippy, and diff-scoped rustfmt are present in CI. No Rust CodeQL or targeted complexity gate was found. `runTurnImpl` remains a critical large function.\\n\\n**Affected surfaces:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `core/Cargo.toml`, TS configuration and targeted complexity documentation.\\n\\n**Design / reuse:** Reuse the existing `make lint` gate for typecheck, Clippy, and changed-file rustfmt; do not add a duplicate CI job. Keep Rust warnings scoped and justified rather than inventing a large analyzer bundle. Add complexity reporting or thresholds only for critical high-change functions after measuring the baseline; avoid arbitrary whole-repository size caps.\\n\\n**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75,196-197`). Workflow run `45047617708` completed successfully on that exact main SHA, including all three static-gate steps. Do not add a duplicate Clippy job. Remaining work in this package is a narrowly scoped, evidence-based complexity metric and its enforcement policy; the independent protection dependency from WP-P10-01 remains unavailable in this single-user repository.\\n\\n**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #766):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails if a tracked function disappears or its cyclomatic complexity or control nesting increases, and reports line count without enforcing a global size cap. Extracted helpers require separate assessment. The focused tests passed 3/3; typecheck, Clippy, and fmt passed. PR #766's required Node 22/24, Linux, and test-shard checks passed at exact head `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631`; post-merge CI passed on `061843fc5fca4c874ac298093120b46073e50ab9` (`45319250946`).\\n\\n**Required tests / acceptance:** The focused tests prove that decision-count and nesting growth are rejected and that the tracked release-baseline functions pass. `make lint` runs in the required Node 22/24 and Linux CI gates. The gate also fails closed if a tracked function or baseline source cannot be resolved. The verification workflow remains changeable by the sole maintainer under the current single-user policy; independent protection is unavailable and must not be implied.\\n\\n**Migration / rollback:** If historical warnings appear on a new toolchain, baseline them narrowly with tracked expiry/owner; do not suppress globally. The sole maintainer may direct rollback of this specific gate; any rollback must be visible in the PR and must not be described as independently approved. Residual risk: static analysis cannot establish requirements correctness or provider behavior.\\n\\n## Dependency-aware order\\n\\n1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\\n2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\\n3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\\n4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\\n5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\\n\\nEach implementable package lands independently with its own negative tests. CI green on a PR is not proof the implementation is correct; hosted checks must be tied to the exact candidate and reported alongside the single-maintainer review limitation.\\nWP_P10_02_CRASH_EVIDENCE_DOCS.released-20261127T075558Z-pr899-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_DURABLE_BUDGET.released-20261119-rd7\\nWP_P10_02_DURABLE_EFFECT_JOURNAL_FAIL_CLOSED.released-20261128T011343Z-pr924-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_HARD_TOKEN_RESERVATION.released-20261126T231636Z-pr883-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_OBJECTIVE_ELAPSED_BUDGET.released-20261124T1030Z-pr774-merged\\nWP_P10_02_OPERATION_INFERENCE_ADMISSION.released-20261126T11-pr869-pr870-postmerge\\nWP_P10_02_PLUGIN_EXECUTION_BOUNDARY.released-20261128T024240Z-pr928-docs\\nWP_P10_02_POSTMERGE_DOC_EVIDENCE.released-20261128T014209Z-pr926-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_PROGRESS_RECONCILIATION.released-20261125-pr821-merged\\nWP_P10_02_PROVIDER_ENFORCED_OUTPUT_CEILING.released-20261127T004111Z-pr885-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_PROVIDER_OUTCOME_FOLLOWUP.released-20261127T1300Z-pr901-merged-ci\\nWP_P10_02_RPC_TIMEOUT_WORKER_TERMINATION.released-20261126T060322Z-pr862-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_SHARED_REQUEST_ADMISSION.released-20261126T021315Z-pr857-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_02_TOOL_TIMEOUT_BOUND.released-20261126T0642Z-pr864-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_03_ACCEPTANCE_IDENTITY.released-20261126T055401Z-pr863-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_03_ACCEPTANCE_RECEIPT_CREATION.released-20261126T234314Z-pr884-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_03_AUDIT_PLAN_EVIDENCE.released-20261124T050116Z-pr769-merged\\nWP_P10_03_MAIN_FORWARDPORT.released-20261126-pr873-merged\\nWP_P10_03_POSTMERGE_EVIDENCE.released-20261126T11-pr869-pr870-postmerge\\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_CONSTRUCTION_CURRENT.released-20261127T1346Z-pr904-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_CONSTRUCTION_FOLLOWUP.released-20261127T-release-superseded-pr884\\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_FAIL_CLOSED.released-20261126T030311Z-pr858-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_03_RECEIPT_PERSISTENCE.taken-over-20261125T220442Z-owner-approved-p10-03.released-20261126T134840Z-pr858-merged\\nWP_P10_04_ACTIVE_CLIENT_ADMISSION.released-20261128T0744Z-pr934-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_04_ACTIVE_OPERATION_ADMISSION.released-20261127T-PROGRESS-PR889\\nWP_P10_04_AGGREGATE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.released-20261125T163335Z-pr829-merged\\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_OPERATION_ADMISSION.released-20261125T181901Z-pr830-merged\\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_OPERATION_ADMISSION_TEST_FIXTURE.released-20261125T181901Z-pr830-merged\\nWP_P10_04_CROSS_SESSION_LSP_ADMISSION.released-20261125T191442Z-pr831-merged\\nWP_P10_04_PLAN_STATUS.released-20261127T0345Z-pr890-postmerge-ci\\nWP_P10_04_SESSION_ARCHIVE_BOUND.released-20261128T011515Z-pr920-postmerge-ci\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","create_time":1795852624.1518066}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139566,"sampled_through_sequence":139562,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
