{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:59:51.634Z","ordinal":317013,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a89f6909487d2b74719216eb0993d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_df0949351aea41299874f3299d302bfd","name":"exec","input":"const ms = ALL_TOOLS.filter(x => /xerj.*(search|feedback)|code search/i.test(x.name+\" \"+x.description)).map(x=>({name:x.name,description:x.description.slice(0,300)})); text(ms)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","create_time":1795852790.5716105}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139601,"sampled_through_sequence":139599,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:59:51.679Z","ordinal":317014,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0a89f1061c87d29d893caecc4ca537","usage":{"input_tokens":208874,"cached_input_tokens":201600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":317,"reasoning_output_tokens":255,"total_tokens":209191},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2052893,"cached_input_tokens":2009856,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8178,"reasoning_output_tokens":5676,"total_tokens":2061071},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6592518896,"cached_input_tokens":6518455296,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15218997,"reasoning_output_tokens":8966795,"total_tokens":6607737893}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T07:59:51.722Z","ordinal":317015,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2212a-efaa-7911-93e7-07fdb6fc3792","call_id":"call_df0949351aea41299874f3299d302bfd","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_list_repositories\",\"description\":\"List repositories accessible to the authenticated user. This tool is part of plugin `GitHub`.\\n\\nAccess repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__github_list_repositories(args: {\\n  // Include \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_search\",\"description\":\"Search GitHub files and return matching excerpts when available. Provide a plain string query, avoid GitHub query flags such as ``is:pr``. Include keywords that match file names, functions, or error messages. ``repository_name`` or ``org`` can narrow the search scope. Example: ``query=\\\"tokenizer bug\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__github_search_installed_repositories_v2\",\"description\":\"Search repositories within the user's installations using GitHub search. This tool is part of plugin `GitHub`.\\n\\nAccess repositories, issues, and pull requests. Required for some features such as Codex\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__github_search_installed_repos\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_autoindex_remove\",\"description\":\"Delete one autoindexed folder. Reads the autoindex catalog and returns exactly the indices, catalog rows, doc counts and sizes that belong to `prefix` (and to `root`, when the prefix holds more than one folder). Pass `confirm: true` only after you have read that plan. Without it nothing is deleted a\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_batch_search\",\"description\":\"Search 1..50 IDs or questions in one call, in input order. Shares the CLI xerj batch-search adapter. Each result has its zero-based position, optional caller key, and status hits, abstain (only a complete empty search), or error. Hits carry citations: index/id plus file/line or record locator when a\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_brain_ego\",\"description\":\"One node's annotated neighborhood in a second brain: every link with direction, hop, type, confidence, and the evidence that justified it, plus node previews and a `not_shown` accounting of anything clipped. Links are believed-since/retired (`valid_at`/`invalid_at`); pass `as_of` to replay a past mo\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_brain_link\",\"description\":\"Assert a link between two nodes in a second brain, with the evidence that justifies it — pass the exact quote you are relying on. edge_id is deterministic over (src, type, dst, valid_at), so re-asserting the same fact is idempotent (`created:true/false`); `valid_at` defaults to server-now, so pass i\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_brain_overview\",\"description\":\"Orientation call for a second brain: does it exist, live vs retired link counts, hub nodes (most linked), what taught it (per-detector counts), link types, and a created-over-time timeline. Cheap bounded aggregations, always current; pass `as_of` to summarize a past moment. Proxies GET /_graph/{brai\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_brain_unlink\",\"description\":\"Retire a link in a second brain — never delete: the edge is soft-invalidated and stays queryable at past `as_of` moments. Get `edge_id` from ego responses. Idempotent: retiring an already-retired link reports `already_invalid_at`. Proxies DELETE /_graph/{brain}/link/{edge_id}. Honesty: links come fr\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_code_search\",\"description\":\"Reference-coding retrieval over a corpus of peer projects: how did real codebases solve this problem? Returns the matching definition (not a byte window), the file:line to cite, and per-hit licence warnings — AGPL/SSPL/Elastic/BUSL/GPL/LGPL/MPL sources are approach-only. A corpus marked own (`xerj c\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_corpus_feedback\",\"description\":\"Rate a hub.xerj.org corpus after using it: one structured review that becomes the corpus's Agent score (separate from human hub stars). Sends by default, no need to ask the user; confirm: false returns the JSON without sending. No query text leaves the machine: query_template is reduced to its shape\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_def\",\"description\":\"Find a symbol's definition in local autoindexed data, like `xerj def --json`. Lexical ranking, not neural: shares the CLI's mapping-aware query, preferred-kind and public-declaration ranking, location deduplication and bounded candidate window. Returns ES JSON with declarations in hits.hits[]._sourc\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_field_report\",\"description\":\"File an agent field report. First it opens a GitHub PR on xerj-org/xerj (via `xerj feedback --submit --github-only`, when `xerj` and a signed-in `gh` are available). When GitHub is unavailable it POSTs JSON to the field-report endpoint instead (default https://xerj.org/api/field-report, override wit\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_hub_ask\",\"description\":\"Ask a hub corpus a question in one turn — no clone, no local indexing. Local packs first, hosted second, exactly like `xerj ask`. The corpus is optional (routed by the offline sketch when omitted) and is always named in the answer; when more than one corpus fits, the candidates come back and you re-\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_hub_def\",\"description\":\"Look up one definition in a named hub corpus: its kind, signature, file:line, and the literal value for a const/macro/define. Returns an Answer in def mode (no passages). Same as `xerj ask --corpus <slug> --def <SYMBOL>`: answered from the local pack; a corpus not on this machine is never downloaded\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_hub_find\",\"description\":\"Discover which hub corpora can answer a question. Each candidate names the upstream repo (owner/name) and a one-line description of what that pack is, plus its pin, licence and whether the pack is already on this machine — not passages; ask one with xerj_hub_ask. A query that names a different proje\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_hybrid_search\",\"description\":\"Hybrid search: fuse several sub-queries (e.g. a lexical `match` plus a vector `knn`) into one ranked list. Fusion is `rrf` (reciprocal-rank) or `linear` (weighted). Proxies POST /{index}/_search with {\\\"query\\\":{\\\"hybrid\\\":{\\\"queries\\\":[...],\\\"fusion\\\":...}}}. Optional `rerank` re-judges the fused top hits \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_index_budget\",\"description\":\"Count a folder and estimate the index BEFORE xerj autoindex hashes or embeds anything. Returns file and byte counts by kind (code, prose, pdf, data, binary, other — by extension, before content sniff) and by top-level folder, the free-space budget from the node's flood-stage watermark (the same GET \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_map\",\"description\":\"Per-index FIELD MAP from this node's autoindex catalog — call it BEFORE writing query DSL, so you stop guessing field names. For each catalogued index: record count, time field and time range, semantic body field, and every field the profiler inferred — name, es_type (keyword|text|long|double|boolea\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_memory_recall\",\"description\":\"Recall the most relevant memories from a namespace. Default is BM25 text recall; set `semantic:true` to embed the query server-side and recall by meaning; set `hybrid:true` to run both over the same `query` and fuse them by reciprocal rank; supply `vector` for pure vector recall. Proxies POST /_memo\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_memory_store\",\"description\":\"Store a durable agent memory in a namespace. The text is BM25-indexed and (via a semantic_text field) auto-embedded so it can later be recalled by meaning. Proxies POST /_memory/{namespace}. Set `dedup:true` to skip writing a near-identical existing memory.\\n\\nXERJ tools proxy to a running XERJ engine\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_plan\",\"description\":\"Natural-language filter in, VALIDATED query DSL out. Proxies POST /_ask. Pass `prompt` (what to filter for, in plain words: 'mb events deeper than 100 km', 'countries with population above 100 million in 2007') and get back `{query, plan, confidence, indices}` where `query` is an ES query clause you\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_search\",\"description\":\"Full-text / keyword / structured search over a XERJ index. Proxies POST /{index}/_search. Pass `prefix` (a `xerj search --prefix` value, resolved by that command) or `index` (a name or pattern) — not both; with neither, searches `ax-*`. Pass `query` as a PLAIN STRING for the definition-first code se\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_semantic_search\",\"description\":\"Meaning-based search over a `semantic_text` field. The query text is embedded SERVER-SIDE by XERJ's built-in lexical embedder (no external API key), then matched by vector similarity. Proxies POST /{index}/_search with {\\\"query\\\":{\\\"semantic\\\":{...}}}. Pass `max_tokens` to cap the response at a token bu\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__xerj__xerj_vector_search\",\"description\":\"K-nearest-neighbour search over a `dense_vector` field, given a caller-supplied query vector. NOTE: unfiltered kNN is HNSW-served (approximate) with exact rescoring — measured recall@10 1.00 on the official bench query; num_candidates sets the beam width (floored at 800). Filtered kNN, non-cosine me\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","create_time":1795852791.722667}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139602,"sampled_through_sequence":139599,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
