   2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 15:59 BG1_DETACHED_RUNS\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 09:32 BG1_DETACHED_RUNS.handoff-20261124T1018Z-codex.released-20261126T151900Z-superseded-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 20:18 BG2_SCHEDULES.handoff-20261124T210105Z-claude-preserved.released-20261126T151900Z-superseded-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 21:01 BG2_SCHEDULES.released-20261125T144533Z-pr825-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 23:55 BG3_TRIGGER_FIRER.handoff-20261125T035556Z-owner-directed.released-20261126T151900Z-superseded-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 24 22:02 BG3_TRUST_ABUSE_MODEL\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 03:06 CI_SPEEDUP.claude-handoff-20261123T0306Z.released-20261124T024318Z-superseded\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 03:46 CI_SPEEDUP.codex-handoff-20261123T0830Z.released-20261124T043435Z-pr pr742-pr743\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 01:41 CI_SPEEDUP.cursor-handoff-20261123T0345Z.released-20261124T043435Z-pr pr742-pr743\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 15:49 CI_SPEEDUP.released-20261123-pr748-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 08:30 CI_SPEEDUP.released-20261123T143229Z-pr746-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 27 06:59 CLAUDE_BWRAP_MASKDIRS_MAIN_FORWARDPORT.released-20261127T072109Z-pr897-postmerge-ci\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 27 03:45 CLAUDE_BWRAP_MASK_DIRS.released-20261127T0409Z-pr891-postmerge-ci\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 04:18 CLAUDE_CHANGE_SCOPE.released-20261121-pr665-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 22 02:21 CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_SUNSET.released-20261122T025247Z\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 11:53 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.broken-20261121T120700Z.released-20261122T153022Z-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:10 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.claude-handoff-20261121T121000Z.released-20261122T153022Z-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:13 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.claude-handoff-20261121T121500Z.released-20261122T153022Z-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:21 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.claude-handoff-20261121T125844Z.released-20261122T153022Z-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:07 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.codex-handoff-20261121T120900Z.released-20261124T043435Z-pr pr671\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:13 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.codex-handoff-20261121T121100Z.released-20261124T043435Z-pr pr671\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:17 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.codex-handoff-20261121T122200Z.released-20261124T043435Z-pr pr671\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 12:58 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.released-20261121-pr671-merged\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 17:17 CS10_PHASE2_DOCKER.released-20261121T172330Z-duplicate-claude-pr679\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 03:55 CS10_SANDBOXED_WORKER.released-20261121T054852Z\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 03:38 CS10_WORKER_ISOLATION_DESIGN.released-20261121T045004Z\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 21 03:28 CS9_COMMAND_RULES.released-20261121T050125Z\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 22 19:12 CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.archived-20261128T-owner-approved\ndrwxrwxr-x    2 mike mike    4096 Nov 23 23:29 CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.reconciled-20261127T173326Z-owner-approved\ndocs/WP04_CORRECTION_VERIFICATION.md:176:- Removed claims of absolute zero tracking blind spots.\ndocs/GATEWAY_CONFORMANCE.md:11:- **Claim:** the job takes the `GATEWAY` claim (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/GATEWAY`, `NEXUS_CLAIMS_DIR` overrides) without waiting. If a human or another agent holds it, the run is **skipped** (exit 75, no alert). The claim is released, and one line logged, on every exit path.\ndocs/GATEWAY_CONFORMANCE.md:14:- **Exit codes:** 0 conformant, 1 not conformant or run failed (alert raised), 2 usage or setup error, 75 skipped (claim held).\ndocs/GATEWAY_CONFORMANCE.md:37:`SuccessExitStatus=75` keeps a skipped run (claim held) from showing as a failed unit.\ndocs/GATEWAY_CONFORMANCE.md:45:The claim protocol, the judgement, the alert path (forced failure, a failing alert command, a runner that produces nothing) and the stale-result rule are tested end to end through the script with a fake matrix runner (`cli/test/gateway_conformance.test.ts`, each behaviour mutation-checked). A live run has now been performed once; it failed the configured bar. One run does not establish repeatability or isolate gateway load, worker changes, or other causes.\ndocs/ISSUE12_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:77:| `EVID-002` | 16: Evidence & Provenance | WP-04 (INC-05) | Evidence records supporting negative security claims (e.g., \"no side effect occurred\", ... | `cli/src/core/spine.ts, cli/src/core/candidate.ts, cli/src/flight.ts` | cli/test/candidate.test.ts, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts | **DEMONSTRATED** | None |\ndocs/ISSUE12_REQUIREMENT_CLOSURE_MATRIX.md:84:| `EXEC-005` | 01: Common Execution-Spine | WP-01 (INC-02) | Model completion claims, TDD phase indicators, and discovered test executions MUST NOT ... | `cli/src/core/spine.ts` | cli/test/spine.test.ts, cli/test/system_journey.test.ts | **DEMONSTRATED** | None |\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:170:**Clarification on Implementer Claim:** The implementation report claimed *\"Zero tool invocations bypass ExecutionSpine\"*. While accurate for all autonomous agent tool turns (sequential, parallel, and subagents), standalone MCP server execution (`McpServer`) and internal test runner callbacks remain direct bridge invocations pending downstream work packages (`WP-08`).\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:186:- WP-01 does **not** overclaim candidate identity: no git tree hashes or cryptographic manifests are fabricated. Full candidate identity belongs to `WP-04`.\ndocs/WP01_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:255:- **F-WP01-02 (Minor): Overbroad bypass claim in implementation report.**\ndocs/WP05_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:103:### FINDING-WP05-QUAL-001 (MINOR) — DISC-005 Mode Verification Claim Correction\ndocs/WP05_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:105:- **Previous Claim:** Section 2 previously stated *\"Verified REVERSIBLE_TOKENIZATION, IRREVERSIBLE_REDACTION (destroys plaintext; tokens remain inert permanently), and ENCRYPTION.\"*\ndocs/WP05_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:106:- **Finding:** The independent qualification review established that `ProtectionMode.ENCRYPTION` in `cli/src/core/egress.ts:485-488` is a nominal simulation calling `generateToken()` without an operational cryptographic cipher transform, recipient key management, or demonstrated ciphertext transport. Claiming verification of `ENCRYPTION` was overstated.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:70:The qualification explicitly does not claim that every exception-display path or arbitrary stack trace was globally tested. CRED-003 is therefore `SATISFIED_WITH_BOUNDED_OPERATING_ENVELOPE`, not unqualified `DEMONSTRATED`. The prior `CRED-003-FLIGHTLOG` finding is **RESOLVED** by implementation HEAD `a285204cb83d08b6c6db7cb5e482064768479f54` and accepted qualification provenance commit `a4f3e16bbdd149faf7338421b9a8fe8437ffdbaa`.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:127:| `F-WP11-OBS-01`: secret scanning primarily covers tracked/staged files. | `ACCEPTED_BOUNDED_LIMITATION` | Does not contradict the bounded commit/release scan claims already accepted; retain the scanner boundary precisely. |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:132:| CRED-003 crash/stack-trace envelope. | `ACCEPTED_BOUNDED_LIMITATION` | No separate crash-report persistence writer was found; no universal exception-display claim is made. |\ndocs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md:57:This evidence establishes FlightRecorder and the directly named local audit append behavior. It does not claim that every application persistence subsystem is a logging or telemetry sink, nor does it change WP-05 trust ranks, token scoping, rehydration authority, or egress policy. No separate crash-report persistence writer was found in the examined paths; the Phase 2 acceptance criterion for bearer tokens/private keys in crash reports and stack traces remains a bounded limitation pending qualification of all exception-display paths.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:24:5. **Durable Candidate Identity & Milestone Recovery:** Boolean flags (`verifiedWorktreeCompletion`) are replaced with cryptographic candidate identity receipts covering tracked and relevant untracked candidate state (`CAND-001` .. `CAND-004`), and transcript-only session JSON files are upgraded to durable task recovery envelopes providing durable milestone task recovery with interrupted-state detection (`PERS-001` .. `PERS-004`) without overclaiming transparent resumption of in-flight operations.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:199:8. **`DurableStateManager`:** Persists complete task execution state (plan, worktree, receipts, routing, compaction provenance), enabling durable milestone task recovery and interrupted-state detection without overclaiming in-flight process continuation (`PERS-001` .. `PERS-004`, `F-07`).\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:636:- **Acceptance Properties:** Restarting after crash recovers active plan milestones, worktree binding, candidate identity, and durable summaries; stale validation dependencies detected; ephemeral process handles are safely re-initialized; unresolved in-flight operations are detected as interrupted without false completion claims.\ndocs/PHASE3_IMPLEMENTATION_DECOMPOSITION.md:769:  - Unresolved in-flight effects: Interrupted operations are detected as interrupted without false completion claims.\ndocs/v1.3.1/HIR_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:18:| [arXiv:2610.14224](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.14224), *Harness^2: Recursive Agent Harnessing for an Open World* | Task-level Propose-Probe-Compose with behavioral contrast; harnessing-level reflection/library. | Inspiration for candidate/probe/compose/reflect separation. | High for abstract claims; not independently reproduced. |\ndocs/v1.3.1/HIR_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:22:Unverified/excluded: \"10x better\" marketing claim.\ndocs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md:3:Status: **DRAFT PLAN** (2026-11-25), authored on `v1/v131-plan` from `origin/main` (`e578571b`). This plan is execution guidance, not a release claim. No merge/tag/publish performed.\ndocs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md:172:- Context maturity merged in PR #871 as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`; exact-head and post-merge CI and CodeQL passed. Its focused results and remaining limits are recorded in `docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`. Later release CI runs found shard assertion failures that this branch updates. The base then advanced to `493b78bd0752b6696cb2109d1d0772dd88d80426`, where `core/Cargo.toml` and `core/Cargo.lock` drifted to `1.3.1` while root `package.json` remained the canonical `1.3.0`; this branch runs `scripts/sync-version.mjs` to restore consistency. Manual CI run `45839612643` passed on the earlier PR head, but a fresh pull-request run against the current base is required. The `1.3.1` version-only bump remains in the release process after qualification.\ndocs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md:186:Parallelism is allowed across independent WPs with worktree/claim discipline and per-subsystem merge serialization.\ndocs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md:198:| G-7 | Release notes measured; no frontier-grade claim; external qualification reported as measured/pending. |\ndocs/INVARIANTS.md:3:Baseline: `origin/main` at `c8e986f4f02da37b35a1c26e46f31daf16a506c2` (2026-11-21). This file maps selected, source-backed controls to their enforcement code, relevant tests, and provenance. The checker verifies that referenced files exist and that rule IDs used in code or tests have a row; the listed test files are evidence pointers, not a claim that each test has been executed for this revision. It replaces no other document: `docs/EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md` describes the spine, and `docs/v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md` describes acceptance gates.\ndocs/INVARIANTS.md:52:- **No document claims a tamper-evident audit log (checked 2026-11-17).** The \"immutable\" wording in `docs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md` is about candidate and invocation identities, which the code keeps stable; it is not a claim of a hash-chained log. Nexus does not have one, and none of its documents should be read as promising it.\ndocs/INVARIANTS.md:59:| No live model benchmark is included in this repository revision, so the behavioral effect of reviewer or prompt changes is not established by the deterministic tests. | Scripted scenarios exercise the gates with known inputs; they do not measure autonomous-model behavior. | Make no live-effect claim. Any future comparison is optional, uses only no-cost local or donated capacity, and is never a v1.2.x or publication prerequisite. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:68:  - **F-11 (Verifiable Negative Claims):** Required boundary-defined evidence for negative assertions.\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:106:| **EXEC-005** | Model completion claims, TDD phase indicators, and discovered test executions MUST NOT confer merge authority. Merge authority MUST require an explicit passing result from an authoritative verifier executed against the exact validated candidate. | When an authoritative verifier is configured, `task_completed` calls without passing verification receipts MUST fail closed and keep merge eligibility denied. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:143:| **CAP-003** | Capability availability MUST remain distinct from invocation admission. If an operation is available in the runtime but not permitted for a concrete invocation, the invocation MUST be denied under the canonical capability identity with an explicit scope reason. | Invocation denial MUST report `{ capability: \"linux_file_write\", status: \"DENIED\", reason: \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\" }` rather than claiming the capability does not exist. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:188:| **AUTH-011** | Independent execution domains (MCP servers, plugins, evaluators) MUST declare their authority relationship and isolation boundaries. The core runtime MUST NOT assume or claim enforcement over boundaries it does not control. | External MCP servers running across network sockets MUST declare their own security boundary. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:509:| **EVID-001** | Evidence records MUST be objective, attributable, and bound to a defined observation and enforcement boundary. The system MUST NOT claim universal proof from a single log entry, Git status check, or single scanner result. | Claims of compliance MUST define the exact envelope of observation (e.g., \"Verified within the worktree filesystem boundary\"). |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:510:| **EVID-002** | Evidence records supporting negative security claims (e.g., \"no side effect occurred\", \"no plaintext crossed boundary\", \"authority did not expand\") MUST define the specific observed boundary and inspection mechanism that makes the claim meaningful. | A negative claim that an unauthorized tool produced no filesystem modification MUST be backed by an observable filesystem or worktree state check. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:783:| **F-11** | Negative security claims unverifiable in evidence records (Plausible) | **EVID-001, EVID-002** | Fully resolved. Boundary-defined evidence required for negative claims. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:793:| **IR-04** | `RES-003` claimed absolute \"TOCTOU immunity\"; `RES-004` relied on pre-check lexical canonicalization. | **RES-003, RES-004** | ACCEPTED WITH REFINEMENT. Removed absolute TOCTOU claims and openat/effect-time syscall mandates; reframed as race-resistant resource authority enforcement failing safely before unauthorized effect. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:846:    - `RES-003..004`: Removed absolute TOCTOU immunity claims and pre-check lexical assumptions; mandated race-resistant resource authority enforcement failing safely before unauthorized effect.\ndocs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:27:Mandatory SHA policy remains off while the default branch still contains mutable references. This PR's pins must reach main before enabling it. Release-environment restrictions and release-asset immutability are not claimed applied; they require a coordinated lifecycle check with the publisher. Required CI and review of this PR remain pending independently of the applied settings. CodeQL and Dependabot configuration checks on the original PR head passed; that is not full product qualification.\ndocs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:68:- Record unresolved access/feature limits and avoid claiming a security score or full maturity from template presence.\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:Claim each slice before editing, use a dedicated worktree branched from the current `origin/release/v1.3.1`, and take short hot-file claims where required. Serialize changes to the operation schema and runner, and separately serialize shared REPL, sidecar and export edits. Review any cross-slice file needs before editing. Merge updated release content into a pushed slice. Follow the repository's XERJ procedure before non-trivial peer-analogous implementation and record take/borrow/reject or the documented fallback in each PR. This draft contains no peer-project code.\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:65:1. Add opt-in extraction after terminal work or on an explicit operator request. A bounded no-tool call proposes conventions, architecture, dependency facts, troubleshooting findings or rules from selected records. Keep model suggestions in private candidate storage. Review compares evidence, source class and conflicting claims. Record conflicts and uncertainty explicitly. Suggestions do not alter prompt context or authorization.\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:67:3. Bind repository/workspace/worktree scope and relevant paths to session, operation, unit, candidate/commit and evidence IDs as available. Preserve explicit source classes for operator, model, tool and verified evidence, creation/update time, validation status, freshness, invalidation predicates, retention and content/evidence digests. Resolve references through operator-accessible saved records, apply redaction before persistence and export, and make secret-bearing, personal or protected content ineligible for promotion. Recheck redaction and references at promotion. Missing provenance defaults to rejection or review-only unverified under explicit policy. An evidence reference does not verify the extracted claim.\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:87:| CF-B knowledge and context | Extend `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` and existing context/export coverage. Exercise migration, redaction, promotion authority, replay, conflicts, missing provenance and cross-worktree/repository boundaries. | False claim, stale convention, secret-bearing output, conflict, expiry and rejection. Zero unauthorized promotions or scope leaks in deterministic cases. |\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:91:Add development fixtures through the existing `eval/tasks` or dataset/task machinery where its task contract fits, and operation-specific fault cases through existing restart and provider-neutral fixture infrastructure. Freeze tasks, adjudication rules, sample sizes and comparison thresholds before comparative runs. Compare the pinned baseline and candidate with the same task inputs, resources and budgets. Record acceptance accuracy, verified completions per attempt, false completions per reported completion, regressions, correctly recovered fault cases per injected fault, and complete evidence per required record. Publish raw counts, denominators and missing/unknown outcomes. Report latency and tokens as diagnostics. Label unmeasured metrics explicitly. Preserve WP-131-11 corpus custody and scoring. Deterministic fixtures govern the release gate. Use optional approved local/live runs only with suitable existing access, required claims and no paid-infrastructure assumption. Claims of improved outcomes require comparative evidence.\ndocs/v1.3.1/CLAUDE_FEATURES_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:95:- For each TypeScript slice run `npm --prefix cli run build` and affected tests. For a focused test, run `cd cli && HOME=$(mktemp -d) node --import tsx --test test/<name>.test.ts`. Use a throwaway home and matching XDG paths for test and probe runs. Use Node 22 and 24 for process/runner changes. Build Rust with an isolated target directory when affected. Use a snapshot and the `SUITE` claim for full test runs. Take `GATEWAY` before any inference run. Keep secrets out of artifacts and retain failed run records.\ndocs/STATE_COMPATIBILITY.md:66:Task and session stores use a permanent private `.nexus-state.guard` inode with kernel `flock` ownership. Linux requires `/usr/bin/flock` (util-linux); missing or unsafe lock support fails closed. State transactions wait at most two seconds for another writer, while background retention skips busy stores. Writers, readers, retention and upgrade snapshots must use the same guard. Kernel ownership ends on process death; Nexus never deletes the inode to reclaim it. Rollback preserves guard inodes even when an older backup did not contain that directory.\ndocs/PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md:472:- **Undesirable Outcome:** Unverifiable claims of security boundaries; audit logs cannot prove non-occurrence of events.\ndocs/WP02_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:221:- **OBS-02:** `cargo clippy` emits 21 compiler warnings (collapsible `if` statements, manual flatten). Most predate WP-02, but one in `runner.rs:288` was added. The implementer's report claimed `cargo clippy = clean`; clippy is static linting, not vulnerability scanning.\ndocs/WORKTREES.md:129:  guard (`worktrees.lock.reclaim`, an `flock` that Nexus never deletes), and the lock is judged again under it and deleted\ndocs/WORKTREES.md:130:  only if it is still the same file, so two waiters cannot both reclaim it and a lock another process has just taken is\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:48:4. **Dependency Rigor:** Challenging the directed acyclic graph (DAG), critical path, and parallelization claims for technical validity, hidden surface overlap, and missing edges.\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:143:The critical path claimed in Phase 4 is:\ndocs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md:154:The parallelization claims in Phase 4 were independently audited for potential surface overlaps:\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:213:| `F-WP07-OBS-01` | `OBSERVATION` | **SUPERSEDED** | Historical report overstated fsync durability claims. Atomic rename (`.tmp` -> target) provides atomic persistence on POSIX filesystems. |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:219:## 12. Contradicted or Unsupported Prior Claims\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:221:1. **Phase 1 Claim on SecretsVault Boundary:**\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:222:   - *Claim:* `cli/src/security.ts` `SecretsVault` provides an operational secrets quarantine boundary.\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:224:2. **Critical Path Equivalence Claim:**\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_CLOSURE_ASSESSMENT.md:225:   - *Claim:* Acceptance of the final critical-path package (`WP-11`) constitutes full normative closure of Issue #12.\ndocs/CRED003_INDEPENDENT_QUALIFICATION.md:55:- **OBSERVATION:** No separate crash-report persistence writer was found in the reviewed `cli/src` paths. Exception-display paths were not independently qualified as a global guarantee for every crash report or stack trace; the reviewer bounded its verified disposition to the authorized FlightRecorder and audit persistence operating envelope. Do not interpret this CRED-003 qualification as a claim that every exception-display path was tested.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOCTOR_RECOVERED_REQUEST.md:121:Finish with a concise report explaining what changed, what was tested, which repairs are supported, and any remaining limitations. Do not claim checks passed unless you ran them.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:321:- Under pressure the memory shows each finding condensed (the start of every claim), then indexed (what it mentions),\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:331:- shortened legacy copies are never claimed recoverable;\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:364:  - F-3 claims the findings budget grows with the context limit, but it is capped by `Math.min(1, …)`.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_MULTILINE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-04.md:46:Disposition **BOUNDED**: Phase 3 enables bracketed paste and relies on it for multiline paste. On terminals that do not provide it, multiline paste is unsupported, and the TUI does not claim otherwise. Making it reliable would need paste-burst heuristics, which are out of Phase 3 scope.\ndocs/AUDIT.md:75:  evidence/provenance.json             each requirement's evidence and who produced it (a tool, or the model's claim)\ndocs/AUDIT.md:118:Everything left out is in the manifest's `omitted` and in the command's output, with the reason. A bundle never claims to hold what it does not.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:144:  `ApplicationCore`, despite the comment claiming projection of the shared model.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:325:| C-2 | README overclaims (\"comparable to Codex/Claude Code\", \"state-aware\", persisted history, \"live\" TUI) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_DOGFOODING_READINESS_REVIEW_2026-10-03.md:343:| Claim | Command / driver | Observed |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md:11:| Context-length degradation <=49k | Not demonstrated (b0, 30 trials/size, 0.93-1.00, no trend); not a general claim |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_MATURITY_FIXES_2026-10-11_REQUEST.md:58:Investigate the recorded 2,506,632 prompt tokens versus 17,038 completion tokens. Establish whether totals are correct cumulative provider usage, estimates, retries, or double counting. Trace repeated context reconstruction and oversized retained notes. Preserve the objective, requirements, steering and evidence references while reducing redundant history. Report measured findings; do not claim cost or completion-rate improvements without evidence.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:29:context at *any* step, including step 1. This run is **not evidence for H3/H9-style claims about objective retention**. (UNRESOLVED: that the operator pasted\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:24:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md:54:All fixtures are generated programmatically from a seed so facts, distractors and positions are randomised; each ships with machine-checkable ground truth (`required_facts`, `forbidden_claims`, `expected_label_per_item`).\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md:62:| D | Contradictory scopes | two observations with different conditions (e.g. \"passes on linux/py3.12\", \"fails on py3.9\") | both survive with scopes; no merged claim; `forbidden_claims` list catches flattening |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md:74:Task success and validation success (Layer 3: verifier-backed `VERIFIED` per the existing contract). Objective retention (exact-match of pinned text in packet; adherence by blind rubric). Required-fact recall = |required ∩ packet∪retrieved| / |required| per decision. Irrelevant-context precision = |packet ∩ relevant| / |packet| by token. Stale-evidence rejection rate; **false-current claims** (count; target 0). Provenance preservation (every packet item has ref+scope+gatheredAt). Epistemic-status preservation (label equality). Tokens per inference, cumulative input tokens, peak context (server `usage` where the gateway forwards it; else the estimator **and** a calibration run against server counts). TTFT and inference latency from the gateway (metrics endpoint/aihost exporter, read-only). Redundancy ratio = duplicate-token share. Raw-result residency = tokens of raw results alive in the packet. Retrieval frequency, retrieval success, insufficiency recoveries. Hallucinations attributable to missing context (rubric on fixture H and on any wrong decision whose required fact was excluded). Compaction/reconstruction frequency; continuation success after restart; task duration; output quality (blind rubric, ≥2 raters or rubric + automated checks).\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_PARALLEL_DEFECT_INVESTIGATION_2026-10-04.md:88:**Acceptance:** 1-6 pass; documented recovery actions each behave as claimed (a test per action); no change to admission arithmetic.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:6:**Scope:** Read-only assessment of the current checkout, focused on remaining gaps to dependable application maturity. This is a prioritized review, not a claim of production certification.  \ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:27:`scripts/generate_sbom.sh` constructs dependency inventory from direct `cli/package.json` dependencies and parses direct Rust dependencies from `Cargo.toml` (lines 32–94). It does not derive a complete transitive inventory from lockfiles in this implementation. Its own header calls the output CycloneDX-compatible, but compatibility claims need validation against a schema/tool. `README.md` presents broad product capability claims, while `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` contains specific architecture assertions (e.g. permanent audit log) that need to be checked against current runtime behavior rather than treated as proof.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:80:6. Reconcile README and architecture claims against shipped binaries and supported workflows.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.15.md:22:The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\ndocs/WP10_INDEPENDENT_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md:109:- **Vector:** A task interrupted mid-execution or corrupted on disk is recovered into `ApplicationCore` and claimed completed.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:18:  2. **Summarize** (`processCompaction`): a dedicated `compaction` agent (own model configurable) produces a Markdown summary in a fixed template — `Objective / Important Details / Work State {Completed, Active, Blocked} / Next Move / Relevant Files` (`packages/core/src/session/compaction.ts`). When a prior summary exists it is passed as `<prior-summary>` with rules to carry forward objectives, constraints, directives and to let newer conversation override older claims, and it states the prior summary is *discarded afterwards*.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:89:Source reading only; no behavioural verification of any project. Issue titles are upstream claims, not confirmed defects. Cline's SDK repository was restructured recently; earlier Cline versions (I recall a `ContextManager` with file-read de-duplication and quartile truncation; recalled from memory, not inspected or verified here) were not examined.\ndocs/evidence/VR3_SANDBOX_DENIALS.md:3:Branch: `v1/vr-3-sandbox-denials` (from `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `10942d41`). Slice claim: `VR-3`.\ndocs/evidence/VR3_SANDBOX_DENIALS.md:25:- `xerj feedback --dry-run` inspected. No field report was submitted: the earlier publication blocker (missing GitHub credential) still applies, and no submission is claimed here.\ndocs/evidence/VR3_SANDBOX_DENIALS.md:37:- `worker_isolation` is not claimed as a gate in this slice. With no built core, one subtest failed with `Core engine handshake failed: Rust core RPC daemon disconnected`; after building the core, that suite hung in a real bwrap/core RPC case on this host and was stopped by its own pids. No result is inferred from it.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:15:separate agent with no implementation context (`tui.md`); its result overturned one self-assessed claim (approval\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:87:| Q3 | Preserves operator intent and evidence through long tasks | constraints and facts introduced early are honoured/retained after compaction, resume and continuation; no false absence claims |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:102:| Q3 intent & evidence | **PARTIAL** | pinned objective ledger never compacted; operator-only descoping (verified); context branch keeps findings in full with ids (31d6622) | steering beyond last 10/600 chars dropped after compaction (CTX-02, both branches); crash loses mid-turn findings and ids collide (CTX-01, branch); harness prompts treated as operator text (CTX-06); archive not retrievable by the model; false absence claim in d88a897 review (`context.md`) |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:130:- Benchmark figures found are vendor claims about models under other harnesses; none establishes harness parity.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:159:(cut to fit a 24K budget; a later `| head -20` re-check missed `cli/src/tools.ts`) and the review falsely claimed no\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:242:frequency, memory/CPU of long sessions (TUI frame cost measured: 1.1–1.6 ms). Claims of efficiency are unsupported.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:255:### 7.1 Acceptance blockers (must close before any top-tier claim)\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:302:| 7 | R6 context fixes on main; R7 rebase and accept fix/context-convergence | 3, 5 | CTX exit criteria met; long-task evaluation tier (§9 T3) with fact checks: 0 false absence claims, steering honoured after compaction |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:306:Top-tier qualification may be claimed only after Stage 8 meets its thresholds and an independent reviewer (not the\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:324:| T3 Long-task | 4 tasks needing >60 steps with an early operator constraint and mid-task steering; 2 read-only analyses scored against a fact sheet (absence claims checked) | context retention, intent, false-absence rate |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":55875451}},"started_at_ms":1795853047549,"completed_at_ms":1795853047606}}
