{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T08:04:13.653Z","ordinal":317155,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-999e7a6a-afc1-4b7e-a78a-16c92f71dd3a","process_id":"84909","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find .git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.archived-20261128T-owner-approved .git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.reconciled-20261127T173326Z-owner-approved -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p\\n'; git status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery diff --check 2>/dev/null; sed -n '155,195p' docs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find .git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.archived-20261128T-owner-approved .git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.reconciled-20261127T173326Z-owner-approved -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p\\n'; git status --short --branch; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery diff --check 2>/dev/null; sed -n '155,195p' docs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":".git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.archived-20261128T-owner-approved/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.reconciled-20261127T173326Z-owner-approved/owner.json\n## release/v1.3.1\n## codex/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery...origin/release/v1.3.1\n M cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts\n\n**Scope:**\n- Define publishable package name/scope, license confirmation, README/install docs, semver/release workflow.\n- Remove `private: true` / prepublishOnly block only when publish is authorized and package contents are correct.\n- Add `files`/`.npmignore`/export map validation, provenance/SBOM/signing as appropriate.\n- Update release workflow for stable npm publish (owner-gated) while preserving RC/stable GitHub release flow.\n- Ensure CLI binary/core packaging model is clear (npm package may ship JS/TS dist + launcher; Rust core handling documented).\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- Dry-run publish passes; package contents audited.\n- Release process docs updated.\n- Owner authorization required before first real publish/tag.\n\n### WP-131-11 — Backlog closure and qualification\n\n**Scope:**\n- #1 PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal held-out T2/T3 corpus, or close/supersede with measured evidence.\n- Context maturity merged in PR #871 as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`; exact-head and post-merge CI and CodeQL passed. Its focused results and remaining limits are recorded in `docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`. Later release CI runs found shard assertion failures that this branch updates. The base then advanced to `493b78bd0752b6696cb2109d1d0772dd88d80426`, where `core/Cargo.toml` and `core/Cargo.lock` drifted to `1.3.1` while root `package.json` remained the canonical `1.3.0`; this branch runs `scripts/sync-version.mjs` to restore consistency. Manual CI run `45839612643` passed on the earlier PR head, but a fresh pull-request run against the current base is required. The `1.3.1` version-only bump remains in the release process after qualification.\n- G-1–G-7 re-evaluated for v1.3.1; release notes/readiness updated with measured status.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- #1 closed with evidence.\n- v1.3.1 readiness doc has no silent TBD for in-scope items.\n\n## 5. Sequencing\n\n1. **Foundation/safety first:** WP-131-08, WP-131-09, WP-131-01 (security + required PA-3 bug).\n2. **Platform correctness:** WP-131-02, WP-131-06, WP-131-03.\n3. **Feature completion:** WP-131-04, WP-131-05, WP-131-07.\n4. **Release packaging:** WP-131-10, WP-131-11.\n\nParallelism is allowed across independent WPs with worktree/claim discipline and per-subsystem merge serialization.\n\n## 6. Release gates (v1.3.1)\n\n| Gate | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| G-1 | `make test` green at exact head; required CI green; release-branch CI green after each merge. |\n| G-2 | Protocol/schema/ACP conformance green; no undocumented protocol drift. |\n| G-3 | Hostile gate-bypass suite green across client/hook/plugin/schedule/trigger/socket/policy surfaces; no allow-always/bypass/regression. |\n| G-4 | Unattended runs: no allow-always, fresh worktree, unattended flag in receipts, kill-and-resume pass; stale-driver pause cannot be silently overridden (#807). |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":70643253}},"started_at_ms":1795853053582,"completed_at_ms":1795853053653}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T08:04:13.696Z","ordinal":317156,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2212e-ef00-72f0-9637-e2f6aca9759a","call_id":"call_173f716719c140e59104fbd8e299484a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":".git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.archived-20261128T-owner-approved/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM.reconciled-20261127T173326Z-owner-approved/owner.json\n## release/v1.3.1\n## codex/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery...origin/release/v1.3.1\n M cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts\n\n**Scope:**\n- Define publishable package name/scope, license confirmation, README/install docs, semver/release workflow.\n- Remove `private: true` / prepublishOnly block only when publish is authorized and package contents are correct.\n- Add `files`/`.npmignore`/export map validation, provenance/SBOM/signing as appropriate.\n- Update release workflow for stable npm publish (owner-gated) while preserving RC/stable GitHub release flow.\n- Ensure CLI binary/core packaging model is clear (npm package may ship JS/TS dist + launcher; Rust core handling documented).\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- Dry-run publish passes; package contents audited.\n- Release process docs updated.\n- Owner authorization required before first real publish/tag.\n\n### WP-131-11 — Backlog closure and qualification\n\n**Scope:**\n- #1 PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal held-out T2/T3 corpus, or close/supersede with measured evidence.\n- Context maturity merged in PR #871 as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`; exact-head and post-merge CI and CodeQL passed. Its focused results and remaining limits are recorded in `docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`. Later release CI runs found shard assertion failures that this branch updates. The base then advanced to `493b78bd0752b6696cb2109d1d0772dd88d80426`, where `core/Cargo.toml` and `core/Cargo.lock` drifted to `1.3.1` while root `package.json` remained the canonical `1.3.0`; this branch runs `scripts/sync-version.mjs` to restore consistency. Manual CI run `45839612643` passed on the earlier PR head, but a fresh pull-request run against the current base is required. The `1.3.1` version-only bump remains in the release process after qualification.\n- G-1–G-7 re-evaluated for v1.3.1; release notes/readiness updated with measured status.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- #1 closed with evidence.\n- v1.3.1 readiness doc has no silent TBD for in-scope items.\n\n## 5. Sequencing\n\n1. **Foundation/safety first:** WP-131-08, WP-131-09, WP-131-01 (security + required PA-3 bug).\n2. **Platform correctness:** WP-131-02, WP-131-06, WP-131-03.\n3. **Feature completion:** WP-131-04, WP-131-05, WP-131-07.\n4. **Release packaging:** WP-131-10, WP-131-11.\n\nParallelism is allowed across independent WPs with worktree/claim discipline and per-subsystem merge serialization.\n\n## 6. Release gates (v1.3.1)\n\n| Gate | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| G-1 | `make test` green at exact head; required CI green; release-branch CI green after each merge. |\n| G-2 | Protocol/schema/ACP conformance green; no undocumented protocol drift. |\n| G-3 | Hostile gate-bypass suite green across client/hook/plugin/schedule/trigger/socket/policy surfaces; no allow-always/bypass/regression. |\n| G-4 | Unattended runs: no allow-always, fresh worktree, unattended flag in receipts, kill-and-resume pass; stale-driver pause cannot be silently overridden (#807). |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","create_time":1795853053.6965296}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139668,"sampled_through_sequence":139665,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
