"pid\":11247,\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130\",\"scope\":\"Context maturity system implementation, release rebase, exact-head qualification, and evidence.\"}\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:5:PR #871 head `3a486c574ea5d35c85a942e9aa53e61dd606f286` was merged as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`. Exact-head CI (`45828988591`) and CodeQL (`45828988502`) passed; post-merge CI (`45830919705`) and CodeQL (`45830919665`) also passed on the merge commit. PR #911's paperwork update merged as `2c300c9ece1b0ef85744dfaff048e8a204d0a6c7`; its post-merge CI (`46036074224`) and CodeQL (`46036074556`) passed on that merge head. Later release heads `b9f272f`, `64e072b`, and `0977932` passed full hosted CI (runs `46026791001`, `46028099235`, and `46031422051`) and their CodeQL runs passed. The follow-up wording correction in PR #930 (head `9785b8efd3ccfad77c4e077ac14f4a7964b33e1a`) merged as `007c9fc892568e9a1375662caee0db13a800b102`; its exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI (`46102061647`) and CodeQL (`46102061586`) passed on the merge commit. The advisory Entire check was neutral and was not a required gate. The plan's G-1 also names `make test` at the exact head; that command was not run for `0977932`, so this report does not mark that additional gate complete. The earlier v1.3.0 measurements below are historical and are not v1.3.1 qualification evidence.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:29:The first hosted full-suite run on PR #871 was not green. It exposed stale assertions for operator-only knowledge promotion and two fingerprint tests affected by inherited system Git configuration. The fixes were included before PR #871 merged. The final PR head passed CI run `45828988591`, and merge commit `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f` passed post-merge CI run `45830919705`. Targeted reruns after correction also passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 20/20, `turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts` 46/46, and the model-tool/dispatch characterization pair 23/23. No live inference or external task-quality qualification is claimed.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:46:The current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:69:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements.\ndocs/v1.3.1/PLAN.md:172:- Context maturity merged in PR #871 as `8560af8165f7c1ceb1fcc9e309ce0d0c8a77c35f`; exact-head and post-merge CI and CodeQL passed. Its focused results and remaining limits are recorded in `docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`. Later release CI runs found shard assertion failures that this branch updates. The base then advanced to `493b78bd0752b6696cb2109d1d0772dd88d80426`, where `core/Cargo.toml` and `core/Cargo.lock` drifted to `1.3.1` while root `package.json` remained the canonical `1.3.0`; this branch runs `scripts/sync-version.mjs` to restore consistency. Manual CI run `45839612643` passed on the earlier PR head, but a fresh pull-request run against the current base is required. The `1.3.1` version-only bump remains in the release process after qualification.\n.git/nexus-claims.log:8841:2026-11-23T02:05:59Z BROKEN_STALE_CLAIM FILE_docs_v1.3.0_PL