{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T08:10:03.262Z","ordinal":317470,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0a8c532cc487d2acc22dde8e01e662","status":"completed","call_id":"call_52f24a20b0ff4b129db1f6cb76e1615a","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"body_file=$(mktemp); cat > \\\"$body_file\\\" <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Add a deterministic process-crash test for `write_file` after the filesystem mutation returns but before the operation-end journal record is persisted.\\n- Verify recovery marks the in-flight operation as interrupted/unknown and does not repeat the file write.\\n- Forward the isolated `NEXUS_CORE_BIN` path to child processes in the existing crash tests so they work with worktree-local Rust builds.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/nexus-p10-02-target cargo build --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml` — passed.\\n- `HOME=<temporary> XDG_CONFIG_HOME=<temporary> NEXUS_CORE_BIN=/tmp/nexus-p10-02-target/release/harness-core node --import tsx --test test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` — 3/3 passed.\\n- `npm run typecheck` — passed.\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\nQueried XERJ's `opencode` corpus for durable recovery ordering. The comparison at `opencode/packages/core/src/session/execution/restart.ts:37` informed the focus on establishing recovery state before resumed execution. This change reuses Nexus's operation journal and recovery path; no code was copied. The corpus reported incomplete indexing, so this comparison is limited.\\n\\n## Limits\\n\\nThis is local fake-gateway evidence for one filesystem side-effect crash boundary. It does not establish host-loss durability, all side-effect classes, or provider-enforced token bounds.\\nEOF\\ngh pr create --base release/v1.3.1 --head codex/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery --title \\\"test: cover crash after file side effect\\\" --body-file \\\"$body_file\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-side-effect-crash-recovery\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:3000}); text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22128-3667-7142-a098-5707fbe8c197","create_time":1795853395.1788843}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":139816,"sampled_through_sequence":139814,"client_authored":false}}
