{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T08:52:20.407Z","ordinal":318378,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0a96429ed087d2a5efd023c1a47e0d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The next P10-02 recovery gap I can strengthen locally is a second mutating path: `edit_file` goes through the Rust file-operation handler, while the new `write_file` case already exercises another handler. I’m setting up an isolated worktree and will add the same “effect completed, operation-end persistence interrupted” recovery check for `edit_file`. This will extend side-effect coverage without claiming host-loss coverage."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":86,"started_at_ms":1795855938651,"completed_at_ms":1795855940407}}
