{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T09:36:08.771Z","ordinal":319477,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0aa086281887d2b3dd33e8dc6fdf4c","usage":{"input_tokens":99949,"cached_input_tokens":97792,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":107,"reasoning_output_tokens":10,"total_tokens":100056},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":35355796,"cached_input_tokens":34961024,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":49025,"reasoning_output_tokens":20591,"total_tokens":35404821},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6641426960,"cached_input_tokens":6566786816,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15294872,"reasoning_output_tokens":8999144,"total_tokens":6656721832}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T09:36:10.307Z","ordinal":319478,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b6d4d436-f554-421d-9ef3-3a5e46e6080e","process_id":"12121","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"post-merge|file-side-effect|write_file|PR #937|PR #938\" docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-file-crash-evidence","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'post-merge|file-side-effect|write_file|PR #937|PR #938' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","query":"post-merge|file-side-effect|write_file|PR #937|PR #938","path":"POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"51:**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This is not yet a ceiling on all model requests: context-findings extraction and LLM compaction summary/requirement-probe calls do not reserve from it, nor do delegated `spawn_subagent` requests or durable operation work units. Without durable objective state, the counter comes from `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` and resets per turn. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` may be selected in a project `.env` up to 10,000; on resume, an existing saved ceiling can only be lowered. Availability probes are excluded. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope: include all side and delegated requests in a shared durable pre-dispatch counter; account for durable operation units, tokens and cumulative elapsed limits; add per-tool deadlines and process-crash reconciliation.\n55:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #762):** `runTurnImpl` arms a timer for the active turn's `maxTurnMinutes` deadline and requests cancellation while inference or a tool is still awaiting completion. Expiry returns `LIMIT_REACHED` / `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; the timer is cleared on normal completion and caught failure. Tests cover aborting slow streamed inference, stopping a running shell command before its later side effect, and clearing the timer after a normal turn. Exact-head CI passed on PR #762 (`45293148069`); post-merge CI passed at `6b916195d57ddd4b641214ea3e835f10eb722a28` (`45294542653`). This bounded one active direct turn; PR #774 later added cumulative elapsed accounting across resumes of that durable objective. A separate per-tool deadline is still absent. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope includes shared durable accounting for side/delegated model requests and durable operation units, operation-wide elapsed limits, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation.\n59:**Progress (2026-11-25, implementation in progress):** The durable operation runner now has a finite aggregate active wall-time cap (default and hard maximum 4,320 minutes) shared across concurrently executing units. Each active interval is recorded in the operation record; an open interval is charged on recovery, and migrated records conservatively use record age because earlier active time cannot be reconstructed. Expiry aborts the current operation signal, pauses the operation, and records interrupted side effects as unknown so resume cannot silently replay them. The existing `nexus operation budget` command now audits token and active-time cap changes together, and operation status/JSON reports elapsed, remaining, and uncertain legacy history. The implementation deliberately measures the operation driver's wall interval, not the sum of worker CPU time or time spent parked between runs. Focused evidence on the current branch: `p10_operation_active_budget.test.ts` (5/5), `goal_pa3_completion.test.ts` (8/8), `operation_runner_refactor.test.ts` (3/3), `operation_schema.test.ts` (19/19), `operation_view.test.ts` (35/35), and `npm run build` passed. This remains one tranche, not complete WP-P10-02: side/delegated inference requests, token accounting across all operation work, per-tool deadlines, process crash during arbitrary side effects, and durable unknown-outcome reconciliation beyond the in-flight budget-expiry boundary remain open. Exact-head hosted checks and post-merge CI have not yet run for this change.\n61:**Progress (2026-11-26, RPC worker timeout tranche, merged PR #862):** Generic Rust RPC deadlines and cancellation now retire the worker process rather than only ending the bridge wait. A retiring worker accepts no new dispatch; sibling in-flight calls resolve as outcome unknown; stdin EOF requests the Rust worker's normal cleanup; and a bounded grace period ends a worker that does not exit. Command cancellation retains its runner confirmation window before retirement. Focused evidence: `rpc_worker_timeout.test.ts` covers unanswered RPC, sibling unknown outcomes, cancellation, bounded forced exit, and a blocked real Rust filesystem RPC followed by clean worker replacement; `worker_stdin_epipe.test.ts` guards existing disconnect handling; `npm --prefix cli run build` passed. Required PR checks and CodeQL passed at exact head `8ea727e878efea7750e811c8836542299e704e30`; post-merge CI run `45760041918` and CodeQL run `45760041919` passed on release merge `1c48520411d3ddff2dbe8f2bb33cc922394e5e7d`. This closes the unowned in-flight worker portion of per-tool deadlines, but does not add configurable per-tool deadlines, guarantee cancellation of kernel-blocked I/O, or resolve arbitrary side-effect outcomes after process termination.\n69:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #877):** `collectOperationUsage` provides the shared read-only rollup of child-task token records for operation admission, goal accounting, operation status and budget views. It separates reported from estimated tokens and marks missing, malformed, and in-progress usage incomplete instead of presenting it as exact. Operation view schema v4 adds `tokenUsage`. PR #877 merged as `443f52b6871fedf4d65f0a99d10b5c41cdc91d7c`; post-merge CI run `45877783322` and CodeQL run `45877783393` passed on that commit. This rollup makes accounting and reporting consistent but is not a hard per-request token ceiling.\n71:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #881):** Before an operation can become terminal `COMPLETE`, `OperationRunner` rechecks the persisted token rollup when `maxTotalTokens` is configured. It pauses on a measured overrun or incomplete/unavailable usage, while allowing exact-cap completion when no further work needs dispatch; the completed unit remains available for operator review. The focused token-reporting, inference-budget, and goal-lifecycle tests passed 21/21. PR #881 merged as `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d`; post-merge CI run `45896185332` and CodeQL run `45896185330` passed. This prevents false terminal success after the last batch but does not stop a dispatched request or concurrent batch from exceeding the configured token cap.\n73:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #883):** Operation schema v10 persists cumulative request-token estimates. The existing async-local admission hook carries an estimate based on serialized input length plus the configured output allowance; operation scope reserves it with the inference submission count before dispatch. Concurrent calls cannot reserve the same remaining estimate, reservations persist across resume and are not refunded after cancellation or unknown outcomes, and reservation failure prevents dispatch. The final completion gate still checks persisted child usage. Generated ACP, run-result, and sidecar schemas/ledgers were updated. Focused reservation, migration, semantic-conflict tests passed 17/17, and protocol contract tests passed 30/30. PR #883 merged as `09f28d7e73633716859d1c1bb1edd30f26b5a7c6`; post-merge CI run `45908696882` and CodeQL run `45908696908` passed.\n75:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #885):** The request admission scope now narrows the provider output allowance to the remaining operation estimate and serializes the limit for OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses, Anthropic, Gemini, and Bedrock. If a provider rejects the required limit, or the active protocol cannot represent it, the request is not retried without the cap. The prompt-side token estimate remains heuristic, and Nexus cannot prove that each remote provider honors a serialized limit; this is not an exact or hard provider-spend ceiling. The focused provider/operation set passed 160/160, with build and lint passing. PR #885 merged as `d8d2fe2ab8698286660db8d9d78d4f2d5aedc74a`; post-merge CI run `45917052347` and CodeQL run `45917052388` passed.\n77:**Process-crash recovery evidence (2026-11-27, merged PR #887):** A separate Nexus process using a local fake gateway is killed after `run_command` has written a side-effect marker but before its result is saved. Resume reports the interrupted effect as unknown and refuses to replay it; the marker remains at one. The test passed on Node 22 and 24. PR #887 merged as `9bfe2ed86bfcf092e0406e71b83cb5b3e7e2ce62`; post-merge CI run `45927066566` and CodeQL run `45927066332` passed.\n79:**Follow-up process-crash sibling matrix (PR #894):** The real-process regression also covers an ordered two-call response: the first `run_command` completes and is persisted; a second writes an effect and remains in flight when Nexus is killed. Resume retains the first result, reports the second as unknown, and does not repeat either effect. The focused test passed 2/2. PR #894 merged as `5509e1f59ccced4f4e470cdd2ba5006bd73dcd77`; post-merge CI run `45947491306` and CodeQL run `45947491736` passed.\n81:**Provider-request crash accounting (PR #895):** With a local fake gateway holding a provider response after receipt, the test kills Nexus and resumes with a higher configured limit; the saved request count remains 1/1 and Nexus sends no second request. The focused test passed on Node 22 and 24. PR #895 merged as `91e9633cbaee9f6a9dca00cacf94f50e25c1b97c`; post-merge CI run `45951101344` and CodeQL run `45951101366` passed.\n83:**Provider-outcome recovery (PR #901):** Each provider request in objective and durable-operation scopes receives a persisted reservation before dispatch, then settles that specific reservation when Nexus observes a response. On resume, leftover in-flight requests are recorded as unknown before further work; legacy migrations do not invent prior outcomes. This replaces the earlier provider-crash test's weaker “budget exhausted, so no retry” evidence with an explicit unknown-outcome record. The request stays charged; this does not establish provider completion, billing, or exactly-once execution. Required checks passed at PR head `d0053ae4f7b78a3c23d26caf376665184f4020c9`; PR #901 merged as `af10e7b93c2bf2142cd738bda38aa575698c5813`, with post-merge CI run `46001827052` and CodeQL run `46001826978` passing on that commit.\n85:**Durable mutation-intent failure gate (PR #924, merged as `d4feb4d925d22f8d5517d306f5b13df8e8eec2a9`):** A fault-injected failure of `recordOperationStart` previously still allowed `write_file` to execute and create its target. Durable mutating tool calls now return a failed, not-executed receipt when the start record cannot be persisted (including when the durable state manager is unavailable); they do not capture a baseline or dispatch the handler, and they do not append an unmatched end record. If the current task record has not yet been materialized, the existing durable checkpoint path writes it before the operation start; a checkpoint failure also blocks dispatch. The `p10_operation_journal_fail_closed.test.ts` regression exercises a real fake-provider request and Rust file-write handler with start-journal persistence forced to fail. This closes the observed start-record gap for durable registered mutating tools. It does not cover transient non-durable subagent calls, prove host/power-loss behavior, or change the existing degraded-recovery treatment when an end-record write fails. Local verification included the focused regression, `npm run build`, `make lint`, and `git diff --check`. The first PR commit failed the hosted critical-complexity gate because `executeToolCall` increased from CC 43 to 51; helpers reduced it to CC 30. The first exact-head hosted run exposed test fixtures that replaced the constructor's durable store without materializing the task record; checkpoint-before-journal now handles those supported lazy-checkpoint entry paths. All exact-head required CI checks passed on `a06a00d01895b11aaec4de2227b8eff5e3586ec4` (CI run `46089209876`, CodeQL run `46089209866`); advisory Entire Gates failed and did not block the merge under repository policy. Post-merge CI run `46090864177` and CodeQL run `46090864175` passed on `d4feb4d925d22f8d5517d306f5b13df8e8eec2a9`.\n87:**Per-tool Rust RPC deadline slice (PR #922):** `NEXUS_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS_<TOOL>` sets a Rust RPC method's default timeout and ceiling; request-level values can shorten it, while `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS` remains the global hard cap. `run_command` receives the effective value in its runner request and keeps the longer bridge grace; a timed-out non-command RPC retires its shared worker and reports pending outcomes as unknown. Local `make build`, `make lint`, and `git diff --check` passed. On Node 22.22.2 and 24.11.1, `verifier_timeout.test.ts` passed 8/8, `rpc_worker_timeout.test.ts` 6/6, `process_bounds_and_services.test.ts` 3/3, and `tool_surface_characterization.test.ts` 6/6. PR #922 merged as `ed55744f8fda33dcc6410a664e9e50bd62d7d6f3`; required checks passed on the exact merge candidate `83a17fe8f2c3dce3e102b572c7ab8e18d144dce5`, and post-merge CI run `46078951080` plus CodeQL run `46078951108` passed on the release merge commit.\n91:**Plugin execution boundary (closed by PR #932):** The pre-fix findings above showed that asynchronous TypeScript plugin hooks could outlive their caller and that late middleware continuation could dispatch a tool after timeout. PR #932 (`3394b3a429d806256ab07936d62ed0586eaec907`, merged as `d0276535118aa197fc56371ab697220e20d5fd43`) moves file-loaded plugin callbacks into persistent, killable worker processes using versioned JSON IPC, a 1 MiB message cap, a 64 KiB combined stdout/stderr cap, and finite per-callback deadlines (default 15 seconds, maximum 60 seconds). Middleware continuation remains parent-owned; malformed or late messages fail closed; possibly-started custom tools and continuations report unknown outcomes; cancellation and shutdown retire workers. Workspace plugins run from a private temporary copy of the exact approved bytes. Local `make build`, `npm run build`, and `npm run typecheck` passed; the 82-test plugin/trust/policy compatibility set passed on Node 24.11.1, and focused containment tests passed 13/13 on both Node 22.22.2 and Node 24.11.1. Adversarial coverage includes synchronous infinite loops, never-settling callbacks, late continuation, timeout after continuation, cancellation, malformed/oversized IPC, and ordinary/detached child cleanup. Required PR checks passed at the exact head (Node 22/24 gates and matrices, all eight test shards, Linux packaging, and CodeQL); post-merge CI run `46107372969` and CodeQL run `46107372886` passed on merge commit `d0276535118aa197fc56371ab697220e20d5fd43`. This is execution containment, not an OS security sandbox or CPU/memory quota. Windows/macOS process-tree cleanup, host-crash cleanup, aggregate resource limits, and same-user deliberate protocol manipulation remain unproven.\n95:**Filesystem side-effect crash tranche (merged PR #937):** `cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` now kills a durable agent after `write_file` has returned but before its operation-end record can be persisted. Recovery identifies the operation as interrupted, presents its outcome as unknown, and does not replay the completed write. The focused file passed 3/3 on Node 24.11.1; TypeScript typecheck passed. The exact PR head `00dc078fdc16268247baec0a02801b318b63d099` passed required Node 22/24 gates and all eight shards, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL after a retry. The first attempt had one unrelated failure in `upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:813`; that test passed in a focused local rerun and the hosted shard retry passed. PR #937 merged as `419bca1a3f899d9b9d1a30b46c2093ceb2383492`; post-merge CI run `46126488514` and CodeQL run `46126488620` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check and did not block the merge under repository policy. This demonstrates one filesystem write/process-crash boundary only; it does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effect class. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n119:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #763):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. The PR's required checks passed at head `a18ec4c991fa583b52ba6ead441e9afe7d5df36c`; post-merge CI passed on `c2faaa89922a21e90bb1916c654015d417b9b582` (run `45307469727`).\n121:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #764):** `nexus audit verify --json` now fails closed when the flight log contains a durable `recording_gap` marker, including when the marker is the first record and the remaining log is unchained. The verifier reports `tampered` with `log_recording_gap_at_export`; clean bundles retain their prior result. The limit when disk failure prevents the marker from being persisted is documented. Required checks passed at head `5e5bb11f72630c16cad54b71456b512e9a20f370`; post-merge CI passed on `b74edef04083fcdcb2a53b842790792a174e3bcc` (run `45309777194`).\n123:**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, merged as `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required checks passed on PR merge candidate `117ea0a807c0070333d401da5f7994cb694cc705`; post-merge CI passed on `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`.\n125:**Stacked Git-configuration follow-up (PR #772, merged as `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84`):** Audit export lists repository-scoped Git settings that name executable programs or redirect Git behavior and marks receipt binding unavailable when any are present or the listing fails. Its five adversarial configurations are tested with a same-size tracked-file re-hash. The negative control without the preflight executes the planted clean filter and fails the marker assertion. Local verification passed on Node 24: `audit_export` 20/20, `audit_command` 8/8, `audit_bundle` 25/25, `audit_schema` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6, `candidate_git_paths` 36/36, and `tsc --noEmit`. Required PR checks passed on merge candidate `99a742ce529df0b79facb936002993e46e1d16f6`; post-merge CI passed on `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84` (run `45351066175`; CodeQL run `45351065784`). The non-required Entire check failed and did not gate merging under repository guidance.\n127:**Mandatory receipt-persistence failure slice (PR #858, merged as `33565128d7e2be14d7e80a09757144c3da28430a`):** If durable candidate-receipt persistence fails or the durable task state is unavailable, the in-memory receipt is invalidated, verified completion remains false, and the turn returns `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the speculative worktree is retained and cannot auto-merge. Failure injection verifies this path, while the successful receipt-binding regression still verifies normal acceptance and merge. Local focused tests passed (2/2), adjacent audit-export tests passed (21/21), and `npm run build` passed. Required checks passed on the exact PR merge candidate; post-merge CI run `45745010423` and CodeQL run `45745010340` passed on descendant release tip `1a5a05b204bba6cebe4ccbf2aaf94c571d474eae`, which includes the fix.\n129:**Acceptance identity slice (PR #863, merged):** Candidate validation receipts now include the source revision and candidate digest/id, verifier command and result, a digest of the pre-change verifier definition when available, Nexus/Node/OS/architecture identity, and a canonical digest of the effective policy and verifier configuration. Raw verifier contents and effective policy are not copied into the receipt. The receipt explicitly records `independentApproval: \"unavailable_single_maintainer\"`; it does not assert independent review. `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` checks the receipt fields, confirms the verifier source sentinel is absent, and retains the failure-closed persistence assertions. `audit_export.test.ts` checks that the existing state manager and audit bundle preserve the identity. Required PR checks passed on exact head `2d10d3780c0621d3cd5b9aecb811cbe30b4ea074`; post-merge CI run `45773723629` and CodeQL run `45773723883` passed on release commit `a421799bacaeb94d5dc64b5726dce18e6c1dd658`. WP-P10-03 still has same-user evidence mutability and no independent approval.\n131:**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\n133:**Receipt-construction fail-closed slice (PR #884, release; PR #886, main):** The first implementation's outer receipt-construction catch only cleared `verifiedWorktreeCompletion`; if candidate identity construction threw after a passing configured verifier, `task_completed` still returned success and the final turn was `COMPLETED/VERIFIED`. A failure-injection regression reproduced this at release base `abfa58c62c651ed4e113d0d9203667986739289d`. The catch now sets the existing acceptance failure latch, clears the active in-memory receipt, and invalidates any receipt for the candidate worktree. `run_turn.ts` consumes that latch as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; no change to the turn runner was needed. The merged regression asserts non-success, no active receipt, and no auto-merge while retaining the worktree. PR #884 merged as `4987ac573fe8415e3fe561a2adbb82d77014afde` on `release/v1.3.1`; all required exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI run `45911392549` and CodeQL run `45911392550` succeeded on that merge commit. PR #886 forward-ported the fix to `main` at `881798b282a0bc1198628955d5645ae27402b1b6`; all required exact-head checks passed (CI run `45920208046`, CodeQL run `45920208028`). I reran `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` and `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` together on Node 24.11.1 with the worktree-local Rust core built; all 3 tests passed. The earlier local attempts without that core were invalid because the verifier/tool runner never reached receipt creation. No independent approver is available; this local failure-injection test does not add external evidence immutability or independent review.\n135:**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing tests cover altered, deleted, reordered and truncated events and candidate mutation invalidation. Failure injection confirms an omitted event cannot be followed by an apparently intact chain, sanitizer failure does not preserve that claim, and mandatory receipt-persistence failure prevents verified acceptance. The release/v1.3.1 acceptance-identity slice adds source revision, candidate digest, verifier definition digest, command/result, runtime, and policy identity to durable receipts and verifies bundle retention. Legacy receipt export migration behavior is now tested: older receipts remain readable with their historical status, are not assigned synthesized acceptance identity, and are explicitly identified as missing structured identity. Exact-head CI and post-merge CI/CodeQL are complete for the legacy export follow-up. Same-user bundle mutability and the lack of independent approval remain explicit limitations; local evidence does not provide external immutability or a second-person review.\n159:**Progress (2026-11-28, merged PR #934):** The normal CLI and sidecar lifecycle reserve a named slot through the existing `SharedResourceAdmission` before using state. Admission is scoped per canonical home and defaults to 64 concurrent client processes; the launching environment may lower `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64 because admission runs before project `.env` loading. The kernel releases slots on process exit, and the existing exclusive restore lease remains unchanged. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced false capacity errors under zero-wait guard contention, then passed in three consecutive runs with the bounded 10-second guard wait; genuine slot exhaustion still fails closed. `npm run build` passed on Node 24.11.1. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices, all eight test shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host, not in-process sessions, aggregate CPU/memory, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n173:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #766):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails if a tracked function disappears or its cyclomatic complexity or control nesting increases, and reports line count without enforcing a global size cap. Extracted helpers require separate assessment. The focused tests passed 3/3; typecheck, Clippy, and fmt passed. PR #766's required Node 22/24, Linux, and test-shard checks passed at exact head `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631`; post-merge CI passed on `061843fc5fca4c874ac298093120b46073e50ab9` (`45319250946`).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":300643950}},"started_at_ms":1795858569005,"completed_at_ms":1795858570307}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T09:36:11.208Z","ordinal":319479,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a22183-1fc8-70e2-86ef-0068b504281a","call_id":"call_576759214bae4738a4e59fbbd015439a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7087)\nTotal output lines: 27\n\n51:**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This is not yet a ceiling on all model requests: context-findings extraction and LLM compaction summary/requirement-probe calls do not reserve from it, nor do delegated `spawn_subagent` requests or durable operation work units. Without durable objective state, the counter comes from `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` and resets per turn. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` may be selected in a project `.env` up to 10,000; on resume, an existing saved ceiling can only be lowered. Availability probes are excluded. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope: include all side and delegated requests in a shared durable pre-dispatch counter; account for durable operation units, tokens and cumulative elapsed limits; add per-tool deadlines and process-crash reconciliation.\n55:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #762):** `runTurnImpl` arms a timer for the active turn's `maxTurnMinutes` deadline and requests cancellation while inference or a tool is still awaiting completion. Expiry returns `LIMIT_REACHED` / `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; the timer is cleared on normal completion and caught failure. Tests cover aborting slow streamed inference, stopping a running shell command before its later side effect, and clearing the timer after a normal turn. Exact-head CI passed on PR #762 (`45293148069`); post-merge CI passed at `6b916195d57ddd4b641214ea3e835f10eb722a28` (`45294542653`). This bounded one active direct turn; PR #774 later added cumulative elapsed accounting across resumes of that durable objective. A separate per-tool deadline is still absent. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope includes shared durable accounting for side/delegated model requests and durable operation units, operation-wide elapsed limits, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation.\n59:**Progress (2026-11-25, implementation in progress):** The durable operation runner now has a fi…5887 tokens truncated… sidecar lifecycle reserve a named slot through the existing `SharedResourceAdmission` before using state. Admission is scoped per canonical home and defaults to 64 concurrent client processes; the launching environment may lower `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64 because admission runs before project `.env` loading. The kernel releases slots on process exit, and the existing exclusive restore lease remains unchanged. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced false capacity errors under zero-wait guard contention, then passed in three consecutive runs with the bounded 10-second guard wait; genuine slot exhaustion still fails closed. `npm run build` passed on Node 24.11.1. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices, all eight test shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host, not in-process sessions, aggregate CPU/memory, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n173:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #766):** Measured the critical-path baseline at release commit `4d9996d485c2db866918c110d35e1c1a1d3b2911` using Babel's TypeScript parser. `runTurnImpl` is 1,262 lines / CC 324 / nesting 5; `dispatchToolCallImpl` is 900 / CC 288 / nesting 6; `runSubagent` is 209 / CC 70 / nesting 4; `compactNowImpl` is 63 / CC 17 / nesting 3; `driveOperation` is 47 / CC 17 / nesting 3. `make lint` now compares those named functions to that exact Git baseline, fails if a tracked function disappears or its cyclomatic complexity or control nesting increases, and reports line count without enforcing a global size cap. Extracted helpers require separate assessment. The focused tests passed 3/3; typecheck, Clippy, and fmt passed. PR #766's required Node 22/24, Linux, and test-shard checks passed at exact head `23a563ff31383136d7ad3b93ec59410f39bac631`; post-merge CI passed on `061843fc5fca4c874ac298093120b46073e50ab9` (`45319250946`).\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795858571.2079992}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":140693,"sampled_through_sequence":140690,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
