{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:40.636Z","ordinal":320347,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0aaa07471c87d2ad773396f2458f12","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The post-merge CI and CodeQL runs passed on `d9fec18`, and the release branch points to that commit. The documentation and test worktrees are clean, and there’s no Claude process still running. I’m checking the current assurance plan for the next unfinished package before closing this progress report."}],"phase":"commentary"},"content_token_count":63,"started_at_ms":1795860999304,"completed_at_ms":1795861000636}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:40.640Z","ordinal":320348,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0aaa07471c87d2ad773396f2458f12","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The post-merge CI and CodeQL runs passed on `d9fec18`, and the release branch points to that commit. The documentation and test worktrees are clean, and there’s no Claude process still running. I’m checking the current assurance plan for the next unfinished package before closing this progress report.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795860999.2805932,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":141062,"sampled_through_sequence":141060,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0aaa07471c87d2ad773396f2458f12","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a221a8-31c0-7e70-81a7-e0f224d1a6fa","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":11166}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:42.791Z","ordinal":320349,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0aaa0897a087d290190a1adb4a846c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9da2e91c32884e8abb94c92ffdb1637e","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git fetch origin release/v1.3.1 && git show origin/release/v1.3.1:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md | sed -n '1,190p' | rg -n '^## WP|\\\\*\\\\*Priority|\\\\*\\\\*.*remains|\\\\*\\\\*WP-P10|Remaining scope|Next' \",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1800}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795861000.6071894}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":141063,"sampled_through_sequence":141060,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:42.879Z","ordinal":320350,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0aa9fe7bb887d2b340c732b53fd524","usage":{"input_tokens":142795,"cached_input_tokens":142336,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":632,"reasoning_output_tokens":431,"total_tokens":143427},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":52502119,"cached_input_tokens":51966848,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":66887,"reasoning_output_tokens":25853,"total_tokens":52569006},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6658573283,"cached_input_tokens":6583792640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15312734,"reasoning_output_tokens":9004406,"total_tokens":6673886017}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:45.812Z","ordinal":320351,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4d62f880-5b82-4a1c-a302-92a0ee1a0031","process_id":"91723","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git fetch origin release/v1.3.1 && git show origin/release/v1.3.1:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md | sed -n '1,190p' | rg -n '^## WP|\\*\\*Priority|\\*\\*.*remains|\\*\\*WP-P10|Remaining scope|Next' "],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git fetch origin release/v1.3.1 && git show origin/release/v1.3.1:docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md | sed -n '1,190p' | rg -n '^## WP|\\*\\*Priority|\\*\\*.*remains|\\*\\*WP-P10|Remaining scope|Next' "}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"From https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n * branch                release/v1.3.1 -> FETCH_HEAD\n   b764b7539..d9fec1838  release/v1.3.1 -> origin/release/v1.3.1\n9:## WP-P10-01 — Protect the independent acceptance authority\n11:**Priority:** Deferred (original risk is Critical) · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none.\n13:**Current operating constraint (2026-11-23):** This is a single-user FOSS repository; no second human reviewer is available, and the nominated account is suspended. The owner has decided not to seek paid infrastructure or another account, and has confirmed that the limitation must not block work or publication. Independent approval remains unavailable and must never be claimed. Do not add an approval or CODEOWNERS gate that prevents the sole maintainer from publishing. Keep the existing required CI checks and owner-controlled release authority. Reopen this package only if an independent maintainer becomes available or the owner changes this decision.\n27:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\n29:**Priority:** P0 · **Complexity:** L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-01 recommended first; can be implemented independently.\n51:**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This is not yet a ceiling on all model requests: context-findings extraction and LLM compaction summary/requirement-probe calls do not reserve from it, nor do delegated `spawn_subagent` requests or durable operation work units. Without durable objective state, the counter comes from `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` and resets per turn. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` may be selected in a project `.env` up to 10,000; on resume, an existing saved ceiling can only be lowered. Availability probes are excluded. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope: include all side and delegated requests in a shared durable pre-dispatch counter; account for durable operation units, tokens and cumulative elapsed limits; add per-tool deadlines and process-crash reconciliation.\n53:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #857):** Each `runTurn` installs an `AsyncLocalStorage` inference-admission scope. `client.ts` consults every active scope before each provider completion request, while the durable objective reserves and persists its counter before dispatch. Nested in-process turns inherit the enclosing scope, so provider retries/failovers, same-turn side requests, and nested delegates consume the same objective allowance; persistence failure prevents the provider call. `cli/test/p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts` covers finite limits and overrides, retry accounting and resume, side requests and nested delegates, persisted parent allowance, failed persistence, and legacy unknown history. Required CI run `45739706503` and CodeQL run `45739706508` passed on merge commit `d5e3f602c721fdaf213d1031d1616364c126bf43` (PR #857). This does not create a shared counter across distinct durable operation units; their request counts remain separate. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete** for operation-wide inference-request accounting and arbitrary side-effect recovery after process or host failure.\n55:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #762):** `runTurnImpl` arms a timer for the active turn's `maxTurnMinutes` deadline and requests cancellation while inference or a tool is still awaiting completion. Expiry returns `LIMIT_REACHED` / `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; the timer is cleared on normal completion and caught failure. Tests cover aborting slow streamed inference, stopping a running shell command before its later side effect, and clearing the timer after a normal turn. Exact-head CI passed on PR #762 (`45293148069`); post-merge CI passed at `6b916195d57ddd4b641214ea3e835f10eb722a28` (`45294542653`). This bounded one active direct turn; PR #774 later added cumulative elapsed accounting across resumes of that durable objective. A separate per-tool deadline is still absent. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope includes shared durable accounting for side/delegated model requests and durable operation units, operation-wide elapsed limits, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation.\n57:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #774):** The direct durable-objective elapsed-time ceiling is configurable with `--max-task-minutes` / `NEXUS_MAX_TASK_MINUTES` (default and hard maximum 4,320 minutes). Active intervals are checkpointed before inference or tools; resume charges an unclosed interval, cannot raise its saved ceiling, and legacy records conservatively estimate from `objective.startedAt` or fail closed when that timestamp is unavailable. A backward wall-clock change exhausts the remaining budget rather than restoring it. The additive elapsed fields are included in the `run --json` contract without changing its schema version. PR #774's required checks passed at head `02e1d7550ea48bb91cbf5ba0c67a69deb88d4baf`; it merged as `45520edcf33569802698f58c43277cad1e04a0a4`. Post-merge CI run `45374543474` and CodeQL run `45374543479` completed successfully on that merge commit, which is an ancestor of the current release baseline `257d324d61bbd1957a464f5ca6312d49d18e1c68`. This ceiling applies to one durable objective ledger; it does not cap aggregate elapsed work across all units in a durable operation. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete:** shared accounting for side/delegated requests, operation-wide elapsed limits, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash/unknown-outcome reconciliation remain.\n59:**Progress (2026-11-25, implementation in progress):** The durable operation runner now has a finite aggregate active wall-time cap (default and hard maximum 4,320 minutes) shared across concurrently executing units. Each active interval is recorded in the operation record; an open interval is charged on recovery, and migrated records conservatively use record age because earlier active time cannot be reconstructed. Expiry aborts the current operation signal, pauses the operation, and records interrupted side effects as unknown so resume cannot silently replay them. The existing `nexus operation budget` command now audits token and active-time cap changes together, and operation status/JSON reports elapsed, remaining, and uncertain legacy history. The implementation deliberately measures the operation driver's wall interval, not the sum of worker CPU time or time spent parked between runs. Focused evidence on the current branch: `p10_operation_active_budget.test.ts` (5/5), `goal_pa3_completion.test.ts` (8/8), `operation_runner_refactor.test.ts` (3/3), `operation_schema.test.ts` (19/19), `operation_view.test.ts` (35/35), and `npm run build` passed. This remains one tranche, not complete WP-P10-02: side/delegated inference requests, token accounting across all operation work, per-tool deadlines, process crash during arbitrary side effects, and durable unknown-outcome reconciliation beyond the in-flight budget-expiry boundary remain open. Exact-head hosted checks and post-merge CI have not yet run for this change.\n63:**Progress (2026-11-26, tool timeout hard bound):** `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS` is now parsed as a strict positive integer and capped at 86,400 seconds. This keeps the command runner's outer RPC timer within Node's supported timer range. Before the cap, `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS=2147484` produced a `2,147,489,000ms` bridge timer; a direct Node probe showed that an oversized timer fires after 1ms, which could prematurely retire the worker and return an unknown result. The regression test verifies oversized and malformed operator values and that the bridge timeout remains below `2,147,483,647ms`. This initially bounded the command timeout path; the non-command bridge input path is addressed by the follow-up below. WP-P10-02 remains incomplete for aggregate inference-request accounting across durable work units and arbitrary side-effect recovery.\n65:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, non-command RPC timeout input bound):** `rpcDeadlines` now accepts a non-command `timeout_secs` only when it is a positive safe integer, caps it using the existing `maxToolTimeoutSecs()` operator limit, and otherwise uses the finite 35-second RPC default. This also prevents untrusted bridge inputs from overflowing Node timers. The regression was reproduced before the fix: `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` yielded a `9,007,199,254,740,996,000ms` bridge delay. The test covers the hard cap, a lower operator override, negative/fractional/non-finite/unsafe inputs, and default fallback. Local evidence on Node 22.23.5 and 24.11.1: focused timeout, process-bound and RPC-worker suites passed 15/15 on each runtime; `make build`, `make lint`, and `git diff --check` passed. This closes timeout arithmetic for the covered bridge paths, but does not resolve aggregate inference-request accounting across durable work units or arbitrary side-effect recovery; WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.\n67:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #869):** Durable operation state now stores a finite `maxInferenceCalls` policy (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000), the consumed `inferenceCalls` count, and whether historical usage is known. Each provider submission made under an operation work-unit execution scope reserves and persists one count before dispatch; persistence failure prevents the request. Older records migrate with unknown history and pause before dispatch until the operator explicitly starts an accounting epoch. Reaching the cap pauses the operation, and changing the cap preserves the consumed count. The existing `nexus operation budget` command configures or explicitly resets this accounting and reports usage. The five tests in `p10_operation_inference_budget.test.ts` cover limits, cross-unit counting and exhaustion, cap changes and legacy reset, unknown legacy history, and failed reservation persistence. Local evidence: the CLI build passed and the focused operation origin, semantic conflict, and team convergence suites passed 62/62. Required Node 22/24 matrix, Linux, and CodeQL checks passed on the exact PR merge ref `ae1b0d560153985b2c94a9d095ce5ecbcab11d51`; PR #869 merged as `50207a6781ee1152950f0d42a3087aee034cc790`. Post-merge CI run `45807999265` and CodeQL run `45807999264` both passed on that release merge. This closes aggregate inference submission accounting across durable operation work units, but does not establish one counter across every possible provider call path or resolve arbitrary side-effect outcomes after process or host failure. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n71:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #881):** Before an operation can become terminal `COMPLETE`, `OperationRunner` rechecks the persisted token rollup when `maxTotalTokens` is configured. It pauses on a measured overrun or incomplete/unavailable usage, while allowing exact-cap completion when no further work needs dispatch; the completed unit remains available for operator review. The focused token-reporting, inference-budget, and goal-lifecycle tests passed 21/21. PR #881 merged as `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d`; post-merge CI run `45896185332` and CodeQL run `45896185330` passed. This prevents false terminal success after the last batch but does not stop a dispatched request or concurrent batch from exceeding the configured token cap.\n75:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #885):** The request admission scope now narrows the provider output allowance to the remaining operation estimate and serializes the limit for OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses, Anthropic, Gemini, and Bedrock. If a provider rejects the required limit, or the active protocol cannot represent it, the request is not retried without the cap. The prompt-side token estimate remains heuristic, and Nexus cannot prove that each remote provider honors a serialized limit; this is not an exact or hard provider-spend ceiling. The focused provider/operation set passed 160/160, with build and lint passing. PR #885 merged as `d8d2fe2ab8698286660db8d9d78d4f2d5aedc74a`; post-merge CI run `45917052347` and CodeQL run `45917052388` passed.\n77:**Process-crash recovery evidence (2026-11-27, merged PR #887):** A separate Nexus process using a local fake gateway is killed after `run_command` has written a side-effect marker but before its result is saved. Resume reports the interrupted effect as unknown and refuses to replay it; the marker remains at one. The test passed on Node 22 and 24. PR #887 merged as `9bfe2ed86bfcf092e0406e71b83cb5b3e7e2ce62`; post-merge CI run `45927066566` and CodeQL run `45927066332` passed.\n79:**Follow-up process-crash sibling matrix (PR #894):** The real-process regression also covers an ordered two-call response: the first `run_command` completes and is persisted; a second writes an effect and remains in flight when Nexus is killed. Resume retains the first result, reports the second as unknown, and does not repeat either effect. The focused test passed 2/2. PR #894 merged as `5509e1f59ccced4f4e470cdd2ba5006bd73dcd77`; post-merge CI run `45947491306` and CodeQL run `45947491736` passed.\n81:**Provider-request crash accounting (PR #895):** With a local fake gateway holding a provider response after receipt, the test kills Nexus and resumes with a higher configured limit; the saved request count remains 1/1 and Nexus sends no second request. The focused test passed on Node 22 and 24. PR #895 merged as `91e9633cbaee9f6a9dca00cacf94f50e25c1b97c`; post-merge CI run `45951101344` and CodeQL run `45951101366` passed.\n87:**Per-tool Rust RPC deadline slice (PR #922):** `NEXUS_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS_<TOOL>` sets a Rust RPC method's default timeout and ceiling; request-level values can shorten it, while `NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECS` remains the global hard cap. `run_command` receives the effective value in its runner request and keeps the longer bridge grace; a timed-out non-command RPC retires its shared worker and reports pending outcomes as unknown. Local `make build`, `make lint`, and `git diff --check` passed. On Node 22.22.2 and 24.11.1, `verifier_timeout.test.ts` passed 8/8, `rpc_worker_timeout.test.ts` 6/6, `process_bounds_and_services.test.ts` 3/3, and `tool_surface_characterization.test.ts` 6/6. PR #922 merged as `ed55744f8fda33dcc6410a664e9e50bd62d7d6f3`; required checks passed on the exact merge candidate `83a17fe8f2c3dce3e102b572c7ab8e18d144dce5`, and post-merge CI run `46078951080` plus CodeQL run `46078951108` passed on the release merge commit.\n91:**Plugin execution boundary (closed by PR #932):** The pre-fix findings above showed that asynchronous TypeScript plugin hooks could outlive their caller and that late middleware continuation could dispatch a tool after timeout. PR #932 (`3394b3a429d806256ab07936d62ed0586eaec907`, merged as `d0276535118aa197fc56371ab697220e20d5fd43`) moves file-loaded plugin callbacks into persistent, killable worker processes using versioned JSON IPC, a 1 MiB message cap, a 64 KiB combined stdout/stderr cap, and finite per-callback deadlines (default 15 seconds, maximum 60 seconds). Middleware continuation remains parent-owned; malformed or late messages fail closed; possibly-started custom tools and continuations report unknown outcomes; cancellation and shutdown retire workers. Workspace plugins run from a private temporary copy of the exact approved bytes. Local `make build`, `npm run build`, and `npm run typecheck` passed; the 82-test plugin/trust/policy compatibility set passed on Node 24.11.1, and focused containment tests passed 13/13 on both Node 22.22.2 and Node 24.11.1. Adversarial coverage includes synchronous infinite loops, never-settling callbacks, late continuation, timeout after continuation, cancellation, malformed/oversized IPC, and ordinary/detached child cleanup. Required PR checks passed at the exact head (Node 22/24 gates and matrices, all eight test shards, Linux packaging, and CodeQL); post-merge CI run `46107372969` and CodeQL run `46107372886` passed on merge commit `d0276535118aa197fc56371ab697220e20d5fd43`. This is execution containment, not an OS security sandbox or CPU/memory quota. Windows/macOS process-tree cleanup, host-crash cleanup, aggregate resource limits, and same-user deliberate protocol manipulation remain unproven.\n93:**WP-P10-02 status and remaining limits:** Merged changes provide operation-wide inference-submission reservations, estimated-token admission, provider-serialized output limits, a terminal measured-usage gate, persisted unknown provider outcomes after process interruption, process-crash evidence for selected command/provider paths, and bounded plugin callback execution from PR #932. PR #922 adds per-tool deadline defaults/caps for Rust RPC calls. Local provider inference requests also have a finite whole-request client deadline, with focused Node 24 tests passing 46/46 as recorded above; remote provider processing/billing after local abort remains unknown. These controls do not demonstrate exact token usage or provider spend: input-token admission is heuristic and remote providers may ignore a serialized output cap. Plugin process containment does not impose aggregate CPU/memory quotas or establish host-crash cleanup; crash tests do not establish host/power-loss safety or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effectful tool/provider path. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete** for exact/provider-enforced cumulative token containment and recovery qualification for other side-effect classes and host/power failure.\n95:**Filesystem side-effect crash tranche (merged PR #937):** `cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` now kills a durable agent after `write_file` has returned but before its operation-end record can be persisted. Recovery identifies the operation as interrupted, presents its outcome as unknown, and does not replay the completed write. The focused file passed 3/3 on Node 24.11.1; TypeScript typecheck passed. The exact PR head `00dc078fdc16268247baec0a02801b318b63d099` passed required Node 22/24 gates and all eight shards, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL after a retry. The first attempt had one unrelated failure in `upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:813`; that test passed in a focused local rerun and the hosted shard retry passed. PR #937 merged as `419bca1a3f899d9b9d1a30b46c2093ceb2383492`; post-merge CI run `46126488514` and CodeQL run `46126488620` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check and did not block the merge under repository policy. This demonstrates one filesystem write/process-crash boundary only; it does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effect class. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n97:**Filesystem side-effect crash follow-up (merged PR #939):** The same real-process recovery harness now covers the Rust `edit_file` path as well as `write_file`. It kills the durable agent after the file mutation returns but before the operation-end journal record is saved, then confirms recovery records an interrupted/unknown outcome and does not replay the mutation. The focused suite passed 4/4 on Node 24.11.1; `npm run typecheck` and `git diff --check` passed. Required PR checks and CodeQL passed on refreshed merge commit `a2b01991881538ee9775be7c76e8a94b39b096f6` (base `e44edcedd3aa711a0d05c058351c8f86946507ba`, PR head `a76b414c120e3342ff638a0b4f8cf8cd707fad55`); all eight Node 22/24 shards, both matrices, Linux, and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check. PR #939 merged as `b764b753926759650f971ba41823b9e631305db2`; post-merge CI run `46130593983` and CodeQL run `46130593979` passed on that exact commit. This expands process-crash evidence to two filesystem mutation tools; it still does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior, exactly-once execution, or unknown-outcome recovery for other side-effect classes. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n99:## WP-P10-03 — Acceptance evidence integrity and export\n101:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M · **Dependencies:** none for local evidence integrity; independent policy identity remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n121:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #763):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. The PR's required checks passed at head `a18ec4c991fa583b52ba6ead441e9afe7d5df36c`; post-merge CI passed on `c2faaa89922a21e90bb1916c654015d417b9b582` (run `45307469727`).\n129:**Mandatory receipt-persistence failure slice (PR #858, merged as `33565128d7e2be14d7e80a09757144c3da28430a`):** If durable candidate-receipt persistence fails or the durable task state is unavailable, the in-memory receipt is invalidated, verified completion remains false, and the turn returns `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the speculative worktree is retained and cannot auto-merge. Failure injection verifies this path, while the successful receipt-binding regression still verifies normal acceptance and merge. Local focused tests passed (2/2), adjacent audit-export tests passed (21/21), and `npm run build` passed. Required checks passed on the exact PR merge candidate; post-merge CI run `45745010423` and CodeQL run `45745010340` passed on descendant release tip `1a5a05b204bba6cebe4ccbf2aaf94c571d474eae`, which includes the fix.\n133:**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\n141:## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n143:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02 for shared task budgets; existing operation-local scheduling is already implemented.\n155:**Migration / rollback:** Start with advisory resource estimates, then enforce with operator-visible defaults; do not kill unrelated sessions. Rollback disables only the new admission layer while retaining process cleanup. Residual risk: OS estimates are approximate; host OOM remains an external failure mode without cgroups/container limits.\n157:**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #889):** A shared, cross-process active-operation cap now reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version processes using the same admission store. It does not bound aggregate CPU/memory, session count, disk use, provider spend, or processes that do not participate in this lease protocol; older running Nexus versions do not hold the new lease until they exit. Cancellation and crash reconciliation outside the existing lease boundary still need separate evidence.\n159:**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #919):** Session history archive writes enforce an aggregate cap equal to the existing 2 GiB retained-state ceiling. `SessionManager.assertSessionArchiveCapacity` scans archive files under the existing state-store guard, rejects unreadable/non-regular entries and scans above 100,000 entries, and refuses a write before archive append or fork creation if it would cross the cap. It preserves existing archives and does not add another cleanup or admission framework. The new `session_archive_bounds.test.ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n161:**Progress (2026-11-28, merged PR #934):** The normal CLI and sidecar lifecycle reserve a named slot through the existing `SharedResourceAdmission` before using state. Admission is scoped per canonical home and defaults to 64 concurrent client processes; the launching environment may lower `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64 because admission runs before project `.env` loading. The kernel releases slots on process exit, and the existing exclusive restore lease remains unchanged. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced false capacity errors under zero-wait guard contention, then passed in three consecutive runs with the bounded 10-second guard wait; genuine slot exhaustion still fails closed. `npm run build` passed on Node 24.11.1. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices, all eight test shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host, not in-process sessions, aggregate CPU/memory, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n163:## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n165:**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n167:**Gap/evidence:** Strict TS build, CodeQL JS/TS, Clippy, and diff-scoped rustfmt are present in CI. No Rust CodeQL or targeted complexity gate was found. `runTurnImpl` remains a critical large function.\n173:**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75,196-197`). Workflow run `45047617708` completed successfully on that exact main SHA, including all three static-gate steps. Do not add a duplicate Clippy job. Remaining work in this package is a narrowly scoped, evidence-based complexity metric and its enforcement policy; the independent protection dependency from WP-P10-01 remains unavailable in this single-user repository.\n177:**Required tests / acceptance:** The focused tests prove that decision-count and nesting growth are rejected and that the tracked release-baseline functions pass. `make lint` runs in the required Node 22/24 and Linux CI gates. The gate also fails closed if a tracked function or baseline source cannot be resolved. The verification workflow remains changeable by the sole maintainer under the current single-user policy; independent protection is unavailable and must not be implied.\n183:1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n184:2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n185:3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\n186:4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n187:5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":2,"nanos":718768208}},"started_at_ms":1795861003091,"completed_at_ms":1795861005811}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:16:46.412Z","ordinal":320352,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a221a8-484c-77d3-aea0-a7ed756bd1ed","call_id":"call_9da2e91c32884e8abb94c92ffdb1637e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7800)\nTotal output lines: 47\n\nFrom https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code\n * branch                release/v1.3.1 -> FETCH_HEAD\n   b764b7539..d9fec1838  release/v1.3.1 -> origin/release/v1.3.1\n9:## WP-P10-01 — Protect the independent acceptance authority\n11:**Priority:** Deferred (original risk is Critical) · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none.\n13:**Current operating constraint (2026-11-23):** This is a single-user FOSS repository; no second human reviewer is available, and the nominated account is suspended. The owner has decided not to seek paid infrastructure or another account, and has confirmed that the limitation must not block work or publication. Independent approval remains unavailable and must never be claimed. Do not add an approval or CODEOWNERS gate that prevents the sole maintainer from publishing. Keep the existing required CI checks and owner-controlled release authority. Reopen this package only if an independent maintainer becomes available or the owner changes this decision.\n27:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\n29:**Priority:** P0 · **Complexity:** L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-01 recommended first; can be implemented independently.\n51:**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This is not yet a ceiling on all model requests: context-findings extraction and LLM compaction summary/requirement-probe calls do not reserve from it, nor do delegated `spawn_subagent` requests or durable operation work units. Without durable objective state, the counter comes from `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` and resets per turn. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` may be selected in a project `.env` up to 10,000; on resume, an existing saved ceiling can only be lowered. Availability probes are excluded. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope: include all side and delegated requests in a shared durable pre-dispatch counter; account for durable operation units, tokens and cumulative elapsed limits; add per-tool deadlines and process-crash reconciliation.\n53:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #857):** Each `runTurn` installs an `AsyncLocalStorage` inference-admission scope. `client.ts` consults every active scope before each provider completion request, while the durable objective reserves and persists its counter before dispatch. Nested in-process turns inherit the enclosing scope, so provider retries/failovers, same-turn side requests, and nested delegates consume the same objective allowance; persistence failure prevents the provider call. `cli/test/p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts` covers finite limits and overrides, retry accounting and resume, side requests and nested delegates, persisted parent allowance, failed persistence, and legacy unknown history. Required CI run `45739706503` and CodeQL run `45739706508` passed on merge commit `d5e3f602c721fdaf213d1031d1616364c126bf43` (PR #857). This does not create a shared counter across distinct durable operation units; their request counts remain separate. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete** for operation-wide inference-request accounting and arbitrary side-effect recovery after process or host failure.…6000 tokens truncated…s scoped per canonical home and defaults to 64 concurrent client processes; the launching environment may lower `NEXUS_MAX_ACTIVE_CLIENTS` from 1 to 64 because admission runs before project `.env` loading. The kernel releases slots on process exit, and the existing exclusive restore lease remains unchanged. A 16-process same-home regression reproduced false capacity errors under zero-wait guard contention, then passed in three consecutive runs with the bounded 10-second guard wait; genuine slot exhaustion still fails closed. `npm run build` passed on Node 24.11.1. Required exact-head checks passed at PR head `4f55c6d4bfd4a58f480816b5871d5b97c36a0221`: both Node test matrices, all eight test shards, Linux build, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL. PR #934 merged at `2026-11-28T07:16:02Z` as `9b415dfdf8b754dd67a6cbb7b0a5084a1bfe9395`; post-merge CI run `46120407959` and CodeQL run `46120408066` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head, but is advisory and not a required merge check. This bounds cooperating Nexus CLI processes per canonical home on one Linux host, not in-process sessions, aggregate CPU/memory, separate homes, or non-Nexus processes. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the other aggregate resource, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\n163:## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\n165:**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n167:**Gap/evidence:** Strict TS build, CodeQL JS/TS, Clippy, and diff-scoped rustfmt are present in CI. No Rust CodeQL or targeted complexity gate was found. `runTurnImpl` remains a critical large function.\n173:**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75,196-197`). Workflow run `45047617708` completed successfully on that exact main SHA, including all three static-gate steps. Do not add a duplicate Clippy job. Remaining work in this package is a narrowly scoped, evidence-based complexity metric and its enforcement policy; the independent protection dependency from WP-P10-01 remains unavailable in this single-user repository.\n177:**Required tests / acceptance:** The focused tests prove that decision-count and nesting growth are rejected and that the tracked release-baseline functions pass. `make lint` runs in the required Node 22/24 and Linux CI gates. The gate also fails closed if a tracked function or baseline source cannot be resolved. The verification workflow remains changeable by the sole maintainer under the current single-user policy; independent protection is unavailable and must not be implied.\n183:1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\n184:2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n185:3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\n186:4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\n187:5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795861006.4127336}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":141064,"sampled_through_sequence":141060,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
