{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:32:07.629Z","ordinal":320884,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_033f353a673dbf89016b0aad9ed90c87d284eee74e66c3e3af","status":"completed","call_id":"call_40a4bb82861b4e79a3d8cb13d49e515d","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/p10-02-delete-file-pr-body.md <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n- Extend the durable process-crash harness to cover the Rust delete_file path after the file is removed but before operation-end persistence.\\n- Assert recovery reports the interrupted effect as unknown, preserves the absent-file state, and produces exactly one tool result rather than automatically dispatching again.\\n- Raise the shared harness polling window from 10 to 20 seconds after local Node 22 runs exceeded the previous bound under host load.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- Node 22.22.2: `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` passed 5/5.\\n- Node 24.11.1: `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` passed 5/5.\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` passed; `git diff --check` passed.\\n- The first local Node 22 attempt had four polling timeouts at the old 10-second limit; after increasing the wait to 20 seconds, the full file passed. No product behavior failure was observed.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\nXERJ lookup found existing durable crash coverage in `cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts:1012` and a child-process recovery test description in `cli/test/suspend_resume_acceptance.test.ts:4`; the definition lookup located `core/src/file_ops.rs:917`. There was no direct delete_file crash test or relevant peer-project pattern, so this reuses Nexus's existing real-process fixture and tests the Rust handler; no peer code was copied.\\n\\n## Scope limits\\nThis demonstrates one local process-crash boundary for delete_file. It does not establish host/power-loss recovery, exactly-once execution, or recovery behavior for every side-effect class. P10-02 remains incomplete.\\nEOF\\ngh pr create --base release/v1.3.1 --head codex/p10-02-delete-file-crash-recovery --title \\\"test: cover delete-file crash recovery\\\" --body-file /tmp/p10-02-delete-file-pr-body.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-delete-file-crash-recovery\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:900}); text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795861918.8517122}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":141314,"sampled_through_sequence":141312,"client_authored":false}}
