{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T10:57:26.826Z","ordinal":321425,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a2bfe89d-5d74-4ca3-959d-85a169478588","process_id":"94334","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'Filesystem side-effect crash' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md && sed -n '92,100p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-delete-file-evidence","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Filesystem side-effect crash' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","query":"Filesystem side-effect crash","path":"POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '92,100p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","name":"POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","path":"docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"95:**Filesystem side-effect crash tranche (merged PR #937):** `cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` now kills a durable agent after `write_file` has returned but before its operation-end record can be persisted. Recovery identifies the operation as interrupted, presents its outcome as unknown, and does not replay the completed write. The focused file passed 3/3 on Node 24.11.1; TypeScript typecheck passed. The exact PR head `00dc078fdc16268247baec0a02801b318b63d099` passed required Node 22/24 gates and all eight shards, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL after a retry. The first attempt had one unrelated failure in `upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:813`; that test passed in a focused local rerun and the hosted shard retry passed. PR #937 merged as `419bca1a3f899d9b9d1a30b46c2093ceb2383492`; post-merge CI run `46126488514` and CodeQL run `46126488620` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check and did not block the merge under repository policy. This demonstrates one filesystem write/process-crash boundary only; it does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effect class. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n97:**Filesystem side-effect crash follow-up (merged PR #939):** The same real-process recovery harness now covers the Rust `edit_file` path as well as `write_file`. It kills the durable agent after the file mutation returns but before the operation-end journal record is saved, then confirms recovery records an interrupted/unknown outcome and does not replay the mutation. The focused suite passed 4/4 on Node 24.11.1; `npm run typecheck` and `git diff --check` passed. Required PR checks and CodeQL passed on refreshed merge commit `a2b01991881538ee9775be7c76e8a94b39b096f6` (base `e44edcedd3aa711a0d05c058351c8f86946507ba`, PR head `a76b414c120e3342ff638a0b4f8cf8cd707fad55`); all eight Node 22/24 shards, both matrices, Linux, and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check. PR #939 merged as `b764b753926759650f971ba41823b9e631305db2`; post-merge CI run `46130593983` and CodeQL run `46130593979` passed on that exact commit. This expands process-crash evidence to two filesystem mutation tools; it still does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior, exactly-once execution, or unknown-outcome recovery for other side-effect classes. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n\n**WP-P10-02 status and remaining limits:** Merged changes provide operation-wide inference-submission reservations, estimated-token admission, provider-serialized output limits, a terminal measured-usage gate, persisted unknown provider outcomes after process interruption, process-crash evidence for selected command/provider paths, and bounded plugin callback execution from PR #932. PR #922 adds per-tool deadline defaults/caps for Rust RPC calls. Local provider inference requests also have a finite whole-request client deadline, with focused Node 24 tests passing 46/46 as recorded above; remote provider processing/billing after local abort remains unknown. These controls do not demonstrate exact token usage or provider spend: input-token admission is heuristic and remote providers may ignore a serialized output cap. Plugin process containment does not impose aggregate CPU/memory quotas or establish host-crash cleanup; crash tests do not establish host/power-loss safety or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effectful tool/provider path. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete** for exact/provider-enforced cumulative token containment and recovery qualification for other side-effect classes and host/power failure.\n\n**Filesystem side-effect crash tranche (merged PR #937):** `cli/test/p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` now kills a durable agent after `write_file` has returned but before its operation-end record can be persisted. Recovery identifies the operation as interrupted, presents its outcome as unknown, and does not replay the completed write. The focused file passed 3/3 on Node 24.11.1; TypeScript typecheck passed. The exact PR head `00dc078fdc16268247baec0a02801b318b63d099` passed required Node 22/24 gates and all eight shards, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL after a retry. The first attempt had one unrelated failure in `upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts:813`; that test passed in a focused local rerun and the hosted shard retry passed. PR #937 merged as `419bca1a3f899d9b9d1a30b46c2093ceb2383492`; post-merge CI run `46126488514` and CodeQL run `46126488620` passed on that exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check and did not block the merge under repository policy. This demonstrates one filesystem write/process-crash boundary only; it does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior or unknown-outcome recovery for every side-effect class. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n\n**Filesystem side-effect crash follow-up (merged PR #939):** The same real-process recovery harness now covers the Rust `edit_file` path as well as `write_file`. It kills the durable agent after the file mutation returns but before the operation-end journal record is saved, then confirms recovery records an interrupted/unknown outcome and does not replay the mutation. The focused suite passed 4/4 on Node 24.11.1; `npm run typecheck` and `git diff --check` passed. Required PR checks and CodeQL passed on refreshed merge commit `a2b01991881538ee9775be7c76e8a94b39b096f6` (base `e44edcedd3aa711a0d05c058351c8f86946507ba`, PR head `a76b414c120e3342ff638a0b4f8cf8cd707fad55`); all eight Node 22/24 shards, both matrices, Linux, and JavaScript/TypeScript passed. Entire Gates failed as an advisory check. PR #939 merged as `b764b753926759650f971ba41823b9e631305db2`; post-merge CI run `46130593983` and CodeQL run `46130593979` passed on that exact commit. This expands process-crash evidence to two filesystem mutation tools; it still does not demonstrate host/power-loss behavior, exactly-once execution, or unknown-outcome recovery for other side-effect classes. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete.**\n\n## WP-P10-03 — Acceptance evidence integrity and export\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":987277585}},"started_at_ms":1795863445838,"completed_at_ms":1795863446826}}
