{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:54:41.738Z","ordinal":322523,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a22201-eec9-7d80-93cf-fa2277c794ca","call_id":"call_37e7e5f26c114ee1bb0a5f1a8c83bf44","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"531c33\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.269456355,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":56,\"output\":\"[{\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"codex/p10-02-delete-file-evidence\\\",\\\"number\\\":942,\\\"title\\\":\\\"docs: record delete-file crash recovery evidence\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-11-28T10:58:25Z\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/942\\\"}]\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"451b5f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000035231,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7793,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7793)\\nTotal output lines: 42\\n\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:15:3. Execution records are not authoritative tamper-evident evidence. The flight recorder sanitizes and appends locally, but catches append failures and has no integrity chain or signature (`cli/src/flight.ts:77-108`). GitHub currently requires three status checks but zero approving reviews; an accepted change can alter its own workflow or verification configuration without a repository-enforced independent approval (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`; live ruleset 25340146 queried 2026-11-18).\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:50:| Tool execution | `cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`, `cli/src/core/spine.ts`, `cli/src/tools.ts`, `core/src/runner.rs`. | Capability/policy dispatch produces receipts; Rust owns child process groups and cancellation; ordinary host commands remain powerful unless sandboxed/approved. Tool timeouts are explicit and capped by configured maximum. |\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_GAP_ANALYSIS.md:79:| 10. Warnings and analysis | Strict compiler/type checks and static analyzers in CI, with protected mandatory job definitions and controlled suppressions. | M3 | Strict TS build and CI, CodeQL TS/JS and dependency checks exist. `cargo clippy -D warnings` passed in this audit but is absent from CI. Branch status checks do not require approval and are non-strict. |\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:3:**Planning baseline (reconciled 2026-11-25):** `release/v1.3.0` `257d324d61bbd1957a464f5ca6312d49d18e1c68`. The owner approved this implementation plan on 2026-11-23. No dates are assigned.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:9:## WP-P10-01 — Protect the independent acceptance authority\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:19:**Design / reuse:** Do not build a policy service or configure a second-approval/CODEOWNERS requirement while this is a single-user repository. Preserve mandatory status checks and exact-head evidence. If an independent maintainer later becomes available, revisit GitHub's existing ruleset and CODEOWNERS for acceptance-critical paths.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:23:**Required tests / acceptance:** Record the configured ruleset and required status checks at the exact revision; report independent approval as unavailable. This package is not a prerequisite for implementation, PR publication, or release work under the current owner decision.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:27:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:29:**Priority:** P0 · **Complexity:** L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-01 recommended first; can be implemented independently.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:51:**Progress (2026-11-23, merged PR #760):** The primary turn's provider-recovery loop reserves each request, including retries, against a persisted objective ceiling (default 1,000; hard maximum 10,000). Persistence failure prevents dispatch; resume can lower but not raise the saved ceiling; legacy records expose earlier inference history as unknown. The feature test and all required exact-head checks passed at merge commit `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3`; post-merge CI passed on that merge commit. This is not yet a ceiling on all model requests: context-findings extraction and LLM compaction summary/requirement-probe calls do not reserve from it, nor do delegated `spawn_subagent` requests or durable operation work units. Without durable objective state, the counter comes from `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` and resets per turn. `NEXUS_MAX_INFERENCE_SUBMISSIONS` may be selected in a project `.env` up to 10,000; on resume, an existing saved ceiling can only be lowered. Availability probes are excluded. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope: include all side and delegated requests in a shared durable pre-dispatch counter; account for durable operation units, tokens and cumulative elapsed limits; add per-tool deadlines and process-crash reconciliation.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:53:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-26, merged PR #857):** Each `runTurn` installs an `AsyncLocalStorage` inference-admission scope. `client.ts` consults every active scope before each provider completion request, while the durable objective reserves and persists its counter before dispatch. Nested in-process turns inherit the enclosing scope, so provider retries/failovers, same-turn side requests, and nested delegates consume the same objective allowance; persistence failure prevents the provider call. `cli/test/p10_inference_submission_budget.test.ts` covers finite limits and overrides, retry accounting and resume, side requests and nested delegates, persisted parent allowance, failed persistence, and legacy unknown history. Required CI run `45739706503` and CodeQL run `45739706508` passed on merge commit `d5e3f602c721fdaf213d1031d1616364c126bf43` (PR #857). This does not create a shared counter across distinct durable operation units; their request counts remain separate. **WP-P10-02 remains incomplete** for operation-wide inference-request accounting and arbitrary side-effect recovery after process or host failure.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:55:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #762):** `runTurnImpl` arms a timer for the active turn's `maxTurnMinutes` deadline and requests cancellation while inference or a tool is still awaiting completion. Expiry returns `LIMIT_REACHED` / `TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED`; the timer is cleared on normal completion and caught failure. Tests cover aborting slow streamed inference, stopping a running shell command before its later side effect, and clearing the timer after a normal turn. Exact-head CI passed on PR #762 (`45293148069`); post-merge CI passed at `6b916195d57ddd4b641214ea3e835f10eb722a28` (`45294542653`). This bounded one active direct turn; PR #774 later added cumulative elapsed accounting across resumes of that durable objective. A separate per-tool deadline is still absent. **P10-02 remains incomplete.** Remaining scope includes shared durable accounting for side/delegated model requests and durable operation units, operation-wide elapsed limits, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:57:**Progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #774):** The direct durable-objective elapsed-time ceiling is configurable with `--max-task-minutes` / `NEXUS_MAX_TASK_MINUTES` (default and hard maximum 4,320 minutes). Active intervals are checkpointed before inference or tools; resume charges an unclosed interval, cannot raise its saved ceiling, and legacy records conservatively estimate from `objective.startedAt` or fail closed when that timestamp is unavailable. A backward wall-clock change exhausts the remaining budget rather than restoring it. The additive elapsed fields are included in the `run --json` contract without changing its schema version.…4293 tokens truncated…hat per-operation scheduling is unbounded, and no OS-level host CPU/memory ceiling is claimed.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:143:**Follow-up evidence (2026-11-26, current release):** Cross-operation inference-resource slots and same-home LSP slots have since been implemented in `SharedResourceAdmission` (PRs #830 and #831; see `docs/assurance/WP-P10-04_RESOURCE_ADMISSION_BASELINE.md`). A separate process-boundary probe on release commit `5061a3e83ce6daf34f34785bd3753f11604ba77d` confirms that `UsageLedger` provider request/token/cost caps remain process-local: two fresh Node 24.11.1 processes sharing one temporary `HOME` and workspace each admitted under `NEXUS_CLOUD_MAX_REQUESTS=1`, then wrote two receipts to the shared workspace file. No live inference was run. This is a confirmed gap only if these limits are expected to aggregate across processes; their reset/window semantics are not defined, so do not turn them into persistent global quotas without an explicit accounting epoch. Durable operation inference counters are the existing operation-scoped control and must not be duplicated here.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:153:**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #889):** A shared, cross-process active-operation cap now reuses `SharedResourceAdmission.acquireNamed`; it does not add a parallel admission framework. `NEXUS_MAX_SHARED_OPERATION_UNITS` defaults to 4 and accepts operator values from 1 through 64. The aggregate lease is acquired before the provider lease, released if provider admission misses, and held through executor completion and result persistence. Focused tests passed 33/33 and the TypeScript build passed on Node 24.11.1. Required PR checks passed at head `f552c2c885b7fe9d00b9acd1677435f084d20be6` and merge candidate `f07cf89d0e44885dbb24beef6721ac7540212ea5`. Post-merge CI run `45932311657` and CodeQL run `45932311572` passed on merge `0390df6b5ff619201600360ff016364ca0bc6af6`; Entire remained advisory. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open:** this control limits active operation units across cooperating current-version processes using the same admission store. It does not bound aggregate CPU/memory, session count, disk use, provider spend, or processes that do not participate in this lease protocol; older running Nexus versions do not hold the new lease until they exit. Cancellation and crash reconciliation outside the existing lease boundary still need separate evidence.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:155:**Progress (2026-11-27, merged PR #919):** Session history archive writes enforce an aggregate cap equal to the existing 2 GiB retained-state ceiling. `SessionManager.assertSessionArchiveCapacity` scans archive files under the existing state-store guard, rejects unreadable/non-regular entries and scans above 100,000 entries, and refuses a write before archive append or fork creation if it would cross the cap. It preserves existing archives and does not add another cleanup or admission framework. The new `session_archive_bounds.test.ts` covers aggregate accounting across sessions, byte preservation on refusal, fork refusal before state creation, inability to raise the ceiling through options, and empty append behavior at a full quota. With the worktree-local Rust core built, `session_archive_bounds.test.ts`, `session_fork.test.ts`, and `compaction_continuity.test.ts` passed **43/43** on Node 24.11.1 (exit 0); process-death recovery cases and the existing archive-write failure case were included. After the final empty-append guard, the current archive and fork suites passed **10/10**, `npm --prefix cli run build` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. PR #919 merged at `2026-11-27T20:00:55Z` as `a944a4eac448fdd1b08f1adfdca5be5696376ad2`. Required PR-head CI run `46059219684` and CodeQL run `46059219707` passed at exact PR head `d1778581428312574f24057e5b2741e6d3aae802`. Post-merge CI run `46060674463` passed both Node test gates, all eight shards, Linux packaging, and diff coverage; CodeQL run `46060674335` also passed on the exact merge commit. Entire Gates failed on the PR head but is advisory and excluded from required merge gates by project policy. Scope is limited to `*.history.jsonl` archives written by participating current-version Nexus processes; this is not a general disk quota and does not cap other state, external writers, or older running versions. **WP-P10-04 remains partially open** for the broader CPU/memory, session-count, provider-accounting, and cleanup/recovery gaps above.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:157:## WP-P10-05 — Compiler/static-analysis gate and hotspot metrics\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:159:**Priority:** P2 · **Complexity:** S/M · **Dependencies:** none; independent protection of CI remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:167:**Progress (2026-11-23, `main` at `9156571f7d5fd8f8436c3105f0237628ab35e857`):** The Clippy CI gate proposed above is already implemented through `make lint` (`Makefile:24-27`), which runs CLI typecheck, Clippy with `-D warnings`, and diff-scoped rustfmt. CI calls this target in `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:74-75,196-197`). Workflow run `45047617708` completed successfully on that exact main SHA, including all three static-gate steps. Do not add a duplicate Clippy job. Remaining work in this package is a narrowly scoped, evidence-based complexity metric and its enforcement policy; the independent protection dependency from WP-P10-01 remains unavailable in this single-user repository.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:173:**Migration / rollback:** If historical warnings appear on a new toolchain, baseline them narrowly with tracked expiry/owner; do not suppress globally. The sole maintainer may direct rollback of this specific gate; any rollback must be visible in the PR and must not be described as independently approved. Residual risk: static analysis cannot establish requirements correctness or provider behavior.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:177:1. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:178:2. **WP-P10-03** durable evidence and candidate/policy binding (P1; implement local integrity controls and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:179:3. **WP-P10-04** aggregate resource admission and cleanup (P1; budget counters feed this work).\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:180:4. **WP-P10-05** static-analysis/complexity gate (P2; reuse existing CI gates and state the single-maintainer trust limit).\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:181:5. **WP-P10-01** remains deferred until a second independent maintainer is available; it is not a prerequisite for the work above or publication.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"26dfca\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.493513382,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":164,\"output\":\"[{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-11-28T10:58:20Z\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":46137637907,\\\"displayTitle\\\":\\\"docs: record delete-file crash recovery evidence\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pull_request\\\",\\\"headSha\\\":\\\"6e73e1ecf957af00ef1a58fea902ab27d128a425\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/46137637907\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"cancelled\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-11-28T10:58:20Z\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":46137637984,\\\"displayTitle\\\":\\\"docs: record delete-file crash recovery evidence\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pull_request\\\",\\\"headSha\\\":\\\"6e73e1ecf957af00ef1a58fea902ab27d128a425\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/46137637984\\\"}]\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795866881.737818}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":142008,"sampled_through_sequence":142005,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
