{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:55:03.439Z","ordinal":322549,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","session_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","root_turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","response_id":"resp_033f353a673dbf89016b0ac1107f3487d2a61f7ff0568b1876","usage":{"input_tokens":65410,"cached_input_tokens":62464,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":346,"reasoning_output_tokens":235,"total_tokens":65756},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":123596501,"cached_input_tokens":122688640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":120332,"reasoning_output_tokens":47328,"total_tokens":123716833},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6729667665,"cached_input_tokens":6654514432,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15366179,"reasoning_output_tokens":9025881,"total_tokens":6745033844}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:55:03.574Z","ordinal":322550,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-96aa99fe-5e43-4481-9d45-bb108fdb1baa","process_id":"4355","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '95,137p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md | rg -n '^\\*\\*|^\\* |^##|remains|Remaining|Regression|process-crash|PR #9[0-9]+'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '95,137p' docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","name":"POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","path":"docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^'\"\\\\*\\\\*|\"'^'\"\\\\* |\"'^##|remains|Remaining|Regression|process-crash|PR #9[0-9]+'","query":"^\\*\\*|^\\* |^##|remains|Remaining|Regression|process-crash|PR #9[0-9]+","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:## WP-P10-03 — Acceptance evidence integrity and export\n3:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M · **Dependencies:** none for local evidence integrity; independent policy identity remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n5:**Existing capability:** `FlightRecorder` hash-chains persisted events and `FlightPlayer` reports altered, reordered, removed or unchained records (`cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`). GV-2 already exports bounded audit bundles with per-file SHA-256, a canonical manifest, hash-linked file entries, offline verification, and optional operator-key Ed25519 signatures (`cli/src/core/audit_bundle.ts`, `cli/src/audit_contract.ts`). `CandidateTracker` invalidates receipts on known mutations and recomputes the candidate identity before merge (`cli/src/core/candidate.ts`). These controls must be reused; this package does not need a second chain or evidence store.\n7:**Confirmed gap:** Before this slice, `FlightRecorder.appendEvent` silently returned an apparent event after a write or redaction failure while leaving later writes on the same chain (`cli/src/flight.ts`). A later complete chain could therefore omit a middle event without the on-disk chain indicating missing evidence. Flight logs are optional telemetry and must not block authorized work, but they must not continue to attest to an intact chain after a skipped event. The completion receipt also does not yet carry a complete, durable environment and acceptance-policy identity; distinguish that remaining work from the existing candidate binding and audit-bundle integrity.\n9:**Affected surfaces:** `flight.ts`, `evidence.ts`, completion oracle, durable state and audit commands.\n11:**Design / reuse:** Keep the GV-3 flight chain and GV-2 audit bundle. On any event omission, stop chaining subsequent events so the existing verifier reports a broken or unchained log; return an explicit `recordingSkipped` result without blocking the authorized action. For later work, extend the existing receipt/bundle only for missing candidate, verifier, environment and policy identity. Use operator-supplied signing only when explicitly configured; unsigned bundles remain clearly unsigned. Do not promote optional flight telemetry into a mandatory acceptance store.\n13:**Implementation steps:**\n21:**Progress (2026-11-23):** The flight recorder now returns `recordingSkipped` and disables further chaining after sanitization or append failure. A failure-injection test reproduces an `EISDIR` append failure and confirms the next persisted event makes the flight read as `CHAIN BROKEN`; a separate test covers sanitizer failure. This intentionally does not block tool execution.\n23:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #763):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. The PR's required checks passed at head `a18ec4c991fa583b52ba6ead441e9afe7d5df36c`; post-merge CI passed on `c2faaa89922a21e90bb1916c654015d417b9b582` (run `45307469727`).\n25:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #764):** `nexus audit verify --json` now fails closed when the flight log contains a durable `recording_gap` marker, including when the marker is the first record and the remaining log is unchained. The verifier reports `tampered` with `log_recording_gap_at_export`; clean bundles retain their prior result. The limit when disk failure prevents the marker from being persisted is documented. Required checks passed at head `5e5bb11f72630c16cad54b71456b512e9a20f370`; post-merge CI passed on `b74edef04083fcdcb2a53b842790792a174e3bcc` (run `45309777194`).\n27:**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, merged as `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required checks passed on PR merge candidate `117ea0a807c0070333d401da5f7994cb694cc705`; post-merge CI passed on `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`.\n29:**Stacked Git-configuration follow-up (PR #772, merged as `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84`):** Audit export lists repository-scoped Git settings that name executable programs or redirect Git behavior and marks receipt binding unavailable when any are present or the listing fails. Its five adversarial configurations are tested with a same-size tracked-file re-hash. The negative control without the preflight executes the planted clean filter and fails the marker assertion. Local verification passed on Node 24: `audit_export` 20/20, `audit_command` 8/8, `audit_bundle` 25/25, `audit_schema` 7/7, `leak_guard` 6/6, `candidate_git_paths` 36/36, and `tsc --noEmit`. Required PR checks passed on merge candidate `99a742ce529df0b79facb936002993e46e1d16f6`; post-merge CI passed on `fb396a42ac311670e52dd4bf3153b2e464ac3a84` (run `45351066175`; CodeQL run `45351065784`). The non-required Entire check failed and did not gate merging under repository guidance.\n31:**Mandatory receipt-persistence failure slice (PR #858, merged as `33565128d7e2be14d7e80a09757144c3da28430a`):** If durable candidate-receipt persistence fails or the durable task state is unavailable, the in-memory receipt is invalidated, verified completion remains false, and the turn returns `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the speculative worktree is retained and cannot auto-merge. Failure injection verifies this path, while the successful receipt-binding regression still verifies normal acceptance and merge. Local focused tests passed (2/2), adjacent audit-export tests passed (21/21), and `npm run build` passed. Required checks passed on the exact PR merge candidate; post-merge CI run `45745010423` and CodeQL run `45745010340` passed on descendant release tip `1a5a05b204bba6cebe4ccbf2aaf94c571d474eae`, which includes the fix.\n33:**Acceptance identity slice (PR #863, merged):** Candidate validation receipts now include the source revision and candidate digest/id, verifier command and result, a digest of the pre-change verifier definition when available, Nexus/Node/OS/architecture identity, and a canonical digest of the effective policy and verifier configuration. Raw verifier contents and effective policy are not copied into the receipt. The receipt explicitly records `independentApproval: \"unavailable_single_maintainer\"`; it does not assert independent review. `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` checks the receipt fields, confirms the verifier source sentinel is absent, and retains the failure-closed persistence assertions. `audit_export.test.ts` checks that the existing state manager and audit bundle preserve the identity. Required PR checks passed on exact head `2d10d3780c0621d3cd5b9aecb811cbe30b4ea074`; post-merge CI run `45773723629` and CodeQL run `45773723883` passed on release commit `a421799bacaeb94d5dc64b5726dce18e6c1dd658`. WP-P10-03 still has same-user evidence mutability and no independent approval.\n35:**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\n37:**Receipt-construction fail-closed slice (PR #884, release; PR #886, main):** The first implementation's outer receipt-construction catch only cleared `verifiedWorktreeCompletion`; if candidate identity construction threw after a passing configured verifier, `task_completed` still returned success and the final turn was `COMPLETED/VERIFIED`. A failure-injection regression reproduced this at release base `abfa58c62c651ed4e113d0d9203667986739289d`. The catch now sets the existing acceptance failure latch, clears the active in-memory receipt, and invalidates any receipt for the candidate worktree. `run_turn.ts` consumes that latch as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; no change to the turn runner was needed. The merged regression asserts non-success, no active receipt, and no auto-merge while retaining the worktree. PR #884 merged as `4987ac573fe8415e3fe561a2adbb82d77014afde` on `release/v1.3.1`; all required exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI run `45911392549` and CodeQL run `45911392550` succeeded on that merge commit. PR #886 forward-ported the fix to `main` at `881798b282a0bc1198628955d5645ae27402b1b6`; all required exact-head checks passed (CI run `45920208046`, CodeQL run `45920208028`). I reran `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` and `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` together on Node 24.11.1 with the worktree-local Rust core built; all 3 tests passed. The earlier local attempts without that core were invalid because the verifier/tool runner never reached receipt creation. No independent approver is available; this local failure-injection test does not add external evidence immutability or independent review.\n39:**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing tests cover altered, deleted, reordered and truncated events and candidate mutation invalidation. Failure injection confirms an omitted event cannot be followed by an apparently intact chain, sanitizer failure does not preserve that claim, and mandatory receipt-persistence failure prevents verified acceptance. The release/v1.3.1 acceptance-identity slice adds source revision, candidate digest, verifier definition digest, command/result, runtime, and policy identity to durable receipts and verifies bundle retention. Legacy receipt export migration behavior is now tested: older receipts remain readable with their historical status, are not assigned synthesized acceptance identity, and are explicitly identified as missing structured identity. Exact-head CI and post-merge CI/CodeQL are complete for the legacy export follow-up. Same-user bundle mutability and the lack of independent approval remain explicit limitations; local evidence does not provide external immutability or a second-person review.\n41:**Migration / rollback:** Legacy logs remain readable but classify `integrity=unverified_legacy`; never silently “upgrade” them to verified. Keep old export path read-only during migration. Residual risk: same-user can delete both evidence and local chain unless an external signed/immutable copy is retained.\n43:## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39337}},"started_at_ms":1795866903574,"completed_at_ms":1795866903574}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:55:03.673Z","ordinal":322551,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a22202-4478-7133-8017-365f1eb9ca64","call_id":"call_8407f45afc89407d9d098cecbded3ff4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3152)\nTotal output lines: 19\n\n1:## WP-P10-03 — Acceptance evidence integrity and export\n3:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M · **Dependencies:** none for local evidence integrity; independent policy identity remains unavailable under WP-P10-01.\n5:**Existing capability:** `FlightRecorder` hash-chains persisted events and `FlightPlayer` reports altered, reordered, removed or unchained records (`cli/src/core/hash_chain.ts`, `cli/src/flight.ts`). GV-2 already exports bounded audit bundles with per-file SHA-256, a canonical manifest, hash-linked file entries, offline verification, and optional operator-key Ed25519 signatures (`cli/src/core/audit_bundle.ts`, `cli/src/audit_contract.ts`). `CandidateTracker` invalidates receipts on known mutations and recomputes the candidate identity before merge (`cli/src/core/candidate.ts`). These controls must be reused; this package does not need a second chain or evidence store.\n7:**Confirmed gap:** Before this slice, `FlightRecorder.appendEvent` silently returned an apparent event after a write or redaction failure while leaving later writes on the same chain (`cli/src/flight.ts`). A later complete chain could therefore omit a middle event without the on-disk chain indicating missing evidence. Flight logs are optional telemetry and must not block authorized work, but they must not continue to attest to an intact chain after a skipped event. The completion receipt also does not yet carry a complete, durable environment and acceptance-policy identity; distinguish that remaining work from the existing candidate binding and audit-bundle integrity.\n9:**Affected surfaces:** `flight.ts`, `evidence.ts`, completion oracle, durable state and audit commands.\n11:**Design / reuse:** Keep the GV-3 flight chain and GV-2 audit bundle. On any event omission, stop chaining subsequent events so the existing verifier reports a broken or unchained log; return an explicit `recordingSkipped` result without blocking the authorized action. For later work, extend the existing receipt/bundle only for missing candidate, verifier, environment and policy identity. Use operator-supplied signing only when explicitly configured; unsigned bundles remain clearly unsigned. Do not promote optional flight telemetry into a mandatory acceptance store.\n13:**Implementation steps:**\n21:**Progress (2026-11-23):** The flight recorder now returns `recordingSkipped` and disables further chaining after sanitization or append failure. A failure-injection test reproduces an `EISDIR` append failure and confirms the next persisted event makes the flight read as `CHAIN BROKEN`; a separate test covers sanitizer failure. This intentionally does not block tool execution.\n23:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #763):** Sanitization and append failures now attempt to persist a payload-free, unchained `recording_gap` marker, retain degraded status across recorder restart, and emit one operator warning per recorder. If the filesystem also rejects the marker write, only the runtime warning survives; persistence cannot be guaranteed when the evidence sink is unavailable. `nexus replay` reports skipped evidence explicitly, including when the first record was skipped. Audit verification returns a finding and nonzero result when a bundled log was already broken at export; an unchained legacy log remains a stated limitation. The PR's required checks passed at head `a18ec4c991fa583b52ba6ead441e9afe7d5df36c`; post-merge CI passed on `c2faaa89922a21e90bb1916c654015d417b9b582` (run `45307469727`).\n25:**Follow-up progress (2026-11-24, merged PR #764):** `nexus audit verify --json` now fails closed when the flight log contains a durable `recording_gap` marker, including when the marker is the first record and the remaining log is unchained. The verifier reports `tampered` with `log_recording_gap_at_export`; clean bundles retain their prior result. The limit when disk failure prevents the marker from being persisted is documented. Required checks passed at head `5e5bb11f72630c16cad54b71456b512e9a20f370`; post-merge CI passed on `b74edef04083fcdcb2a53b842790792a174e3bcc` (run `45309777194`).\n27:**Candidate-binding slice (PR #771, merged as `3b15d89fd421b23e1161cae577f6e7c373236312`):** `nexus audit export` adds a bounded `receipts/candidate-binding.json` report, reusing the existing candidate identity routine and the bundle's existing `validation_receipts` artefact role. It records match, mismatch, partial, no-receipt, or unavailable outcomes; the human-readable export prints the status, and it never upgrades a verifier result or acceptance decision. The candidate scan is capped at 50,000 entries and 256 MiB; binding output is capped at 10,000 receipts and explicitly describes its non-atomic sampling relationship to bundle collection. Platforms where the existing safe candidate traversal cannot run report unavailable. The added `git ls-files` invocation disables `core.fsmonitor`, preventing a repository-configured monitor from running if local Git configuration changes after the audit-export preflight. Local verification passed: `audit_export.test.ts` 19/19, `candidate_git_paths.test.ts` 36/36, and the TypeScript build. Required checks passed on PR merge cand…552 tokens truncated…al digest of the effective policy and verifier configuration. Raw verifier contents and effective policy are not copied into the receipt. The receipt explicitly records `independentApproval: \"unavailable_single_maintainer\"`; it does not assert independent review. `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` checks the receipt fields, confirms the verifier source sentinel is absent, and retains the failure-closed persistence assertions. `audit_export.test.ts` checks that the existing state manager and audit bundle preserve the identity. Required PR checks passed on exact head `2d10d3780c0621d3cd5b9aecb811cbe30b4ea074`; post-merge CI run `45773723629` and CodeQL run `45773723883` passed on release commit `a421799bacaeb94d5dc64b5726dce18e6c1dd658`. WP-P10-03 still has same-user evidence mutability and no independent approval.\n35:**Legacy receipt export follow-up (PR #867, merged as `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`):** The existing `receipts/candidate-binding.json` now records per sampled receipt whether a structured acceptance identity object was saved, plus the count of sampled legacy receipts without one. Export warnings and human-readable output call out that absence. This is a presence report only: it does not validate the identity object's claims, alter the historical receipt status, or indicate verifier success or acceptance. The regression `legacy validation receipts remain readable and are explicitly reported without structured acceptance identity` verifies an old `PASSED` receipt is exported without synthesizing identity and the task store remains byte-for-byte unchanged. On Node 24, the full `audit_export.test.ts` file passed 22/22 with `TMPDIR=/var/tmp` to avoid the host's unrelated `/tmp/.git` marker; `npm --prefix cli run build` and `git diff --check` passed. Required exact-head checks passed on `396c4a5e3be7174453f5c3e9e4ba43d714a37b85` (CI run `45785980552`, CodeQL run `45785980671`); post-merge CI run `45788238436` and CodeQL run `45788238467` passed on merge commit `f5e88e4f39ef5bfed8b674738575a9522b37f3ec`. Local bundles and their source stores remain mutable by the same user.\n37:**Receipt-construction fail-closed slice (PR #884, release; PR #886, main):** The first implementation's outer receipt-construction catch only cleared `verifiedWorktreeCompletion`; if candidate identity construction threw after a passing configured verifier, `task_completed` still returned success and the final turn was `COMPLETED/VERIFIED`. A failure-injection regression reproduced this at release base `abfa58c62c651ed4e113d0d9203667986739289d`. The catch now sets the existing acceptance failure latch, clears the active in-memory receipt, and invalidates any receipt for the candidate worktree. `run_turn.ts` consumes that latch as `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; no change to the turn runner was needed. The merged regression asserts non-success, no active receipt, and no auto-merge while retaining the worktree. PR #884 merged as `4987ac573fe8415e3fe561a2adbb82d77014afde` on `release/v1.3.1`; all required exact-head checks passed, and post-merge CI run `45911392549` and CodeQL run `45911392550` succeeded on that merge commit. PR #886 forward-ported the fix to `main` at `881798b282a0bc1198628955d5645ae27402b1b6`; all required exact-head checks passed (CI run `45920208046`, CodeQL run `45920208028`). I reran `p10_receipt_persistence.test.ts` and `p10_process_crash_recovery.test.ts` together on Node 24.11.1 with the worktree-local Rust core built; all 3 tests passed. The earlier local attempts without that core were invalid because the verifier/tool runner never reached receipt creation. No independent approver is available; this local failure-injection test does not add external evidence immutability or independent review.\n39:**Required tests / acceptance:** Existing tests cover altered, deleted, reordered and truncated events and candidate mutation invalidation. Failure injection confirms an omitted event cannot be followed by an apparently intact chain, sanitizer failure does not preserve that claim, and mandatory receipt-persistence failure prevents verified acceptance. The release/v1.3.1 acceptance-identity slice adds source revision, candidate digest, verifier definition digest, command/result, runtime, and policy identity to durable receipts and verifies bundle retention. Legacy receipt export migration behavior is now tested: older receipts remain readable with their historical status, are not assigned synthesized acceptance identity, and are explicitly identified as missing structured identity. Exact-head CI and post-merge CI/CodeQL are complete for the legacy export follow-up. Same-user bundle mutability and the lack of independent approval remain explicit limitations; local evidence does not provide external immutability or a second-person review.\n41:**Migration / rollback:** Legacy logs remain readable but classify `integrity=unverified_legacy`; never silently “upgrade” them to verified. Keep old export path read-only during migration. Residual risk: same-user can delete both evidence and local chain unless an external signed/immutable copy is retained.\n43:## WP-P10-04 — Resource admission and cleanup envelope\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795866903.6729925}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":142020,"sampled_through_sequence":142017,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
