{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:55:10.818Z","ordinal":322553,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f090-96c7-7f02-ae7d-1a090d633b76","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0ac118673c87d28cd787b74e84093e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Still outstanding**\n\n- **PR #942:** The documentation update for the delete-file crash-recovery work is open. CodeQL passed, but the CI run was cancelled after one shard stalled, so the required checks are unresolved. It should not be merged until a fresh run passes.\n- **WP-P10-02, execution bounds and recovery:** Much has landed, including durable budgets, deadlines, and crash-recovery checks for selected operations. The plan still identifies gaps in exact provider-enforced token/spend limits and recovery evidence for other side effects and host or power failures.\n- **WP-P10-03, acceptance evidence:** Receipt and audit protections are in place, but evidence remains mutable by the same user, and no independent approval is available. The single-maintainer decision means that limitation should remain explicit; it must not block publication.\n- **WP-P10-04, resource limits and cleanup:** Admission controls and a session archive cap are implemented. Broader CPU/memory, session-count and disk limits, plus cleanup and recovery outside existing lease boundaries, remain open.\n- **WP-P10-05, static analysis:** Existing build, lint, and CI checks are working. The plan still calls for the critical-function complexity gate; its status needs a current exact-head check before calling this package complete.\n- **WP-P10-01:** Independent review remains unavailable and deferred by your decision. It is not a prerequisite for continuing or publishing work.\n\nThe context-maturity paperwork is complete. I found no other open pull requests; the only one currently open is #942. The main checkout is clean on `release/v1.3.1`."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"content_token_count":333,"started_at_ms":1795866904419,"completed_at_ms":1795866910818}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-28T11:55:10.874Z","ordinal":322554,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0ac118673c87d28cd787b74e84093e","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**Still outstanding**\n\n- **PR #942:** The documentation update for the delete-file crash-recovery work is open. CodeQL passed, but the CI run was cancelled after one shard stalled, so the required checks are unresolved. It should not be merged until a fresh run passes.\n- **WP-P10-02, execution bounds and recovery:** Much has landed, including durable budgets, deadlines, and crash-recovery checks for selected operations. The plan still identifies gaps in exact provider-enforced token/spend limits and recovery evidence for other side effects and host or power failures.\n- **WP-P10-03, acceptance evidence:** Receipt and audit protections are in place, but evidence remains mutable by the same user, and no independent approval is available. The single-maintainer decision means that limitation should remain explicit; it must not block publication.\n- **WP-P10-04, resource limits and cleanup:** Admission controls and a session archive cap are implemented. Broader CPU/memory, session-count and disk limits, plus cleanup and recovery outside existing lease boundaries, remain open.\n- **WP-P10-05, static analysis:** Existing build, lint, and CI checks are working. The plan still calls for the critical-function complexity gate; its status needs a current exact-head check before calling this package complete.\n- **WP-P10-01:** Independent review remains unavailable and deferred by your decision. It is not a prerequisite for continuing or publishing work.\n\nThe context-maturity paperwork is complete. I found no other open pull requests; the only one currently open is #942. The main checkout is clean on `release/v1.3.1`.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","create_time":1795866904.4070153,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":142021,"sampled_through_sequence":142020,"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_033f353a673dbf89016b0ac118673c87d28cd787b74e84093e","turn_id":"01a22143-fcf9-7462-927e-e66d27ee2285","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a22202-6099-7d01-9227-0697f4576300","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":11290}}
