w v1.0.104\\n\\u001b[1m\\u001b[92m    Checking\\u001b[0m anstyle-query v1.1.5\\n\\u001b[1m\\u001b[92m    Checking\\u001b[0m bstr v1.13.1\\n\\u001b[1m\\u001b[92m    Checking\\u001b[0m lru v0.18.5\\n\\u001b[1m\\u001b[92m    Checking\\u001b[0m line-clipping v0.3.8\\n\\u001b[1m\\u001b[92m    Checking\\u001b[0m clap_lex v1.1.1\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"ce7f55\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000032569,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":931,\"output\":\"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\\n\\nCreate a fork of a repository.\\n\\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\\nthe specified repository.\\n\\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\\n\\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\\n\\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\\n\\n\\nUSAGE\\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\\n\\nFLAGS\\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \\\"origin\\\")\\n\\nINHERITED FLAGS\\n  --help   Show help for command\\n\\nEXAMPLES\\n  # Fork a repository\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\\n  \\n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\\n  \\n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\\n\\nLEARN MORE\\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\\n\\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\\nNothing was branched.\\n\\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\\ncd xerj\\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\\nxerj feedback \\\\\\n --agent \\\"Codex\\\" \\\\\\n  --used-for \\\"reviewing Nexus durable operation journal failure handling\\\" --pointed-at \\\"439143 records across 148 dataset(s)\\\" \\\\\\n  --verdict \\\"Definition search located the durable operation-end writer and lexical test search found adjacent crash-recovery cases, but no targeted end-record failure regression; used only for navigation and validated behavior against current source and executable tests.\\\" --numbers \\\"not measured\\\" \\\\\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-28-reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure.md\\ngit checkout -b field-report/reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure\\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-28-reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure.md\\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-28-reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure.md -m \\\"docs(field-report): reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure\\\"\\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure\\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure \\\\\\n  --title \\\"Agent field report: reviewing Nexus durable operation journal failure handling\\\" \\\\\\n  --body \\\"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-11-28-reviewing-nexus-durable-operation-journal-failure.md.\\\"\\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\\n{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"stored\\\":true,\\\"note\\\":\\\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\\\"}\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a22202-664d-7671-a9c4-ed550c36ebc8","create_time":1795867686.310476}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":142317,"sampled_through_sequence":142314,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
